            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "When AI answers describe your brand inaccurately or omit key services, use AEO software to document those cases, identify which content the engines are pulling from, and prioritize new or revised pages that clearly correct the narrative. You may need to front-load concise, factual statements that answer engines can easily quote.\n\nYou can’t directly “edit” AI answers, but you can influence the sources they rely on.\n\nKey factors:\n- Where AI seems to be sourcing outdated or incorrect information\n- Gaps in your current content that allow misinterpretation\n- Opportunities to add authoritative, up-to-date explainer pages\n- Cadence for monitoring whether answers improve over time\n\nCreate a remediation backlog in your AEO tool: list bad answers, map them to content changes, and re-check after publishing and indexing. Repeat until AI responses align better with your intended positioning.\n\nUse AEO insights as an early-warning system for brand narrative issues in AI ecosystems.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "AEO software can surface incorrect AI answers about your brand, show what content they likely rely on, and help you plan new or updated pages that correct the narrative. You then monitor whether AI responses change as those authoritative, well-structured explanations are crawled and incorporated."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "AEO software can surface incorrect AI answers about your brand, show what content they likely rely on, and help you plan new or updated pages that correct the n"
      }
    },
