          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What should I do if I can’t afford full AEO software right now but still want better visibility in AI answers?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If you’re on a tight budget, focus on low- or no-cost AEO tactics and lightweight tools: structured data plugins, FAQ builders, and basic monitoring from Search Console and analytics. Many AEO principles can be applied manually before you invest in a full platform.\n\nThe goal is to get your most important pages into an answer-friendly format: clear questions, short direct answers, and valid schema. Software mainly makes this scalable and easier to track.\n\nKey factors:\n- Use free or freemium schema generators and validators\n- Turn existing content into FAQ and how‑to sections\n- Track question queries and snippets in Search Console\n- Prioritize a small set of high-value queries\n\nStart with your top 5–10 money pages and add structured FAQs that match real customer questions, then monitor snippet gains over 1–2 months. Once you prove value, you’ll have a stronger case to upgrade to dedicated AEO software.\n\nThink of budget-friendly AEO as a staged approach: manual foundations first, then software to scale what’s already working.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "With a limited budget, focus on manual AEO basics: add FAQ and how‑to sections to key pages, implement free structured data (FAQPage, HowTo), and track question queries in Search Console. Prove results on 5–10 core pages, then consider upgrading to dedicated AEO software to scale."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "With a limited budget, focus on manual AEO basics: add FAQ and how‑to sections to key pages, implement free structured data (FAQPage, HowTo), and track question"
      }
