          {
            "name": "My business is in Austin/Denver and I already get good SEO traffic—when does adding AEO software make sense?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If your analytics show strong traffic but AI tools rarely mention you, AEO software helps identify which content isn’t answer-friendly and what changes might earn citations. It’s particularly valuable in markets like Austin and Denver where tech-savvy users rely heavily on AI for recommendations.\n\nYou’ll want to connect your analytics and Search Console, then map which queries drive traffic vs which AI questions you’re missing entirely.\n\nKey factors:\n- High organic traffic but low AI/voice answer presence\n- Competitive markets where users ask “best” and “vs” questions\n- Existing content that lacks clear Q&A or structured data\n- Appetite for testing new content formats (FAQs, how‑tos, comparisons)\n\nIn Austin or Denver, start by tracking how AI tools answer key “best X” and “X vs Y” queries in your niche; then use AEO software to guide content and schema updates aimed at those questions. Re-check AI responses monthly to gauge progress.\n\nFor tech-forward cities, being cited in AI answers can become as important as ranking on page one of Google.",
