        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How do I measure whether my AEO software is actually working and not just adding another dashboard?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "To judge AEO software performance, track both visibility metrics (snippets, AI citations, impressions) and downstream outcomes like branded searches, assisted conversions, and lead quality. Rankings alone won’t capture answer-engine impact.\n\nYou should establish a baseline before making changes, then compare 60‑ to 90‑day windows so you’re measuring trends, not day‑to‑day noise.\n\nKey factors:\n- Number and quality of featured snippets and rich results\n- Frequency and sentiment of AI-generated brand mentions\n- Changes in branded search volume and direct visits\n- Conversion and lead metrics for pages targeted by AEO\n\nUse the software’s dashboards plus your analytics to build a simple KPI set, then review it monthly with both marketing and sales. Tie improvements in answer visibility to actual business outcomes whenever possible.\n\nGood AEO tools make these relationships easier to see, but you still need internal clarity on what “success” means for your organization.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Measure AEO software effectiveness by tracking snippet and AI citation gains, branded search and direct traffic lifts, and conversions from pages you’ve optimized. Set a pre‑AEO baseline, then compare 60–90‑day windows to see whether answer visibility translates into actual business outcomes."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Measure AEO software effectiveness by tracking snippet and AI citation gains, branded search and direct traffic lifts, and conversions from pages you’ve optimiz"
      }
