            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "When choosing AEO software, focus on how well it supports your specific content types (FAQs, how‑tos, product pages) and the answer engines that matter most for your audience. Flashy features matter less than reliable tracking and clear, actionable recommendations.\n\nYou should also consider how easily it fits into your current SEO and content workflows so your team actually uses it.\n\nKey factors:\n- Coverage of Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity, Bing\n- Support for FAQPage, HowTo, Product, and LocalBusiness schema\n- Integrations with your CMS, analytics, and project tools\n- Quality of reporting and guidance (not just raw data)\n\nShortlist 2–3 tools, run a 30‑day trial on specific questions, and compare not only the data but how intuitive each platform feels to your team. Involve both SEO and content stakeholders in that evaluation.\n\nPick the tool that makes it easiest to turn insights into concrete changes, not just the one with the longest feature list.",
