          {
            "name": "I’ve been burned by SEO tools before—how do I avoid wasting money on AEO software too?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If previous SEO tools or agencies burned you, treat AEO software as a testable experiment with modest scope and clear success criteria, not a big, vague promise. Start small, demand transparency, and avoid long contracts until you see real impact.\n\nYou’ll want to own your data, understand exactly what changes are recommended, and verify whether they match known best practices rather than opaque “magic”.\n\nKey factors:\n- Short, cancellable trials instead of long-term lock‑ins\n- Clear documentation of each recommendation and rationale\n- Access to exports so you’re never stuck inside one platform\n- Vendor willingness to set realistic expectations and timelines\n\nFrame your first AEO project around a small set of high-value queries and analyze before‑and‑after metrics yourself. If the tool and support team are candid about limits and tradeoffs, that’s a good trust signal.\n\nUse AEO as a way to regain control over search visibility, not to outsource strategy entirely again.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Avoid repeating past SEO mistakes by treating AEO software as a small, time‑boxed experiment with clear success metrics, not a big promise. Choose tools with short trials, transparent recommendations, data exports, and realistic timelines, then verify before‑and‑after results yourself."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Avoid repeating past SEO mistakes by treating AEO software as a small, time‑boxed experiment with clear success metrics, not a big promise. Choose tools with sh"
      }
    },
