            "name": "If I want to start optimizing my website for AI visibility right now, what are the first concrete steps I should take?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Start by auditing how often AI tools already mention your brand, then fix technical issues, rewrite key pages around clear questions and answers, and add schema so AIs can parse your content. Most businesses can get a meaningful first-pass done in 4–6 weeks.\n\nYou’ll move faster if you work from a simple audit checklist instead of random changes. Focus on your homepage, top service pages, and any content that should be a go‑to resource for your niche.\n\nKey factors:\n- Whether AI tools currently surface your brand for core queries\n- Existing technical health (speed, crawlability, structured data)\n- Quality of your Q&A, FAQ, and topical content\n- Internal bandwidth for content and dev updates\n\nIn week 1–2, run AI queries, map gaps, and fix critical crawl issues. In weeks 3–6, rewrite content around users’ real questions, implement FAQ/schema markup, and re-test AI visibility monthly.\n\nIf you don’t have in‑house SEO or dev support, consider bringing in a partner for the audit and initial implementation, then maintain it internally.",
