            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Most small to mid-sized sites can significantly improve AI visibility within 1–3 months, with stronger, more consistent results over 6–12 months as content and authority mature. Technical fixes and better FAQs often show impact fastest.\n\nTimelines depend on how broken things are now and how quickly you can ship changes. AI tools re-crawl and retrain differently from search engines, so improvements tend to show in waves rather than overnight.\n\nKey factors:\n- Current technical health and content quality\n- How often AIs already cite you or your competitors\n- Speed of implementation (dev and content resources)\n- Domain age and existing authority\n\nExpect quick wins in weeks 4–8 from fixing crawl issues and rewriting top pages around clear questions and answers. Deeper authority-building and topic clusters tend to show in AI answers over several months.\n\nIf you need faster validation, focus first on a narrow set of high‑value queries and track visibility there before expanding site‑wide.",
