        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "When is it worth hiring someone to handle structured data generation instead of trying to do it myself?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Structured data generation becomes worth hiring a specialist for when you have complex schemas, many page types, multi-location operations, or need synthetic data for testing and analytics at scale.\nIf it’s mission‑critical for SEO or AI, expert design pays off.\n\nKey factors:\n- Number of templates and domains\n- Importance of rich results and AI visibility to revenue\n- Complexity of data sources and relationships\n- Internal skill gaps in schema design and validation\n\nPractically, if you’re operating across cities like Los Angeles and Denver and rely on organic traffic, consider at least a one‑time engagement to design your schema model and rollout plan.\nYou can keep routine maintenance in‑house afterwards.\nAsk potential partners to show concrete examples and error‑rates from past projects.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "It’s worth hiring a specialist when you have complex schemas, many templates, multi-location sites, or depend heavily on organic traffic and AI visibility. An expert can design a robust schema model, automate generation, and set up validation so your in‑house team can safely maintain it."
            }
          }
        ],
