            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "In cities like Los Angeles, San Diego, Austin, Denver, and Salt Lake City, local search and AI answers often depend on clear location signals in your structured data.\nWithout accurate addresses, hours, and categories, your visibility can suffer even if your content is strong.\n\nKey factors:\n- Precise geocoded addresses and phone numbers\n- Correct business categories and services per city\n- Consistent naming conventions and URLs\n- Alignment between on‑page NAP (name, address, phone) and schema\n\nPractically, generate location-specific structured data for each city page or branch, and double-check that every property matches the visible contact information.\nMonitor local impressions and map‑pack presence after implementation.\nIf local visibility is strategic, schedule regular audits of your location schema.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Yes. For local visibility, you need accurate, city-specific structured data with addresses, phones, hours, and categories that match your on‑page details. Clean location schema helps search and AI systems correctly surface your Los Angeles, San Diego, Austin, Denver, and Salt Lake City operations."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Yes. For local visibility, you need accurate, city-specific structured data with addresses, phones, hours, and categories that match your on‑page details. Clean"
      }
