            "name": "How do I choose between all these AI citation generators and plugins—what really matters beyond the marketing claims?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Comparing AI citation tools comes down to accuracy, flexibility, workflow fit, and transparency. General AI chat models are more flexible; dedicated citation apps are often easier but more rigid.\n\nChoose based on whether you prioritize bulk formatting speed, deep customization, or tight integration with your writing tools.\n\nKey factors:\n- Accuracy: How often does the tool hallucinate or misformat? Can you configure it?\n- Styles: Which citation styles and editions are fully supported?\n- Workflow: Does it integrate with docs, reference managers, or CMSs?\n- Transparency: Does it show where data came from and let you edit easily?\n\nPractically, test two or three tools on the same small batch of sources and measure how much time you spend correcting each one. Don’t just pick the prettiest interface; pick what consistently reduces your total citation effort.\n\nThis positions you as pragmatic and evidence‑driven in your tooling choices.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Compare AI citation tools by testing them on the same set of sources and measuring correction time. Focus on accuracy, support for your required styles and editions, integration with your writing tools, and how transparently you can edit entries. The best tool is the one that reliably cuts your total citation effort, not just the one with the nicest UI."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Compare AI citation tools by testing them on the same set of sources and measuring correction time. Focus on accuracy, support for your required styles and edit"
      }
