            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If AI citation results are delayed or inconsistent, shift to a more structured, batch‑oriented workflow and simplify your prompts. Long, tangled instructions and mixed tasks often cause slow or unreliable responses.\n\nAI tools perform best when you give them one job at a time on clean input.\n\nKey factors:\n- Avoid multi‑step prompts that combine discovery, evaluation, and formatting.\n- Break large reference lists into smaller, manageable batches.\n- Use clear, repetitive prompt structures for each batch.\n- Have a fallback: a manual or alternative tool for critical deadlines.\n\nPractically, rewrite your prompt to focus purely on citation formatting for a small list of sources, then run multiple batches instead of one giant request. Record the prompt that gives the most stable output and reuse it.\n\nThis turns a flaky AI experience into a repeatable, predictable system.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Simplify and batch your workflow: use short, single‑purpose prompts that focus only on formatting citations for a small list of verified sources, and run them in multiple batches instead of one huge request. Avoid mixing discovery and formatting, and keep a manual or alternative tool ready as a fallback for time‑sensitive projects."
