            "name": "I’m overwhelmed—what’s the very first thing I should do to optimize my website for answer engines and voice search?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "The best starting point is to identify the real questions your customers ask and rebuild a few core pages around clear Q&A structures.\n\nYou don’t need to redo your whole site at once; focus first on the pages most likely to earn voice answers.\n\n**Key factors**\n- Pull question queries from Search Console, support tickets, and sales calls.\n- Add question-based H2s and 40–60 word direct answers near the top.\n- Create an FAQ section with natural, conversational questions.\n- Implement FAQ and Speakable schema on those pages.\n\nBegin with a content audit of 5–10 priority pages, rework them into answer-first formats, then monitor changes in featured snippets, “People Also Ask,” and voice traffic.\n\nTreat it as an iterative project: optimize, measure, refine, then expand to the rest of your site.",
