        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Can answer engine optimization for voice search backfire or hurt my rankings if I do it wrong?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Poorly executed AEO can backfire if answers are misleading, over-optimized, or technically broken.\n\nVoice assistants are cautious about low-quality or inconsistent information.\n\n**Key factors**\n- Overly promotional or vague answers may be ignored or downranked.\n- Incorrect schema markup can confuse crawlers and hurt visibility.\n- Thin content built only for keywords can reduce trust signals.\n- Inconsistent NAP data can harm local and “near me” voice results.\n\nTreat every answer as a mini, factual commitment: verify accuracy, keep claims modest, and align information across your site and profiles.\n\nThink of AEO as strengthening clarity, not gaming algorithms—quality and consistency are the safeguards.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Yes. If AEO leads you to write vague, misleading, or thin answers, or you implement broken schema or inconsistent business data, your rankings and trust signals can suffer. Focus on accurate, well-structured, genuinely helpful answers and clean markup to avoid negative side effects."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Yes. If AEO leads you to write vague, misleading, or thin answers, or you implement broken schema or inconsistent business data, your rankings and trust signals"
      }
    },
