            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You don’t need a dedicated developer to start AEO; many key steps are content and configuration changes.\n\nTechnical help becomes more important as you push into advanced schemas and performance tuning.\n\n**Key factors**\n- Content teams can handle Q&A rewrites and FAQ creation.\n- Markup often can be implemented via CMS plugins or tag managers.\n- Developers are helpful for custom schema, speed, and complex site structures.\n- Collaboration matters so content and technical changes support each other.\n\nBegin with content-led AEO and basic plugin-based schema, then involve developers once you identify performance or markup needs beyond what tools can handle.\n\nThink of AEO as a cross-functional effort where content leads, with technical support on key bottlenecks.",
