            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For a business in Salt Lake City, local seasonality and regional phrasing can matter in voice queries.\n\nAnswer engine optimization should reflect how locals actually talk and search throughout the year.\n\n**Key factors**\n- Capture questions about winter access, parking, or hours during snow.\n- Include nearby landmarks, canyons, and neighborhoods in natural language.\n- Use LocalBusiness schema with accurate service areas around Salt Lake City.\n- Refresh content periodically to reflect seasonal offerings and conditions.\n\nInterview local customers and staff about the phrases they use with phones (“closest,” “open now,” “in Sugar House,” etc.), then bake those into Q&A content.\n\nTreat AEO as a living reflection of your Salt Lake City reality, not a static, generic set of answers.",
              "@type": "Answer",
