            "name": "Can I handle most answer engine optimization for voice search myself, or do I really need to hire a specialist?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You can absolutely combine DIY efforts with professional tools or advisors; many teams do the foundational AEO work themselves.\n\nOutside help is most valuable for strategy, audits, and complex technical changes.\n\n**Key factors**\n- DIY: question research, content rewrites, basic FAQs, and simple schema.\n- Tools: monitor AI overviews, snippets, and question queries at scale.\n- Experts: deep audits, structured data strategy, and performance tuning.\n- Hybrid approach often yields the best cost-to-impact ratio.\n\nDecide which tasks your team is comfortable owning and where you need specialized guidance, then structure the engagement around those gaps.\n\nThink of professional support as a way to accelerate and de-risk your AEO work, not as a replacement for your internal knowledge.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "You can handle many core AEO tasks yourself—researching real questions, rewriting content into Q&A, adding FAQs, and using basic schema tools. Specialists are most useful for audits, advanced structured data, and performance tuning. A hybrid approach, where you do the groundwork and experts refine it, is often ideal."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "You can handle many core AEO tasks yourself—researching real questions, rewriting content into Q&A, adding FAQs, and using basic schema tools. Specialists are m"
      }
