            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "To compare voice search optimization vendors, look beyond buzzwords and focus on how they handle research, content, schema, local SEO, and measurement. Ask each to walk through a concrete example of voice improvements they’ve driven and how they tracked success.\n\nMany providers bundle voice into generic SEO; you want evidence that they’ve adapted to assistant‑centric behavior, not just renamed old tactics.\n\nKey factors:\n- Depth of question and intent research (beyond simple keyword lists)\n- Proven experience with FAQ, LocalBusiness, and Speakable schema\n- Integration with local SEO and Google Business Profile work\n- Transparent reporting on snippets, queries, and local interactions\n\nPractically, request a small diagnostic or sample plan for one of your core pages and compare approaches. The best partners will talk specifics, tradeoffs, and timelines—not just promise “top rankings.”\n\nA disciplined comparison helps you avoid paying for rebranded legacy SEO instead of true voice optimization.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Compare providers by how they handle real question research, FAQ/LocalBusiness/Speakable schema, local SEO, and measurement. Ask for concrete examples of improved snippets and voice queries and a sample plan for one of your pages. Avoid vendors who only offer generic “SEO” claims without voice‑specific tactics."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Compare providers by how they handle real question research, FAQ/LocalBusiness/Speakable schema, local SEO, and measurement. Ask for concrete examples of improv"
      }
