              "text": "If you’re under intense time pressure—for example, ahead of a seasonal rush in Austin—focus on the “fast wins” for voice search: local profiles, existing high-traffic pages, and FAQ blocks. These usually move the needle quicker than large site-wide rebuilds.\n\nAssistants prioritize current, trustworthy local information and concise answers, so tightening these elements can show impact in weeks, not months. Deep content expansion can wait until after your crunch period.\n\nKey factors:\n- Upcoming seasonal or event-driven demand\n- State of your Google Business Profile and reviews\n- A handful of high-traffic, high-intent pages ready for refinement\n- Available bandwidth for content tweaks vs. major development\n\nRun a short sprint: fully update your Austin listings, add conversational FAQs and snippet-ready answers to 3–5 critical pages, and test real voice queries on your phone. Use the results to decide what to tackle next once the deadline passes.\n\nIn urgent scenarios, think “optimize what matters most now, expand later.”",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "On a short timeline, prioritize quick wins: fully update your Austin Google Business Profile, refine 3–5 key pages with question-based headings and 40–60 word answers, add FAQ sections, and encourage fresh reviews. These changes can improve voice visibility faster than a full site overhaul."
