        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What is voice search SEO, and how is it different from regular SEO?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Voice search SEO means optimizing your content and site so voice assistants like Siri, Alexa, and Google Assistant can easily understand, select, and read your answers aloud to users.\n\nIt focuses on natural, spoken questions, local intent, and quick, snippet-style answers that devices can deliver instantly. Done well, it can win you “position zero” answers and more local traffic from “near me” searches.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Conversational, question-based keywords (who/what/where/how).\n- 40–60 word direct answers that can become featured snippets.\n- Strong mobile performance (fast load, easy tap-to-call, HTTPS).\n- Schema markup (FAQPage, LocalBusiness, HowTo, Speakable) and up-to-date business info.\n\nStart by listing your customers’ most common spoken questions, auditing your top pages for conversational tone, and adding brief Q&A sections with clear answers and proper schema. Over time, track impressions and clicks for question-style queries in Google Search Console.\n\nIf you want help, look for an SEO partner that explicitly understands voice search, featured snippets, and local schema—not just traditional keyword ranking.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Voice search SEO is the process of optimizing your site so voice assistants can understand, select, and read your content as spoken answers to user questions. It focuses on conversational queries, local intent, snippet-style answers, mobile performance, and structured data, rather than only on typed keywords and desktop rankings."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Voice search SEO is the process of optimizing your site so voice assistants can understand, select, and read your content as spoken answers to user questions. I"
      }
