            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "The core of voice search SEO is designing content around the natural questions people ask and providing clear answers that assistants can easily read aloud.\n\nUnder the hood, it’s a blend of conversational keyword research, structured data, local optimization, and technical performance tuning.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Research question-based, long-tail queries using tools and Search Console.\n- Structure pages with question headings and short answers, followed by detail.\n- Implement schema (FAQPage, LocalBusiness, HowTo, Speakable) to flag answerable sections.\n- Maintain strong mobile UX: speed, layout, and tap-friendly calls-to-action.\n\nThink of voice search SEO as turning your site into a well-organized Q&A library, not just a set of keyword-stuffed pages. Identify and answer the top 10–20 spoken questions your audience has, then build out from there.\n\nA good SEO partner will help you systematize this across your content rather than treating voice search as a one-off tweak.",
