              "text": "On a tight budget, focus on the free or low-cost actions that drive most of the impact: content, local profiles, and basic technical hygiene.\n\nYou don’t need expensive tools to make your site more voice-friendly; you need well-targeted questions and clean answers.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Use free tools like Google Search Console and simple question generators.\n- Update Google Business Profile and key local citations thoroughly.\n- Add FAQ sections and question-style headings to top pages.\n- Prioritize mobile speed improvements that your existing developer can handle.\n\nSet a small monthly routine: review queries, add or refine 2–3 Q&As, and ensure your core pages stay fast and accessible. As results grow, you can reinvest into more advanced schema or content support.\n\nIf you do engage an expert, be clear that your priority is high-impact fundamentals, not an oversized retainer.",
