            "name": "What are the risks if I ignore voice search SEO and just stick with my current strategy?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If you don’t optimize for voice search, you risk losing visibility for a growing share of high-intent local and informational queries, especially on mobile.\n\nCompetitors who answer spoken questions better may become the default suggestions from assistants.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Fewer appearances in “near me” and conversational searches.\n- Missed chances at featured snippets and position-zero answers.\n- Underutilized Google Business Profile visibility.\n- Potential mismatch between your content and user expectations.\n\nEven a basic voice search SEO pass—adding FAQs, improving local signals, and speeding up mobile pages—can prevent these losses. You don’t need perfection, but you should avoid being invisible.\n\nA provider who treats voice search as part of overall user experience, not a gimmick, can help you prioritize the most important fixes.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Ignoring voice search SEO means you’ll likely miss a growing stream of high-intent, mobile-heavy queries, especially “near me” searches and conversational questions. Competitors who optimize for spoken answers may capture featured snippets and assistant recommendations, reducing your visibility and potential leads over time."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Ignoring voice search SEO means you’ll likely miss a growing stream of high-intent, mobile-heavy queries, especially “near me” searches and conversational quest"
      }
