            "name": "How much does mobile speed and performance really matter for voice search SEO?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Voice search relies heavily on mobile performance; slow or clumsy pages are less likely to be favored as answers.\n\nSpeed and usability directly affect whether users stay long enough for your content to be considered authoritative.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Aim for mobile load times under about two seconds on key pages.\n- Use responsive design and easily tappable buttons (call, directions).\n- Optimize images, scripts, and hosting for fast delivery.\n- Ensure HTTPS and basic technical SEO health.\n\nRun performance checks on your most important pages and prioritize fixes that significantly cut load time and improve stability. Combine this with good content and schema to strengthen your voice search readiness.\n\nIf your site is slow, involving a developer alongside SEO support is often necessary.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Mobile speed and performance matter a lot for voice search SEO. Fast, secure, responsive pages with simple interactions are more likely to be favored by search engines and provide a good user experience, which supports higher visibility for spoken queries and featured snippets."
            }
          }
