            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For multi-location businesses in places like Los Angeles, San Diego, Austin, Denver, and Salt Lake City, create dedicated pages for each location and optimize them individually for voice search.\n\nThis lets you match city-specific queries and local intent more precisely.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Separate location pages with unique content, NAP, and local details.\n- LocalBusiness schema and city-specific FAQs on each page.\n- Consistent data across Google Business Profiles and citations.\n- Internal links that help users and crawlers navigate between locations.\n\nStart with your highest-traffic or most competitive locations and build a repeatable template: local intro, services, FAQs, schema, and contact options. Apply and refine this pattern as you roll out to other cities.\n\nExperienced multi-location SEO support can help prevent data inconsistencies and schema errors at scale.",
