            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "To target “near me” voice search keywords, combine your core service phrases with natural spoken questions that include proximity and city references. Then support them with strong local signals and accurate business data.\n\nPeople rarely say just “Answer Engine Optimization (AEO) software near me.” They ask things like “where can I get same-day Answer Engine Optimization (AEO) software near me” or “who does affordable Answer Engine Optimization (AEO) software in Denver that’s open late.” Your content and schema should match that level of detail.\n\nKey factors:\n- Use phrases mixing service + proximity + qualifier (same-day, cheap, open now)\n- Create city-specific pages with unique content and embedded maps\n- Ensure NAP (name, address, phone) consistency across listings and schema\n- Answer local questions directly in FAQs: parking, neighborhoods, hours, rush options\n\nPractically, list your top cities (e.g., Los Angeles, San Diego, Austin, Denver, Salt Lake City) and draft 10–20 natural “near me” questions per city. Optimize location pages and GMB profiles around those themes.\n\nRobust local voice keywords make assistants more confident recommending you when users ask nearby questions.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Combine your core services with natural “near me” questions that include city names and qualifiers (same-day, open now, affordable). Build unique location pages for Los Angeles, San Diego, Austin, Denver, and Salt Lake City, keep NAP data consistent, and answer common local questions in FAQs and schema."
            }
