            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Voice search keyword optimization typically takes a few weeks to research and implement, and another 2–3 months before you see consistent impact in rankings and traffic. It’s a medium-term investment, not an overnight quick fix.\n\nSearch engines and voice assistants need time to crawl new content, understand schema, and test your pages against competing answers before consistently surfacing you in responses.\n\nKey factors:\n- Research and planning: 1–3 weeks, depending on site complexity\n- Implementation: 2–6 weeks across content, FAQs, and schema\n- Initial impact: usually visible in 6–12 weeks in impressions and snippets\n- Full effect: 4–9 months, especially for competitive queries\n\nPractically, set expectations with your team that this is part of ongoing SEO, not a one-time campaign. Track featured snippets, FAQ impressions, and local query visibility as early signals of progress.\n\nTreat voice optimization timelines like other organic SEO efforts—slow but compounding.",
