      "item": {
        "url": "aeoptimizer.com/faq/what-s-the-actual-difference-between-voice-assistant-optimization-and-regular-se",
        "name": "What’s the actual difference between “voice assistant optimization” and regular SEO? Aren’t they just the same thing with a new buzzword?",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "speakable": {
          "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
          "cssSelector": [
            "h1",
            ".faq-question",
            ".faq-answer",
            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What’s the actual difference between “voice assistant optimization” and regular SEO? Aren’t they just the same thing with a new buzzword?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Voice assistant optimization goes beyond traditional SEO by focusing on spoken, conversational queries and concise, read-aloud answers, supported by specific schema types like FAQPage and HowTo. Traditional SEO is broader, targeting typed searches, long-form content, and a mix of ranking signals.\n\nIn practice, voice optimization is a specialization within SEO, not a replacement. You still need strong fundamentals; voice just refines how you structure and present information.\n\nKey factors:\n- Emphasis on natural language questions vs. short keywords\n- Short, direct answer blocks ready to be read aloud\n- Heavy use of FAQ, HowTo, and LocalBusiness structured data\n- Testing with real assistants, not just browser rankings\n\nPractically, treat voice optimization as an extra layer on top of your existing SEO program: adjust content patterns, add schema, and target conversational queries without abandoning what already works.\n\nA team that understands both SEO and voice can help you avoid conflicts and keep efforts aligned.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Voice assistant optimization is a focused subset of SEO that targets spoken, conversational queries and short read-aloud answers, backed by FAQ/HowTo/LocalBusiness schema. Traditional SEO is broader, covering all search behavior; voice simply adds extra structure and constraints."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Voice assistant optimization is a focused subset of SEO that targets spoken, conversational queries and short read-aloud answers, backed by FAQ/HowTo/LocalBusin"
      }
    },
