            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Voice assistant optimization for eCommerce means structuring product and category content so assistants can answer “best,” “price,” “availability,” and “how to” questions, and guide users toward purchase. Product and FAQ schema play a big role here.\n\nIf assistants can’t easily find and interpret your product details and common questions, they’ll favor marketplaces or competitors with cleaner data.\n\nKey factors:\n- Product schema with price, availability, reviews, and descriptions\n- Category and guide pages with Q&A and HowTo content\n- Voice-friendly answers about shipping, returns, and sizing\n- Fast, mobile-first UX for browsing and checkout\n\nPractically, start by optimizing your top-selling product and category pages with detailed, structured data and topical FAQs. Then test voice queries like “best [product] for [use]” and adjust content accordingly.\n\nAn optimization partner familiar with commerce can help align voice improvements with real conversion goals.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "For eCommerce, voice optimization means adding rich Product schema, Q&A, and HowTo content so assistants can answer questions about “best,” price, and availability. Focus on top products and categories, with concise, voice-ready answers about features, shipping, and returns."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "For eCommerce, voice optimization means adding rich Product schema, Q&A, and HowTo content so assistants can answer questions about “best,” price, and availabil"
      }
