            "name": "I’m in a destination city like Las Vegas—how should voice assistant optimization account for tourists and short-term visitors using Siri/Google?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For businesses in Las Vegas and similar destinations, voice assistant optimization should target time-sensitive, situational queries like “open now,” “near my hotel,” and “best option for tonight.” That means real-time accuracy and clear, action-oriented answers.\n\nVisitors rely heavily on assistants for quick decisions; stale or vague information leads them elsewhere fast.\n\nKey factors:\n- Up-to-date hours, events, and offers in LocalBusiness and Event schema\n- Location-context FAQs (near which hotels, on which strip, parking)\n- Strong integration with maps and navigation actions\n- Fast, mobile-friendly pages that load well on hotel Wi-Fi\n\nPractically, align your content and schema with the most common visitor scenarios and keep time-sensitive data updated daily or weekly. Test queries from typical visitor locations.\n\nAn optimization strategy tuned to destination behavior helps you capture high-intent, in-the-moment voice searches.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "In destination cities, focus on situational, time-sensitive queries like “open now” and “near my hotel.” Keep hours and events current in LocalBusiness/Event schema, build location-context FAQs, and ensure maps and mobile experiences work flawlessly."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "In destination cities, focus on situational, time-sensitive queries like “open now” and “near my hotel.” Keep hours and events current in LocalBusiness/Event sc"
      }
    },
