        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How do I get Siri to show my business when people in Los Angeles say ‘near me’ or ‘in LA’?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "The quickest way to show up on Siri for “near me” searches in Los Angeles is to claim and optimize your Apple Maps listing and make sure your local SEO signals point clearly to your LA location. Most changes start to matter within a few days to a few weeks.\n\nSiri leans heavily on Apple Maps for local business results, then cross-references that with other authoritative signals like reviews, citations, and your website. In a competitive city like LA, quality and consistency matter more than just being listed.\n\nKey factors:\n- Claimed Apple Maps listing with “Los Angeles” clearly in address and service area\n- Consistent NAP and hours across Yelp, Google, and other directories\n- Localized content on your site mentioning Los Angeles neighborhoods and queries\n- A steady stream of real, positive reviews from LA customers\n\nPractically, claim your Apple Maps profile, add LA-specific details, photos, and categories, then audit your existing listings for mismatched addresses or phone numbers. Add a local FAQ page that answers “in Los Angeles” style questions and encourages reviews from nearby customers.\n\nIn a dense metro like LA, think “local depth” instead of just “local presence” if you want Siri to choose you over dozens of similar options.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "In Los Angeles, you need a fully claimed and optimized Apple Maps listing that clearly anchors you in LA, plus consistent local listings, LA-focused content on your site, and strong reviews. These combined signals help Siri trust and surface your business for “near me” and LA queries."
