            "name": "What’s the right first step if I want my business to start showing up on Siri?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For most businesses, the first step is claiming your profile in Apple Business Connect (which controls Apple Maps), then cleaning up your local listings and website. You don’t need special tools to start; you do need patience and consistency.\n\nSiri pulls business data directly from Apple Maps, but it also checks other sources to confirm your information. Starting in the right order prevents you from amplifying bad or inconsistent data.\n\nKey factors:\n- Step 1: Claim/verify Apple Maps via Apple Business Connect\n- Step 2: Fix NAP consistency across major directories\n- Step 3: Add natural-language FAQs and local content to your website\n- Step 4: Encourage and respond to reviews\n\nPractically, block out a few hours to claim your Apple listing, then run a basic audit of your existing profiles (Yelp, Google, Bing, etc.) to fix mismatches. Once your data is clean, add simple Q&A content that mirrors how your customers talk to Siri.\n\nGetting the sequence right up front saves you from having to undo a network of inconsistent listings later.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Start by claiming and optimizing your Apple Maps listing through Apple Business Connect, then fix your name, address, and phone across major directories, and add natural-language FAQs to your site. This order gives Siri clean, consistent data to work with from day one."
            }
