          {
            "name": "How long does it usually take for changes in Apple Maps to show up in Siri results?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "In most cases, once you claim or update your Apple Maps listing, basic changes can appear in Siri within a few hours to a few days, but full trust and consistent visibility often take several weeks or more. Category and review changes may take longer.\n\nSiri needs time to ingest your updates, reconcile them with other sources, and adjust rankings against competitors. The more conflicting data you had before, the longer it can take.\n\nKey factors:\n- Simple field edits may show quickly; ranking shifts are slower\n- High-conflict or duplicate listings delay stable visibility\n- Review growth and behavioral signals accumulate over months\n- Competitive markets (Austin, Denver, etc.) move more slowly\n\nPractically, make your Apple Maps and citation changes, then monitor Siri for 2–4 weeks, checking different phrasing and query types. Continue improving reviews and content during this window instead of assuming nothing is happening.\n\nThink of Siri visibility timelines as similar to local SEO: partially fast, but fully mature only with patience and ongoing effort.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Minor Apple Maps updates can show in Siri within hours or days, but meaningful ranking and visibility improvements typically take several weeks. The more competitive and inconsistent your previous data was, the longer it takes Siri to fully trust and surface you."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Minor Apple Maps updates can show in Siri within hours or days, but meaningful ranking and visibility improvements typically take several weeks. The more compet"
      }
