          {
            "name": "Is there some hidden Siri setting that makes my app or service show up more often in Siri suggestions?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "There isn’t a single setting that “turns on” Siri recommendations for your app or service; instead, Siri learns from your app’s integration, user behavior, and Apple’s own guidelines. For most businesses, Siri suggestion visibility is controlled more by data than by a switch.\n\nOn iOS, users can control whether individual apps are allowed to show in Siri & Search, but that’s on the user’s device, not something you can override as a business. You influence suggestions by providing structured content and good engagement.\n\nKey factors:\n- Proper app support for SiriKit/intents (if you have an app)\n- High-quality metadata, screens, and content in your app and listings\n- User opt-in to allow your app in Siri & Search settings\n- Strong usage and retention signals\n\nPractically, review Apple’s documentation for SiriKit if you have an app, and ensure your App Store listing, in-app content, and Apple Maps data align. Encourage users to keep Siri & Search enabled for your app in their settings and to use your key features frequently.\n\nThink of Siri suggestions as earned via usefulness and clarity, not guaranteed by a checkbox.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "There’s no magic Siri setting you can flip as a business. Siri suggestions depend on proper integration (like SiriKit), high-quality metadata and content, and real user engagement, plus users allowing your app in Siri & Search settings on their devices."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "There’s no magic Siri setting you can flip as a business. Siri suggestions depend on proper integration (like SiriKit), high-quality metadata and content, and r"
      }
    },
