              "text": "If Siri keeps recommending your competitors in San Diego, it usually means their data, reviews, and content are stronger and more consistent than yours. Siri isn’t “anti-you”; it’s simply picking what looks safest and most relevant.\n\nVoice assistants rely on trust signals. When another business checks more boxes for reliability and popularity, Siri leans in that direction even if you’re closer or cheaper.\n\nKey factors:\n- Competitors have more reviews and higher ratings in San Diego\n- Their Apple Maps listings are richer and more accurate\n- Their websites better match common Siri-style questions\n- Your NAP or categories may be incomplete or confusing\n\nPractically, audit the businesses Siri recommends: compare their Maps listings, reviews, and on-site FAQs to yours. Close the gap by improving your own data, asking happy customers for reviews, and tuning your content to San Diego-specific queries.\n\nTreat competitor visibility as a roadmap for what Siri wants to see from you, not a permanent disadvantage.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Siri is favoring your competitors in San Diego because their Apple Maps listings, reviews, and website content send stronger, clearer signals than yours. Study their profiles, then improve your own data, reviews, and local content to give Siri a better reason to recommend you."
