        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Is it really worth spending time on Siri visibility, or is it just a nice-to-have?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For businesses that rely heavily on immediate walk-in or urgent-service traffic (like HVAC, urgent care, or 24/7 repair), investing in Siri visibility is especially valuable. For purely online or niche B2B services, it’s still helpful but less critical.\n\nSiri shines when people are on the move or in a hurry, asking for nearby help without scrolling through lists. If those moments are part of your customer journey, Siri is worth real effort.\n\nKey factors:\n- Dependence on local, time-sensitive “near me” queries\n- Physical location that customers visit or where you dispatch from\n- Mobile-heavy audience (drivers, travelers, commuters)\n- Competition already showing in Siri for your category\n\nPractically, map out how often your ideal customers are likely to speak their needs instead of typing. If the answer is “often,” prioritize Apple Maps optimization, reviews, and voice-friendly content.\n\nThink of Siri as another front door for your business; if your customers use it, leaving it locked is a missed opportunity.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "It’s worth serious effort if your business depends on local, time-sensitive “near me” customers who search on their phones. Siri plays a big role in those moments, and showing up there can mean immediate visits or calls that you’d otherwise miss."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "It’s worth serious effort if your business depends on local, time-sensitive “near me” customers who search on their phones. Siri plays a big role in those momen"
      }
    },
