        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What should I do first for a brand-new business so Siri can find me as quickly as possible?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For a new business, the fastest and safest way to start showing up on Siri is to set up your Apple Maps listing during or right after opening, then immediately standardize your information across major local directories. Don’t wait until you “have traction.”\n\nNew businesses are invisible by default; any delay in publishing clean data simply gives competitors a head start in voice search and maps.\n\nKey factors:\n- Early Apple Maps listing with accurate opening date and hours\n- Consistent NAP in Google, Yelp, Bing, and key niche sites\n- A basic but clear website with local-schema and FAQs\n- An intentional plan to collect first reviews\n\nPractically, as soon as your address and phone are final, create your Apple Maps entry, then copy that data into other platforms, and launch a simple site with a “new in town” FAQ page. Ask initial customers to leave honest reviews to seed trust.\n\nThink of Siri visibility as part of your launch checklist, not an afterthought.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "For a new business, create and verify your Apple Maps listing immediately, then mirror that data across major directories and a simple website with local-schema and FAQs. Start collecting early reviews so Siri has trustworthy signals from day one."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "For a new business, create and verify your Apple Maps listing immediately, then mirror that data across major directories and a simple website with local-schema"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 492,
      "item": {
        "url": "aeoptimizer.com/faq/can-siri-or-siri-search-settings-on-someone-s-iphone-stop-my-business-from-showi",
        "name": "Can Siri or Siri & Search settings on someone’s iPhone stop my business from showing up for them?",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "speakable": {
          "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
          "cssSelector": [
            "h1",
            ".faq-question",
            ".faq-answer",
            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Can Siri or Siri & Search settings on someone’s iPhone stop my business from showing up for them?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You can’t directly control what Siri recommends on an individual iPhone, but your customers can disable or limit Siri, and restricted settings can affect how often they see voice results. As a business, your job is to make sure that when Siri is on, your data is ready.\n\nOn iOS, users can turn off Siri entirely or restrict certain content types. If their device hides Siri & Search, they simply won’t see or use those recommendations.\n\nKey factors:\n- Siri can be disabled in Settings by the user\n- Content & Privacy Restrictions may hide Siri & Search\n- Individual app settings control Siri’s learning behavior\n- You can’t override customer privacy choices\n\nPractically, don’t assume a specific customer will see your business via Siri; instead, optimize for the many users who keep Siri enabled. You can gently remind customers who rely on Apple devices that Siri can find you if they use voice search.\n\nRespect that Siri access is a user choice, and focus on being the best result when they do opt in.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Yes. Users can disable Siri or restrict Siri & Search on their iPhones, which prevents voice recommendations from appearing. You can’t override those settings, so your focus should be on clean, optimized data for the many users who keep Siri enabled."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Yes. Users can disable Siri or restrict Siri & Search on their iPhones, which prevents voice recommendations from appearing. You can’t override those settings,"
      }
    },
