            "name": "Do I really need to hire a local SEO or “voice search” expert to show up on Siri, or can I do it myself?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You don’t have to hire a specialist to show up on Siri, but it can help once you’re dealing with many locations, messy legacy data, or complex schema. For a single location, most owners can manage the essentials themselves.\n\nThe DIY work is straightforward but tedious: claiming listings, fixing inconsistencies, and writing voice-friendly content. Pros mainly save you time and help avoid technical missteps.\n\nKey factors:\n- Number of locations and existing listings\n- Your comfort with local SEO and schema markup\n- Complexity of your services and regions\n- Budget for ongoing optimization and monitoring\n\nPractically, start by doing the basics yourself for a few weeks—Apple Maps, core citations, simple FAQs—and see how far you get. If you hit a wall or have too many locations to manage, consider bringing in help for the technical and scaling parts.\n\nThink of professionals as accelerators, not gatekeepers; Siri visibility is achievable either way.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "You can handle Siri visibility yourself for one or a few locations by claiming Apple Maps, fixing listings, and adding voice-friendly content. Hiring an expert becomes useful when you have many locations, complex legacy data, or need advanced schema and ongoing monitoring."
