            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If Siri isn’t reflecting your new hours or temporary changes in Salt Lake City, it’s likely that your updates either haven’t fully propagated or conflict with other listings. Siri tends to trust the most consistent information across sources.\n\nSeasonal or emergency hour changes are especially vulnerable to outdated data lingering on third-party sites.\n\nKey factors:\n- Whether Apple Maps shows the correct hours already\n- Matching hours in Google, Yelp, and other directories\n- Website and schema updated to the new schedule\n- Time elapsed since your change\n\nPractically, first confirm your hours in Apple Maps, then immediately update them on your main directories and your website, preferably with a clear notice. Check Siri a few days later using different phrasing (e.g., “Are they open now?”) to see if the update sticks.\n\nFor time-sensitive businesses, keeping hours aligned everywhere is critical so Siri doesn’t misinform customers.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Siri is likely seeing conflicting hours between Apple Maps, your other listings, and your website, or your updates haven’t fully propagated yet. Make sure Apple Maps, major directories, and your site all show the same new schedule, then give it a few days."
            }
          }
