            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "To optimize a specific product for Alexa, you start by rewriting its title, bullets, description, and FAQ to answer the exact spoken questions customers ask about that item, then adjust backend keywords and visuals accordingly. Finally, test those questions on Alexa devices.\n\nThe goal is to make that product the most obvious, clear match when someone speaks a problem or need that it solves.\n\nKey factors:\n- Natural, speech‑friendly product title that front‑loads core attributes.\n- Bullets written as short answers to customer questions instead of feature lists.\n- FAQ content that covers “how,” “why,” and “what if” queries for that product.\n- Backend keywords populated with long‑tail, conversational phrases.\n\nPick one high‑value product, build a list of 20–30 common spoken questions about it, and rewrite all visible copy plus backend terms around those questions. Then ask those questions to Alexa and track how often your product appears.\n\nOnce you’ve proven a playbook on one product, you can scale the same structure to others without reinventing the process each time.",
