            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If you’ve already used a listings service and Alexa still doesn’t show you, there may be hidden issues like duplicate profiles, wrong categories, or stale data the tool didn’t fix.\n\nSoftware doesn’t catch everything; you still need a manual review.\n\nKey factors:\n- Check for duplicates under old names, addresses, or phone numbers\n- Verify that your categories and descriptions match how customers talk about you by voice\n- Look for outdated hours or services on any directory your tool syncs with\n- Confirm that your website’s NAP and schema match the listings data\n\nSet aside time for a manual sweep of your most important profiles and your website, correcting anything your service missed, then re-test Alexa.\nTreat listing software as a helper, not a substitute for periodic human oversight.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "A listings service can miss duplicates, bad categories, old addresses, or mismatched hours, all of which confuse Alexa. Manually audit your Google/Yelp/Bing/Apple Maps profiles and your website NAP/schema, fix anything the software didn’t catch, and then test Alexa again for name and category searches."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "A listings service can miss duplicates, bad categories, old addresses, or mismatched hours, all of which confuse Alexa. Manually audit your Google/Yelp/Bing/App"
      }
