            "name": "What’s the most cost-effective way for a small business to start ranking in Google Assistant without buying a bunch of tools?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For small businesses on a tight budget, the most efficient way to rank in Google Assistant is to focus on three things: question-based content on key pages, Google Business Profile optimization, and basic FAQ schema. These are high-impact and low-cost.\n\nYou don’t need expensive tools to start; you need clear answers to the questions your customers already ask and a well-maintained local presence.\n\nKey factors:\n- Pull questions from support emails, chats, and sales calls.\n- Turn those into H2 headings with direct answers underneath.\n- Fully complete your Google Business Profile and keep reviews flowing.\n- Implement simple FAQ schema using free generators or plugins.\n\nPractically, set aside time to write 15–30 real FAQs and add them to your main service pages, then update your profile description and photos to match. Use free or bundled tools in your CMS to add structured data.\n\nDone well, this gives you a meaningful shot at Assistant answers without big software or agency costs.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "On a tight budget, focus on three things: add real question‑and‑answer sections with concise responses to key pages, fully optimize your Google Business Profile and reviews, and implement basic FAQ schema using free tools or plugins. These low‑cost steps give you a strong chance to be chosen for Google Assistant answers."
            }
