            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "No, you can absolutely start optimizing for Google Assistant yourself, as long as you’re comfortable editing your site and profiles. A professional helps with strategy and scale, but the core steps are DIY-friendly.\n\nMost of the work involves content rewrites, structured data, and local profile management—all things owners or in-house marketers can learn and execute with guidance.\n\nKey factors:\n- Your comfort with basic CMS editing and plugins.\n- Ability to research real questions and write clear answers.\n- Willingness to test and validate schema implementations.\n- Time to monitor rankings and refine over months.\n\nPractically, begin with 1–2 key pages, rewrite them around real questions, add FAQ schema, and improve your Google Business Profile. If you later hit a plateau or have complex multi-location needs, that’s a good moment to bring in an expert.\n\nStarting DIY builds your understanding, so even if you hire help later, you’ll make better decisions and avoid flashy but ineffective tactics.",
