            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For service businesses in Austin or Denver, ranking in Google Assistant often comes down to balancing local presence with clear expertise. You want to be the best local answer, not just another listing.\n\nAssistant tends to favor businesses that combine strong profiles with content that proves they understand the problems their local customers face.\n\nKey factors:\n- City-specific landing pages answering “how much,” “how long,” and “who” questions.\n- References to local neighborhoods, typical project types, and seasons where relevant.\n- LocalBusiness schema and consistent NAP across regional directories.\n- Steady inflow of local reviews mentioning city and service details.\n\nPractically, build an Austin or Denver page that directly answers the top 10–15 questions your local customers ask, then add FAQ schema to those answers. Pair that with a fully filled-out profile and review strategy.\n\nThis makes Google Assistant see you as the authoritative local solution when nearby users ask service-related voice questions.",
