          {
            "name": "What technical SEO factors really affect my rankings in voice search?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "The biggest technical ranking factors for voice search are **page speed**, **mobile optimization**, **HTTPS/security**, and **structured data**. If your site is slow or hard to parse, it’s unlikely to be chosen for voice answers.\n\nVoice queries are often made on phones, and the assistant wants to deliver an instant, reliable response. Technical issues send negative quality signals even if your content is good.\n\nKey factors:\n- Fast load times, optimized images, and minimized scripts.\n- Responsive design and clean mobile layouts.\n- HTTPS, crawlable site structure, and XML sitemaps.\n- Schema markup (FAQ, LocalBusiness, HowTo, Article) to clarify content.\n\nRun speed tests, fix performance bottlenecks, and ensure your site passes basic mobile usability checks. Then add structured data for key pages so search engines can confidently extract and read your answers.\n\nIf you’re not technical, start with a PageSpeed or Core Web Vitals report and work with a developer to address the top issues first.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Technical voice search ranking factors include fast page speed, mobile-friendly responsive design, HTTPS security, and structured data like FAQ and LocalBusiness schema. These signals help search engines quickly load, understand, and trust your pages, making them more likely to be selected for voice answers."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Technical voice search ranking factors include fast page speed, mobile-friendly responsive design, HTTPS security, and structured data like FAQ and LocalBusines"
      }
    },
