          {
            "name": "How long do spoken search queries usually take to process and answer?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "A spoken search query typically takes 1–3 seconds to recognize your voice and another 1–3 seconds to fetch and read a result, depending on your connection.\nOn fast Wi‑Fi, responses can feel almost instantaneous.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Internet speed and network stability\n- Device processing power and assistant used\n- Length of your query and complexity of the answer\n- Whether the assistant is loading apps, maps, or media\n\nIf responses feel slow, test your network, close unused apps, and shorten your query to the essential question.\nFor time-sensitive tasks like directions around Los Angeles traffic, start with a simple spoken query, then refine once navigation is running.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Most spoken search queries answer in 2–6 seconds end-to-end, depending mainly on your internet speed and device. Short, focused questions on solid Wi‑Fi feel nearly instant, while complex or map-heavy requests can take a bit longer."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Most spoken search queries answer in 2–6 seconds end-to-end, depending mainly on your internet speed and device. Short, focused questions on solid Wi‑Fi feel ne"
      }
