        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Does using spoken search queries cost me money or data, and what’s the hidden downside?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Spoken search itself is usually free, but it can use mobile data, and poor queries may cost you time and frustration.\nThe main “cost” is network usage, battery drain, and occasional misfires.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Data usage for streaming voice to the cloud\n- Battery consumption on phones and smart speakers\n- Time spent repeating or correcting misunderstood queries\n- Potential privacy trade-offs for voice recordings\n\nTo limit costs, use Wi‑Fi when possible, keep spoken queries short, and disable saving voice history if you’re concerned about privacy.\nTreat spoken search as a fast, free front end—but be aware you’re paying with data, battery, and some personal information.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Spoken search is free to use, but it consumes mobile data and battery and can store your voice recordings. Use Wi‑Fi when possible, keep requests short, and review your assistant’s privacy settings to control what’s saved."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Spoken search is free to use, but it consumes mobile data and battery and can store your voice recordings. Use Wi‑Fi when possible, keep requests short, and rev"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 618,
      "item": {
        "url": "aeoptimizer.com/faq/what-should-i-do-when-spoken-search-queries-keep-failing-or-mishearing-me",
        "name": "What should I do when spoken search queries keep failing or mishearing me?",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "speakable": {
          "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
          "cssSelector": [
            "h1",
            ".faq-question",
            ".faq-answer",
            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What should I do when spoken search queries keep failing or mishearing me?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If your spoken search queries keep failing, start by checking your microphone, background noise, and how you’re phrasing the question.\nOften the issue is environmental or wording, not the assistant itself.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Microphone blocked, muted, or damaged\n- Loud TV, traffic, or echoing rooms\n- Long, multi-part questions confusing the system\n- Outdated app or device software\n\nTry a simple test phrase (“What time is it?”); if that fails, inspect mic settings, reboot the device, and update the assistant app.\nIf only complex queries misfire, break them into two or three shorter spoken questions instead of cramming everything into one.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "When spoken search keeps failing, test your mic with a simple question, reduce background noise, and break complex requests into shorter queries. Also check app permissions and updates, since outdated or blocked assistants misinterpret speech more often."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "When spoken search keeps failing, test your mic with a simple question, reduce background noise, and break complex requests into shorter queries. Also check app"
      }
    },
