            "name": "How do I know spoken search query results aren’t biased or just showing me ads first?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Spoken search can return biased or ad-heavy results, especially for commercial queries like “best internet provider in Denver.”\nAssistants may prioritize sponsored or popular sources over niche or independent ones.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Use of paid placements and sponsored results\n- Reliance on a few large review platforms\n- Lack of transparency in ranking choices\n- Your tendency to accept the first answer without checking\n\nTo avoid bias, treat the first spoken answer as a starting point and scan at least a few on-screen options before deciding.\nFor important decisions—housing, healthcare, long-term services—use spoken queries to gather options, then research deeper across multiple sources.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Spoken search results can be influenced by ads and popular platforms, so don’t treat the first answer as definitive. Use voice to surface options, then review several on-screen results and cross-check information before making important decisions."
