        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What should I do if my conversational keyword content isn’t getting traffic or rankings?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If you’re not seeing results from conversational keywords, first check whether you’re targeting real questions, answering them clearly, and giving search engines proper signals. Often the issue isn’t the concept but execution.\n\nYou may also need more time or better alignment with user intent.\n\nKey factors:\n- Verify that queries exist: do they show impressions in Search Console?\n- Ensure your content is answer-first and uses the question in headings\n- Add FAQ or Q&A schema where relevant\n- Assess competition and adjust to less saturated or more specific variants\n\nPractically, run a small audit: pick 10 underperforming conversational keywords and search them yourself, comparing your page to top results. Adjust formatting, depth, or angle to better match what’s winning.\n\nIf several cycles pass with no movement, refine your question list with more evidence-based phrases from conversations instead of tool-generated ones.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "First confirm that you’re targeting real, searched questions by checking Search Console. Then ensure your content is answer-first, uses the query in headings, and includes FAQ/Q&A schema where appropriate. If competition is high, pivot to more specific variants based on actual customer conversations."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "First confirm that you’re targeting real, searched questions by checking Search Console. Then ensure your content is answer-first, uses the query in headings, a"
      }
