            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If you need AEO results quickly, prioritize low-hanging questions and pages that already perform decently in search, then tighten answers and add schema. You’re aiming for “fast wins” in citation share rather than a full overhaul.\n\nInitial improvements often appear within 60–90 days, but stronger visibility builds over several months as answer engines re-crawl and learn to trust your content.\n\nKey factors:\n- Target questions where you already rank or get impressions\n- Lead with crisp, 40–60 word answers for each question\n- Implement FAQPage and HowTo schema on existing pages\n- Monitor citations in ChatGPT, Perplexity, and AI Overviews regularly\n\nSet a 90-day sprint: refine content for 20–30 priority questions, apply schema, and log AI citations monthly. Use early feedback to iterate phrasing and structure.\n\nShort sprints won’t unlock full AEO potential, but they can validate the strategy and show whether deeper investment is warranted.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "You can often see early AEO gains within 60–90 days by tightening answers and adding FAQ/HowTo schema to existing high-opportunity pages. Focus on 20–30 priority questions, implement schema, then track citations in AI tools monthly to validate and refine your approach."
