            "name": "What does answer engine optimization typically cost and what actually drives the price up or down?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "The main cost drivers in AEO are question research, content rewriting, schema implementation, and ongoing monitoring, not just tools. Pricing ranges widely—from a few hundred dollars DIY to multi-thousand monthly programs.\n\nCosts depend on how many topics you cover, how deeply you update content, and whether you use in-house resources or external specialists. Technical complexity and scale also matter.\n\nKey factors:\n- Volume of questions and pages to optimize\n- Need for strategic research vs. basic implementation\n- Use of paid tools for schema, analytics, and tracking\n- Ongoing refresh cycles (every 2–3 months is common)\n\nStart by scoping: count priority questions, estimate rewrite time, and identify where you’ll need dev or specialist help. Pilot with a smaller subset before committing to large, recurring spend.\n\nTreat AEO as a long-term visibility investment; align budget with the potential revenue impact of owning key AI answers in your niche.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "AEO costs vary from low-cost DIY to multi-thousand monthly retainers, driven mainly by how many questions/pages you optimize, the depth of content rewrites, schema implementation effort, and ongoing monitoring. Start with a scoped pilot on a limited set of high-value questions to size realistic budget."
            }
