            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Answer engine optimization doesn’t guarantee top placement in AI answers, but it significantly increases your chances of being cited as a key source. Outcomes are usually measured in citation share and answer footprint rather than rankings.\n\nSuccess looks like your brand being referenced in AI tools’ responses across many of your priority questions, often with direct quotes or paraphrased content from your site.\n\nKey factors:\n- Citation frequency for target questions across multiple answer engines\n- Depth and accuracy of information AI pulls from your content\n- Visibility in AI Overviews and conversational search experiences\n- Lead and revenue impact from AI-driven discovery\n\nDefine a clear set of tracked prompts, then log whether your brand appears and how often. Adjust your content and schema based on what AI tools show or omit.\n\nViewed as an ongoing program, AEO outcomes compound over time as answer engines learn to trust your content more and reuse it across related questions.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "AEO won’t guarantee “ranking #1,” but it can materially increase how often AI tools cite your brand as a source for key questions. Track success through citation frequency, answer quality, visibility in AI Overviews, and the leads or sales that come from AI-driven discovery over time."
