            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "AEO offers stronger benefits than traditional SEO when your audience uses conversational, question-style queries and AI assistants to research decisions. In those scenarios, being the quoted source often matters more than having a top blue link.\n\nSEO still matters for classic search, but AEO aligns with how buyers increasingly ask “what” and “how” questions in chat interfaces and voice.\n\nKey factors:\n- Heavy use of AI assistants among your target personas\n- Complex, research-heavy buyer journeys with many questions\n- Need for authority and trust rather than just traffic\n- Opportunity to influence AI answers across an entire topic cluster\n\nCompare how often your audience discovers information via search vs. AI tools; if AI is growing quickly, prioritizing AEO can deliver outsized impact relative to incremental SEO gains.\n\nIn practice, the strongest results come from combining both, using SEO for reach and AEO for answer-level influence.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "AEO matters most when your buyers rely on AI assistants and conversational queries to research decisions. In those cases, being the cited source in AI answers is more valuable than another blue link. Use SEO for general visibility, but lean into AEO where question-based, AI-driven discovery is growing fastest."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "AEO matters most when your buyers rely on AI assistants and conversational queries to research decisions. In those cases, being the cited source in AI answers i"
      }
