              "text": "For local-focused businesses in Los Angeles and San Diego, AEO should combine local business schema with rich, question-based content about your services and neighborhoods. You want AI tools to understand both what you do and where you do it.\n\nThat means consistent NAP (name, address, phone) data plus pages that answer location-specific queries in natural language.\n\nKey factors:\n- LocalBusiness and Organization schema with accurate addresses\n- City-specific FAQs (e.g., “how does this work in Los Angeles?”)\n- Consistent business information across Google profiles and directories\n- Reviews and local signals that reinforce trust in each market\n\nCreate city-focused Q&A sections addressing unique local concerns—traffic, regulations, climate, timing—and mark them up with FAQPage schema. Keep local listings aligned with the same data.\n\nThoughtful AEO in LA and San Diego makes answer engines far more likely to reference your business for regional queries rather than generic national answers.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "For LA and San Diego, blend LocalBusiness schema with city-specific Q&A content. Maintain consistent NAP data, add location-focused FAQs about local conditions and services, and mark them up with FAQPage schema so AI tools understand both what you offer and where you operate."
