            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Voice search tends to drive more specific, higher-intent visits—people asking detailed questions or seeking nearby options right now. That can mean lower overall traffic but better-qualified leads and higher conversion rates, especially for local and service businesses.\n\nThink of voice long-tail keywords as a quality play, not a pure volume play.\n\nKEY FACTORS\n- Traffic may be modest but usually tightly aligned with intent\n- Better matches between question and answer can improve conversions\n- Local, “near me,” and time-sensitive phrases often perform best\n- Results accumulate over months as assistants “learn” your content\n\nTrack not just visits but actions tied to voice-style pages: calls, bookings, direction requests, and signups. Compare behavior on those pages to your broader SEO traffic to see how the quality differs. \n\nOutcomes from voice keyword work often look like “fewer but better” visitors rather than big spikes in sessions.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Expect more specific, higher-intent traffic rather than huge volume: people asking detailed questions or looking for nearby options “right now.” That usually translates into better-qualified leads and higher conversion rates, especially for local and service businesses, with gains building gradually over a few months."
