            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You don’t need a huge budget to compete in local voice search; most gains come from time and consistency rather than ad spend. With a few hours a month, you can fix listings, gather reviews, and build question-based content that assistants can easily read.\n\nPaid tools help, but they’re optional compared to getting the fundamentals right. Think of it like cleaning and organizing your digital storefront.\n\nKEY FACTORS\n- Claim and update all major listings—it costs only your time.\n- Ask every satisfied customer for a review to build trust signals.\n- Create FAQ sections that mirror real spoken questions from your customers.\n\nIf money is tight, prioritize free steps and only add paid tools once you’ve exhausted basic opportunities. Track calls, direction requests, and “near me” queries to prove value.\n\nOn a limited budget, discipline and real customer insight beat fancy software for voice search wins.",
              "@type": "Answer",
