            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "To optimize for “near me” voice searches in Los Angeles, you need accurate map listings, strong reviews, and content that mentions real neighborhoods and landmarks people reference. Voice assistants combine proximity, relevance, and trust when deciding who to read out loud.\n\nLA’s size means generic city-level targeting is often too broad; you have to get more granular.\n\nKEY FACTORS\n- Include areas like Silver Lake, Koreatown, Santa Monica, or DTLA where appropriate.\n- Keep Google Business Profile and Apple Maps details perfectly current.\n- Encourage local reviews that mention neighborhood names and services.\n\nAdd FAQ answers that mirror what locals say, like “Where’s a dog-friendly brunch spot in Echo Park?” and make sure your hours and parking info are crystal clear.\n\nWhen assistants hear “near me” in Los Angeles, you want them to know exactly which part of the city you serve and why you’re a strong option.",
              "@type": "Answer",
