              "text": "If results feel slow, first check whether you’ve fully implemented the basics—accurate listings, reviews, and question-based content—before assuming it “isn’t working.” Voice ecosystems can take several weeks or months to re-crawl and trust new data.\n\nYou might also be in a competitive category with strong incumbents.\n\nKEY FACTORS\n- Review insights for incremental gains in calls and directions, not just rankings.\n- Compare your review volume and rating to top local competitors.\n- Confirm your site is fast and mobile-friendly to avoid technical bottlenecks.\n\nIf fundamentals are solid but growth is flat after 3–6 months, consider deepening city-specific content, improving photos, and expanding FAQs. In crowded markets, differentiation matters.\n\nTreat “slow” as a signal to refine your inputs, not a reason to abandon voice optimization.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Recheck the fundamentals: clean listings, strong and recent reviews, fast mobile site, and solid FAQ content. Voice ecosystems can take months to adjust. If everything is in place and growth is still flat, deepen local content and reviews rather than abandoning the strategy."
