            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "In Los Angeles, voice assistants lean heavily on proximity, traffic realities, and neighborhood relevance, so you need to be explicit about where you are and who you serve.\n\nGeneric “Los Angeles” mentions aren’t enough; assistants and users often care which side of town you’re on and how fast they can get to you.\n\nKey factors:\n- Reference specific areas (e.g., DTLA, West LA, Hollywood, the Valley) on your site.\n- Set realistic service areas in Google Business Profile and Apple Business Connect.\n- Highlight “open now,” parking options, and transit access for on‑the‑go searchers.\n- Encourage reviews that mention neighborhoods or landmarks when natural.\n\nReview your content and listings to make sure they reflect the parts of LA you actually cover. The clearer you are about neighborhoods and access, the more likely assistants are to choose you for “near me” in such a sprawling metro.",
              "@type": "Answer",
