        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "If I’m just starting with featured snippets for voice search, what should I optimize first instead of trying to redo my whole website?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Start by optimizing just a handful of high-intent, question-based pages instead of trying to “voice search–optimize” your entire site at once.\n\nVoice results overwhelmingly pull from featured snippets, so focusing on your most valuable questions yields faster traction.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Choose 10–20 pages that already get search traffic and have clear Q&A potential\n- Add question headings, short direct answers, and supporting detail\n- Implement FAQ / HowTo / Speakable schema on those priority pages\n- Track performance in Search Console for queries and rich results\n\nPractically, build a small pilot: one FAQ hub, one how-to guide, and one product/service explainer, then refine based on what earns impressions or snippets. Scale the same patterns to the rest of your content once you see what works.\n\nThis focused approach gives you early featured-snippet wins without overwhelming your team or budget.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Don’t redo your whole site. Pick 10–20 existing pages that already get traffic, turn their main topics into question headings, add concise 40–60 word answers, and apply FAQ/HowTo/Speakable schema. Use this pilot group to earn your first voice-search snippets, then scale what works."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Don’t redo your whole site. Pick 10–20 existing pages that already get traffic, turn their main topics into question headings, add concise 40–60 word answers, a"
      }
