            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Do featured snippets from voice search actually lead to conversions or are they just “branding” vanity metrics?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Yes, featured snippets can drive conversions, but only if the spoken answer quickly points people to a next step they care about.\n\nMost voice results are top-of-funnel, so you need to bridge that quick answer into a clear path toward a deeper interaction.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Answer the core question completely enough to build trust\n- Include a subtle call-to-action or “what to do next” in nearby content\n- Make the underlying page fast, mobile-friendly, and easy to skim\n- Track assisted conversions from snippet landing pages, not just clicks\n\nIn practice, design snippet-focused sections that both satisfy the query and naturally lead into a comparison table, calculator, or clear benefit-driven explanation. Then watch how those pages influence sign-ups, demos, or purchases over time.\n\nThinking of snippets as micro-trust builders, not just traffic drivers, helps you align voice search with real business outcomes.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Featured snippets from voice search can drive conversions if the short spoken answer builds trust and the page behind it smoothly leads into a useful next step—like a comparison, calculator, or offer. Treat snippets as micro-trust moments and track assisted conversions from those landing pages."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Featured snippets from voice search can drive conversions if the short spoken answer builds trust and the page behind it smoothly leads into a useful next step—"
      }
    },
