            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You don’t need a huge budget for featured snippets; you need a focused content and technical checklist executed consistently.\n\nMost of the work is strategy, editing, and implementation—not paid tools or ads.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Core tasks: keyword research, content restructuring, and schema markup\n- Tools: you can start with free options (Search Console, Rich Results Test)\n- Biggest “cost” is writer and developer time, not software\n- ROI comes from durable organic and voice-search visibility\n\nOn a tight budget, prioritize 10–30 high-value questions, optimize those pages, and use lightweight schema generators or CMS plugins rather than custom development. Reuse internal resources instead of hiring an agency right away.\n\nTreat featured snippets as a low-cost amplification of your existing SEO rather than a separate expensive channel.",
