            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Featured snippets aren’t guaranteed, but they’re achievable if your content is relevant, clearly structured, and already ranking reasonably well.\n\nFor small sites, the path is narrower but often less competitive for very specific, long-tail questions.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Page 1 visibility: snippets almost always come from top results\n- Content quality: direct, jargon-free answers in natural language\n- Topic focus: niche questions are easier wins than broad ones\n- Patience: snippets can appear, disappear, and switch sources over time\n\nIf you’re a smaller site, lean into ultra-specific Q&A that bigger brands ignore, and provide the best possible explanation for those topics. Check your queries regularly to spot new opportunities and refine your answers.\n\nTreat snippet eligibility as a reward for great content and solid SEO, not a switch you can flip instantly.",
