            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If you’re in Los Angeles or San Diego, local cues can dramatically improve your chances for voice-search snippets on “near me” and city-specific queries.\n\nGoogle and assistants lean heavily on LocalBusiness and FAQ content that clearly signals your geography.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Use city names, neighborhoods, and local landmarks naturally in content\n- Implement LocalBusiness schema with accurate address and hours\n- Create localized FAQ pages answering city-specific questions\n- Optimize for “near me” phrases with mobile-friendly pages\n\nPractically, build separate location-aware sections (e.g., “How we handle X in Los Angeles”) and mark them up so assistants know they apply to searchers in that area. Keep your NAP (name, address, phone) fully consistent across the site and profiles.\n\nLocalizing your snippet strategy turns voice search into a real discovery channel in LA and San Diego.",
