            "name": "If I’m targeting customers in Salt Lake City, what should I do differently for featured snippets that are used in voice search?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If you’re in Salt Lake City, your featured snippet strategy should reflect local search behavior: a mix of family-oriented, outdoor, and faith-adjacent queries, often done on mobile.\n\nVoice assistants will favor content that feels locally tuned and practical.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Reference Salt Lake City, nearby suburbs, and major landmarks naturally\n- Offer clear information on hours, parking, weather, and seasonal changes\n- Use LocalBusiness and FAQ schema on location-specific pages\n- Keep pages lightweight and fast for mobile voice queries\n\nCreate Q&A that mirrors what someone might ask while driving to or around Salt Lake City, and structure answers so the first sentence is immediately useful. Update location details often so assistants can trust your data.\n\nLocal context makes your snippets relevant to real Salt Lake voice searches, not just generic traffic.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "In Salt Lake City, weave city names, suburbs, and landmarks into practical Q&A about hours, parking, weather, and seasonal changes. Combine this with LocalBusiness and FAQ schema on fast, mobile-friendly pages so assistants recognize your answers as relevant, up-to-date local voice-search snippets."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "In Salt Lake City, weave city names, suburbs, and landmarks into practical Q&A about hours, parking, weather, and seasonal changes. Combine this with LocalBusin"
      }
