        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Are there any real risks to chasing featured snippets for voice search, or is it basically harmless if I get things wrong?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "The biggest risk is not penalties but **missed opportunities**: poorly designed snippets can confuse users, hurt click-throughs, or send the wrong message when read aloud.\n\nVoice assistants will literally speak whatever you’ve written, including awkward or outdated phrasing.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Overly salesy or vague answers can sound untrustworthy when spoken\n- Outdated numbers or policies may spread via snippets long after changes\n- Ambiguous wording can misrepresent your offer or processes\n- Poor formatting might cause assistants to truncate important details\n\nMitigate risk by reviewing snippet-targeted text as if it will be read out loud, keeping it factual, clear, and time-stamped where relevant. Refresh high-impact answers regularly.\n\nTreat voice snippets as public statements, not just SEO copy, to protect your brand.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "The main risks aren’t penalties but miscommunication: awkward, vague, or outdated answers can sound bad when read aloud and confuse users. Write snippet-focused text as if it will be spoken, keep it factual and current, and refresh key answers so voice results don’t misrepresent you."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "The main risks aren’t penalties but miscommunication: awkward, vague, or outdated answers can sound bad when read aloud and confuse users. Write snippet-focused"
      }
    },
