        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "I had a bad experience with an SEO agency—how can I approach featured snippets for voice search now without getting burned again?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If you’ve had a bad experience with an SEO vendor, treat featured-snippet optimization as a transparent, measurable program rather than a black box.\n\nMost of the work can be documented as specific content and schema changes you can review yourself.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Require clear before/after examples of Q&A structures on target pages\n- Insist on access to Search Console and analytics to see real results\n- Use small pilots (5–10 pages) to prove value before scaling\n- Avoid vague promises; focus on specific queries and snippet formats\n\nWhether you do this in-house or with a new partner, define success upfront: which questions you want to own, how answers will be written, and what metrics you’ll watch. Review copy as if you’re the end user.\n\nA structured, evidence-based approach prevents the “trust me” problems that caused issues before.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Treat featured snippet work as a transparent, testable program: start with a small set of pages, review the exact Q&A and schema changes, and monitor Search Console and analytics yourself. Focus on explicit target queries and measurable snippet formats, not vague promises or black-box tactics."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Treat featured snippet work as a transparent, testable program: start with a small set of pages, review the exact Q&A and schema changes, and monitor Search Con"
      }
    },
