            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "In Austin, strong schema markup helps voice assistants understand both your local presence and your specialized services, which is important in a competitive, tech‑savvy market.\n\nCombining LocalBusiness, Organization, and relevant FAQ/HowTo schema lets you capture “near me,” “how do I,” and branded voice queries more reliably than relying on text alone.\n\nKey factors:\n- Mark your Austin address, phone, hours, and coordinates with LocalBusiness\n- Use FAQ schema for common service questions asked by local customers\n- Add HowTo schema where you provide step‑by‑step guides or tutorials\n- Ensure your Austin location is clearly referenced in visible page content\n\nPractically, build an Austin location page that includes both rich local details and FAQ‑style content, then apply matching JSON‑LD and test with voice queries like “Hey Google, who does Answer Engine Optimization (AEO) software in Austin?” \n\nPositioning: A well‑structured Austin schema setup turns your site into a clearer “answer source” for regional voice assistants.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "For Austin, add LocalBusiness schema with precise address, phone, hours, and coordinates, then layer FAQ and HowTo schema onto local content that answers common customer questions. This combination improves your chances of appearing in Austin‑focused “near me” and how‑to voice queries."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "For Austin, add LocalBusiness schema with precise address, phone, hours, and coordinates, then layer FAQ and HowTo schema onto local content that answers common"
      }
