        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Are there any real downsides or risks to optimizing my local business for voice search, or is it all upside?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "The biggest risk is **giving assistants outdated, inconsistent, or misleading information**, which can lead to frustrated customers and lower trust signals. Over-claiming service areas or hours can backfire when people arrive to find you closed or unavailable.\n\nAnother risk is chasing voice visibility with spammy tactics—stuffing “near me” everywhere, faking reviews, or using misleading categories. That can trigger penalties or make assistants prefer competitors.\n\nKey factors:\n- Honest, current hours and availability\n- Realistic service radius and travel times\n- Authentic reviews and transparent responses\n- Avoiding manipulative keyword stuffing and category misuse\n\nPractically, treat voice search optimization as a customer experience project, not just ranking. Ask yourself whether the assistant’s spoken description would match what a visitor actually sees when they show up.\n\nIf you focus on clarity and truth, the “risks” mostly vanish and voice search becomes a trust builder.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "The main risks come from inaccurate, overhyped information—like claiming wider hours or service areas than you really offer—or using spammy tactics such as keyword stuffing and fake reviews. If you keep your data honest and customer-focused, voice optimization is largely upside with minimal downside."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "The main risks come from inaccurate, overhyped information—like claiming wider hours or service areas than you really offer—or using spammy tactics such as keyw"
      }
    },
