              "text": "You don’t have to choose—**mobile SEO and voice search optimization overlap heavily**, and work on one usually helps the other. The key difference is that voice emphasizes conversational questions and immediate local intent.\n\nMobile SEO focuses on usability, speed, and readable content. Voice adds the layer of “Can an assistant quickly extract a spoken answer that makes sense?” Ignoring either weakens the other.\n\nKey factors:\n- Fast, mobile-friendly pages (critical for both)\n- Conversational, question-based content and FAQs (especially for voice)\n- Schema and clean Business Profiles (supporting all local results)\n- Reviews and trust signals (important in all contexts)\n\nPractically, treat mobile and voice as the same project: improve speed and layout, then rewrite content to sound natural when read aloud and capture common questions. Optimize profiles and schema to support both.\n\nThis way, you spend effort once and gain benefits across devices and assistants.",
