        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How do AI voice assistants decide which business to actually mention in their spoken answers?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "AI voice assistants pick who to mention by combining relevance, clarity, trust, and structured data. They favor sources that answer the exact spoken question in plain language and are backed by strong local and entity signals.\n\nInstead of reading a single web page, assistants blend information from multiple evidence sources. If your brand appears across those sources with consistent data and helpful content, your chances of being named increase dramatically.\n\nKey factors:\n- Question-matching: content that uses the full spoken question as a heading\n- Answer quality: short, complete responses that stand alone\n- Trust signals: reviews, citations on reputable sites, and real author profiles\n- Schema markup and accurate business profiles that make your data machine-readable\n\nAudit how you show up today for core questions, then rebuild pages so your first 40–60 words could be read verbatim as an answer. Pair that with schema and local optimization. Over time, you become the “safe choice” assistants mention.\n\nYou’re not gaming the system; you’re making it easy for AI to see you as the most helpful, dependable answer.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "AI voice assistants choose mentions based on how well your content matches the spoken question, how clear and self-contained your answers are, and how strong your trust and structured-data signals look. Conversational Q&A content plus solid schema and local listings is what moves you into the pool of businesses they’ll name."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "AI voice assistants choose mentions based on how well your content matches the spoken question, how clear and self-contained your answers are, and how strong yo"
      }
