            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For Los Angeles businesses, being mentioned in AI voice search hinges on pairing neighborhood-relevant content with clean local data and schema. Voice assistants lean heavily on geo signals for such a dense, competitive market.\n\nYou need to sound like you serve real LA users while making it trivial for machines to confirm who you are and where you are. Generic content rarely wins clear mentions here.\n\nKey factors:\n- Include LA-specific landmarks, neighborhoods, and user scenarios in your Q&A\n- Maintain precise NAP data across Google Business Profile, Apple Maps, Yelp\n- Add LocalBusiness schema with geo coordinates and hours for each location\n- Encourage and respond to reviews; assistants use them as trust filters\n\nCraft FAQs that answer how you help people in places like Silver Lake, Koreatown, or Santa Monica, then mark those answers up with FAQPage and Speakable schema. Tie everything back to accurate local listings.\n\nIn a city like LA, “local clarity” is often what gets your name spoken instead of a generic competitor.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "In Los Angeles, focus your AI voice optimization on local relevance and clean data: write FAQs around real LA neighborhoods and use cases, implement LocalBusiness and FAQ schema, and keep NAP and hours consistent across Google, Apple, and Yelp. That local clarity helps assistants choose and mention you."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "In Los Angeles, focus your AI voice optimization on local relevance and clean data: write FAQs around real LA neighborhoods and use cases, implement LocalBusine"
      }
