            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "AI voice mentions don’t require a huge marketing team; a solo founder can make real progress by being systematic. The work is more about consistency than scale.\n\nIf you can dedicate a few focused hours per week, you can transform your most important pages into voice-ready assets and slowly expand from there. Assistants care about answer quality, not the size of your company.\n\nKey factors:\n- Prioritize 5–10 core questions your customers actually ask\n- Turn each into a question heading with a tight, direct answer underneath\n- Add simple FAQPage JSON-LD and keep local profiles current\n- Use plain language at an 8th–9th grade reading level for maximum clarity\n\nStart with one FAQ or guide page that targets your highest-intent queries, then listen to how customers phrase questions and mirror that language online. Revisit and refine answers monthly.\n\nThink of voice optimization as a habit you build into your content, not a one-time project only big teams can afford.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Yes. Even solo businesses can earn AI voice mentions by focusing on a handful of key customer questions, writing clear 40–60 word answers under question-style headings, adding FAQ schema, and keeping local listings clean. Consistency matters more than having a big marketing team."
