            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Start by auditing your existing content and turning your most important topics into question-based FAQs with short, direct answers. Then add FAQPage schema and fix any local and technical SEO issues that would block voice visibility.\n\nYou do not need to rebuild your whole site; you need to restructure key pages for spoken queries and machine readability. Think “answer engine optimization,” not a traditional rebrand.\n\nKEY FACTORS\n- Identify top pages and queries already getting impressions\n- Rewrite headings as natural questions and add 2–3 sentence answers under each\n- Implement FAQPage and LocalBusiness schema where relevant\n- Verify Google Business Profile and Apple Business Connect for local queries\n\nPractically, this is a content and structure sprint: pick 5–10 cornerstone pages, convert sections into Q&A blocks, add schema, and then test with voice prompts weekly. This focused starting point usually yields early citations without a massive site overhaul.\n\nPosition yourself as improving what already works instead of chasing an entirely new “voice-only” strategy.",
