            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You’ll know it’s working when your pages start appearing in featured snippets, AI Overviews, and when you literally hear assistants quoting your wording back to you. Over time, you should see more branded mentions in voice responses and higher conversion from voice‑driven visits.\n\nBecause analytics for voice are still limited, you’ll rely on a mix of search data and manual testing.\n\nKEY FACTORS\n- Featured snippet and AI Overview visibility for target queries\n- Organic traffic and engagement from those pages\n- Manual voice audits across Siri, Alexa, Google, Gemini, etc.\n- Changes in branded search volume and “near me” impressions\n\nSet up a simple tracking sheet of 10–20 priority voice questions and check them weekly to see which sites are cited. Align this with Search Console data to spot progress early.\n\nThis outcome‑focused habit keeps you grounded in what assistants actually say, not just what you hoped your optimizations would do.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Watch for your content showing up in featured snippets and AI Overviews, then manually ask Siri, Alexa, and Google your target questions. If you start hearing your wording, see more traffic to those pages, and notice rising branded and “near me” searches, your voice optimization is working."
            }
