            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "No, you don’t need to build a custom Alexa or Google Assistant “skill” to benefit from voice search as a contractor. For most local home‑service businesses, assistants rely on existing web data and listings.\n\nCustom skills are optional and usually only make sense for larger or specialized brands.\n\nKey factors:\n- Local voice queries typically pull from Google Business Profile, maps, and FAQs.\n- Building and maintaining a skill requires development effort and ongoing updates.\n- The return is often limited compared to strengthening basic local SEO.\n- Schema markup and reviews offer higher impact for less complexity.\n\nFocus on being the best‑structured, most trusted answer in the data assistants already use. Consider custom skills only if you have a clear unique interaction in mind.\n\nFor most contractors, fundamentals beat custom voice apps by a wide margin.",
