        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Why is Google Now / Google Assistant only showing text and not speaking responses out loud anymore?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If your phone only types your commands and doesn’t speak back, it usually means voice output or text‑to‑speech is disabled, muted, or misconfigured—not that Google Now/Assistant is broken. You can bring spoken responses back by checking a few audio and Assistant settings.\n\nSome devices switch to silent or “brief” modes, or have text‑to‑speech engines disabled during updates. Accessibility settings can also change how responses are delivered.\n\nKey factors:\n- Make sure **media volume** is up and not muted.\n- In Assistant settings, turn on **Speech output** or “Full” responses.\n- Confirm a text‑to‑speech engine is installed and enabled in system settings.\n- Battery saver or Do Not Disturb can suppress voice output on some phones.\n\nGo to Settings → Sound and raise media volume, then open the Google app → Settings → Google Assistant → Assistant voice & sounds and select full speech output. Also check Settings → Accessibility or Text‑to‑speech to ensure a voice engine is active.\n\nTreat this like an audio configuration issue; once the right toggles are on, spoken answers usually come back immediately.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "This usually isn’t Google Assistant breaking—your **speech output and media volume** are likely disabled or misconfigured. Turn media volume up, enable full speech output in Assistant settings, and check that a text‑to‑speech engine is active in system settings so the assistant can speak responses again."
