            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Compared to Siri and Alexa, Google Assistant (which replaced Google Now) is generally best at pure web search, navigation, and context questions, while Siri integrates tightly with Apple apps and Alexa shines with smart‑home routines. The “best” depends on what you do most.\n\nIf you live in Google’s ecosystem—Maps, Gmail, Calendar—Assistant often feels more natural. iPhone users may prefer Siri’s integration, while smart home fans with many Echo devices like Alexa’s routine flexibility.\n\nKey factors:\n- **Assistant**: strongest search and Maps/navigation capabilities.\n- **Siri**: best integration with iOS and Apple services.\n- **Alexa**: strong smart‑home and multi‑device routines.\n- Device choice (Android, iOS, smart speakers) heavily influences fit.\n\nList your top 5 voice tasks (e.g., navigation, reminders, smart‑home control) and see which platform aligns with them and your hardware. Many people end up using Assistant on phones for search and Maps but keep Alexa or Siri where they fit best.\n\nTreat it as a toolbox: Google Now’s successor is one tool, not the only one.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Google Assistant is usually **best for search and navigation**, Siri is best integrated into Apple devices, and Alexa excels at smart‑home routines. Instead of fully “switching,” match each assistant to what you do most and the devices you already own."
