            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If Google Assistant keeps saying “I’m offline” when you know you have service, the issue is usually with your actual data connection, a captive Wi‑Fi portal, or app/network settings—not the assistant itself. You can narrow it down with a few checks.\n\nSometimes Wi‑Fi shows as “connected” but requires a login, or mobile data is restricted for the Google app specifically.\n\nKey factors:\n- Verify **real internet access** by loading a webpage or video.\n- Check that the Google app can use **mobile data** and background data.\n- Avoid flaky public Wi‑Fi with captive portals when you need voice.\n- Restart router/phone and toggle airplane mode to refresh connections.\n\nTest Assistant on mobile data with Wi‑Fi off; if that works, your Wi‑Fi is the culprit. In Settings → Apps → Google → Mobile data, ensure data isn’t restricted, and review any VPN or firewall apps.\n\nThink of this as debugging your network path first; once connectivity is solid, Assistant’s “offline” errors usually disappear.",
