            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "AEO strategy works by identifying the questions your buyers ask, creating or restructuring content to answer them directly, and marking those answers up with schema so answer engines can reliably extract and trust them. It’s part content design, part technical markup, and part authority building.\n\nAnswer engines scan your pages for clear question‑answer pairs with strong credibility signals; your job is to make those easy to find and verify.\n\nKey components:\n- Question research from search data, calls, chats, and forums\n- Direct‑answer layouts (answer first, detail second)\n- Schema markup (FAQPage, HowTo, Article, Organization, LocalBusiness)\n- E‑E‑A‑T signals: experience, expertise, authoritativeness, trustworthiness\n\nPractically, you’ll map 50–100 buyer questions to specific pages, fix the structure and headings, add concise answer blocks, and implement JSON‑LD markup that matches visible content.\n\nWhen done consistently, AEO turns your website into a well‑indexed Q&A library that AI systems can safely quote across multiple search and assistant surfaces.",
