        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How long does it actually take to see results from an AEO strategy?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "AEO strategy usually takes 3–6 months to show meaningful results because answer engines need time to crawl, interpret your new structure and schema, and test your content in AI Overviews, snippets, and voice responses. You may see isolated wins sooner, but broad impact is rarely immediate.\n\nTimelines depend heavily on how much existing authority your site already has and how quickly you implement changes.\n\nKey timing factors:\n- Crawl and index cycles for your website\n- Domain strength and past performance in search\n- Volume and quality of new or restructured Q&A content\n- Consistency of schema implementation and error‑free markup\n\nPractically, plan your AEO work in 90‑day sprints: first to audit and restructure, then to expand coverage and refine based on early signals.\n\nTreat early answer placements as proof you’re on the right track, not the finish line.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Most businesses see meaningful AEO results in 3–6 months. Answer engines need time to crawl revised content, interpret new schema, and experiment with your answers in AI Overviews and snippets. Expect a few early wins sooner, but plan for at least one or two 90‑day cycles before judging overall impact."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Most businesses see meaningful AEO results in 3–6 months. Answer engines need time to crawl revised content, interpret new schema, and experiment with your answ"
      }
    },
