            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For a SaaS or software product, AEO strategy should focus heavily on practical buyer questions about pricing, integrations, onboarding, security, and ROI, structured as clear Q&A content with product and Organization schema. These are exactly the queries AI tools summarize during vendor research.\n\nYour goal is to become the most quotable source on how your software works, fits, and pays off.\n\nKey focus areas:\n- Feature vs. value explanations in question‑form headings\n- Comparisons, integration details, and setup steps with HowTo schema\n- FAQs on data handling, uptime, support SLAs, and roadmap\n- Case‑study snippets showing real outcomes and metrics\n\nPractically, map each core buying question to a page section and ensure that section opens with a concise, factual answer.\n\nDone right, AEO turns your documentation and marketing site into a sales asset that AI tools surface during evaluation, not just at the awareness stage.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "For SaaS and software, AEO must concentrate on buyer research questions—pricing, integrations, onboarding, security, and ROI—structured as clear Q&A with product‑friendly schema. You’re aiming to be the most quotable source for evaluation‑stage queries, not just general awareness, so focus on specifics and outcomes."
