          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Will AEO strategy help me get better‑qualified leads, or just more random traffic?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "AEO strategy can significantly improve lead quality because people who arrive via AI answers and detailed Q&A content tend to be further along in their research and clearer about what they need. They’ve already consumed a structured explanation before clicking through.\n\nThis usually leads to fewer “just browsing” contacts and more serious inquiries.\n\nKey lead‑quality drivers:\n- Coverage of middle‑ and late‑funnel questions (pricing, timelines, tradeoffs)\n- Clear explanations of who your solution is and isn’t for\n- Real examples, outcomes, and constraints woven into answers\n- Strong alignment between online answers and sales conversations\n\nPractically, monitor leads that originate from your Q&A‑style pages and compare close rates and deal sizes to other sources.\n\nDone well, AEO becomes a filter that educates and qualifies prospects before they ever fill out a form.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "AEO tends to improve lead quality, not just volume. Visitors who come in through AI answers and Q&A‑structured pages have already consumed clear explanations of pricing, timelines, and fit. They’re usually further along in research, so you see fewer casual inquiries and more serious, qualified prospects."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "AEO tends to improve lead quality, not just volume. Visitors who come in through AI answers and Q&A‑structured pages have already consumed clear explanations of"
      }
    },
