        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How does AEO strategy tie into voice search and assistants like Google Assistant or Siri?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Voice search and assistants rely heavily on clear, conversational questions and concise, speakable answers—exactly what AEO strategy is designed to produce. By shaping your content for natural language and adding schema like Speakable and FAQPage, you increase the chances that voice tools read your content aloud.\n\nThis matters most for “how,” “can I,” and “should I” queries users ask away from screens.\n\nKey optimization tactics:\n- Use natural, question‑based headings that sound like real speech\n- Keep lead paragraphs short, direct, and jargon‑light\n- Add Speakable schema to key sections where possible\n- Ensure LocalBusiness data is correct for location‑aware voice queries\n\nPractically, test your top questions on popular assistants and note which answers they use—then refine content to match the tone and structure they favor.\n\nAEO for voice becomes a competitive edge as more users rely on hands‑free answers.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "AEO directly supports voice search by structuring content as natural questions with concise, speakable answers and schema like FAQPage and Speakable. Voice assistants prefer short, clear, conversational responses, so AEO makes your content easier to read aloud and more likely to be selected for hands‑free queries."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "AEO directly supports voice search by structuring content as natural questions with concise, speakable answers and schema like FAQPage and Speakable. Voice assi"
      }
