        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What does it actually mean to optimize for answer engines and how is it different from regular SEO?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You optimize for answer engines by restructuring your content around real questions, giving direct, one‑sentence answers at the top, and backing them with clear, well‑formatted detail and schema markup.\n\nAnswer engines scan for concise, unambiguous answers they can safely quote, then check surrounding context, site quality, and entity signals before citing you.\n\nKey factors:\n- Use question‑style headings and place the answer immediately underneath.\n- Apply FAQPage, HowTo, Article, and Organization schema where relevant.\n- Keep language precise, avoid fluff, and front‑load key facts.\n- Maintain fast, technically sound pages with clear information hierarchy.\n\nStart by auditing your top pages, rewriting them in an “answer first, detail second” structure, and adding schema in JSON‑LD format.\nAs you iterate, track how often AI systems mention or cite your brand name for priority queries.\n\nDone well, answer‑engine optimization quietly positions your site as the “safe answer” systems rely on.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Optimizing for answer engines means structuring content so AI systems can instantly extract a clean, trustworthy answer plus supporting context, using question‑based headings, direct answers, and schema markup. It goes beyond traditional SEO by focusing on machine readability, entity clarity, and citation‑worthiness, not just rankings and clicks."
            }
          }
        ],
