            "name": "What does it really take for my site to be one of the sources AI answer engines quote in their responses?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "To get cited by AI answer engines, you need pages that give short, definitive answers followed by well‑structured detail, plus strong authority and entity signals around your brand.\n\nAnswer engines prefer sources that are clear, consistent, and easy to parse, especially for high‑risk or technical topics.\n\nKey factors:\n- Lead with a 1–2 sentence “direct answer” high on the page.\n- Use schema (FAQPage, HowTo, Article, Organization) to mark up content types.\n- Demonstrate expertise with author bios, references, and original insights.\n- Keep terminology consistent so engines don’t have to guess what you mean.\n\nPractically, pick a few priority topics, rewrite them in an answer‑first format, add schema, and promote them so they earn mentions and links from trusted sites.\nMonitor AI tools periodically to see if your brand starts appearing in their answer citations.\n\nOver time, this makes your site feel like a “safe citation” for answer engines, which is the real goal.",
