            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Start by auditing how AI tools currently describe or recommend you, then compare that to how you want to be presented and close the gaps with clearer identity and schema.\n\nIn Austin or Denver, this means checking for both brand and local mentions, then tightening the wording and signals those systems see.\n\nKey factors:\n- Ask multiple AI tools to summarize your brand and note inconsistencies.\n- Create a single “canonical proof” page that clearly states who you are, what you do, and where.\n- Add Organization and LocalBusiness schema with consistent names, addresses, and categories.\n- Use a short “how to describe us” sentence and repeat it on key pages.\n\nPractically, write and implement your identity block and schema first, then update top content pages to use the same phrasing and descriptors.\nRecheck AI summaries monthly to see if your new structure is being reflected.\n\nFor Austin and Denver businesses, tightening identity and local signals sharply improves how answer engines talk about you.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Audit how major AI tools describe you, then publish a clear “proof page” with a tight identity statement, consistent wording, and Organization/LocalBusiness schema. Reuse that phrasing on key pages so answer engines in Austin and Denver converge on a single, accurate description."
