            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Answer engines rely heavily on your brand’s entity data, so it’s important that your name, descriptions, and locations (like Austin, Denver, Salt Lake City) stay consistent everywhere.\n\nIf those signals are messy, AI systems may merge you with other entities or show outdated information.\n\nKey factors:\n- Consistent company name, category, and short description across your site.\n- Aligned NAP (name, address, phone) details for each city.\n- Unified Organization schema that points to correct profiles and domains.\n- Clean, up‑to‑date local profiles on major platforms and review sites.\n\nAudit your site, schema, profiles, and major directories, fix mismatches, and standardize how you describe your business in one short sentence reused everywhere.\nReconnect that identity to your question‑based content so engines see one coherent story.\n\nStrong entity hygiene is the foundation that makes all other AEO efforts stick.",
