            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "In cities like Los Angeles and San Diego, answer engines care about both your expertise and local relevance, so your content should reflect regional examples and use LocalBusiness schema.\n\nLocal questions (“near me,” neighborhood specifics, regulations, climate) often shape what AI surfaces for users.\n\nKey factors:\n- Include city‑specific contexts, examples, or constraints in key guides and FAQs.\n- Mark up location details with LocalBusiness schema tied to each office.\n- Ensure local pages have direct, answer‑style responses to regional questions.\n- Keep local reviews and profiles active to support trust signals.\n\nDevelop a set of locally flavored question pages (e.g., “How does X work in Los Angeles vs. San Diego?”) and optimize them in answer‑first format.\nCheck how AI tools respond to location‑based queries and refine where needed.\n\nThoughtful localization makes it easier for answer engines to match your answers to nearby users.",
