            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Local businesses can use answer engine optimization examples like Q&A sections about services, “near me” questions, and detailed Google Business Profile content. These help AI assistants and search overviews answer local queries with your business details and reviews.\n\nInstead of just listing services, you explain them through natural questions your customers ask about price, process, and expectations. This creates content answer engines can easily surface and cite.\n\nKey factors:\n- A FAQ page answering “How much does X cost?”, “How long does Y take?”, “Do you serve my neighborhood?”\n- Short how-to or preparation guides (e.g., “How to prepare for a roof inspection”).\n- Detailed, accurate profiles on Google and major review sites with up-to-date categories and descriptions.\n- Customer reviews that mention specific use cases and outcomes.\n\nCollect recurring questions from calls and emails, then turn each into a clear Q&A entry on your site and profiles. Use everyday language, include approximate ranges when possible, and keep information updated.\n\nIf you’re a local service provider, shifting your site to answer-style content can materially improve how you show up in AI local recommendations.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "For local businesses, strong AEO examples include FAQ pages that answer cost, timing, and service-area questions, short how-to or preparation guides, and detailed Google Business Profile plus review-site descriptions. These give AI assistants clear, structured information to use when answering “near me” and “who should I hire” queries."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "For local businesses, strong AEO examples include FAQ pages that answer cost, timing, and service-area questions, short how-to or preparation guides, and detail"
      }
