            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "In cities like Los Angeles and San Diego, answer engine optimization examples often revolve around local intent questions and lifestyle scenarios. Think content that answers “best,” “near me,” “is it worth it,” and “how does this work in my area?” in clear, quotable language.\n\nDense, competitive markets push answer engines to rely on well-structured, trustworthy sources. That means your site has to provide more than a service list; it should address local nuances and user concerns directly.\n\nKey factors:\n- City-specific FAQs like “How long does X usually take in LA traffic?” or “Do you serve North County San Diego?”\n- Pages that explain neighborhood differences or local regulations in simple terms.\n- Local guides that combine recommendations with your expertise, not just lists.\n- Updated content reflecting seasonal or event-driven demand (e.g., summer, festival, sports season).\n\nAudit your content for generic phrases and replace them with concrete answers tied to LA or San Diego realities that customers actually ask about. Make each question a heading and answer it fully in the first few sentences.\n\nIf your brand serves multiple California markets, AEO can help differentiate your presence in each city’s AI-driven discovery layer.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "In Los Angeles and San Diego, strong AEO examples are city-specific FAQs, neighborhood and traffic-related Q&As, simple explanations of local rules, and updated seasonal guides. Each piece should answer a real, location-aware question in the first 2–3 sentences so AI tools can quote it for local queries."
            }
          }
