            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Great answer engine optimization examples for e‑commerce include product FAQs, comparison charts, and how-to guides that answer pre‑purchase questions directly. Each should start with the question in natural language, followed by a short, factual answer and then detail.\n\nOnline shoppers ask about fit, compatibility, returns, and use cases. Structuring content around those questions makes it easier for answer engines to recommend your product in AI results.\n\nKey factors:\n- Product pages with sections like “Will this work with…?” and “Is this true to size?”\n- Comparison articles like “Product A vs Product B: which should I buy if…?” opening with a clear recommendation.\n- How-to content that covers installation, setup, or styling with step-by-step instructions.\n- FAQPage and Product schema so machines understand and surface your Q&As.\n\nReview pre‑purchase chat logs and reviews to find the questions people ask before buying, then bake those into Q&A sections on key product and category pages. Aim for honest, specific answers, not vague marketing.\n\nIf you sell online, investing in AEO-style content can drive visibility in shopping assistants and AI guides, not just search listings.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "For e‑commerce, strong AEO examples are product FAQs about fit and compatibility, comparison pages that open with a clear recommendation, and how-to guides for installation or use. All should be structured as question headings with concise answers, and marked up with FAQPage and Product schema where appropriate."
