            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You can find answer engine optimization examples for your niche by looking at who already wins featured snippets, AI overviews, and People Also Ask boxes. Study how their content is structured, then adapt those patterns to your brand and audience.\n\nThe goal isn’t copying text but understanding which question formats, answer lengths, and schema types answer engines seem to favor for your topics.\n\nKey factors:\n- Search your core questions and note which sites show in snippets or AI summaries.\n- Analyze their use of Q&A headings, bullet lists, and short introductory answers.\n- Check whether they use FAQ, HowTo, Product, or LocalBusiness markup.\n- See how they address user intent (beginner vs advanced, buyer vs researcher).\n\nBuild a spreadsheet of top competitor examples and distill common patterns: intro length, heading style, use of visuals, and internal links. Then design your own content system using those insights while adding unique data or perspectives.\n\nIf this analysis feels overwhelming, a specialist can run an AEO audit and hand you a prioritized list of formats and pages to emulate.",
              "@type": "Answer",
