        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Can you give answer engine optimization examples that show experience and build E‑E‑A‑T?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Content that showcases real experience is a powerful answer engine optimization example, especially for topics where trust matters. You combine a concise, factual answer with first‑hand notes, case studies, or data that large language models can’t easily find elsewhere.\n\nAnswer engines increasingly favor E‑E‑A‑T (experience, expertise, authoritativeness, trustworthiness), so pages with genuine experience signals tend to be cited more often.\n\nKey factors:\n- Named authors with relevant credentials and a short bio on key pages.\n- “In our tests…” or “In our experience…” sections summarizing real outcomes.\n- Original data, studies, or benchmarks packaged in clear charts and narratives.\n- Transparent citations to reputable external sources where applicable.\n\nTake your most important topics and add a short experience section below the primary answer, explaining what you’ve actually seen in practice. Keep it specific and free of hype.\n\nIf your content is currently generic, weaving in authentic experience is one of the best AEO upgrades you can make.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Strong AEO examples for E‑E‑A‑T include Q&A pages with named expert authors, short “in our experience” sections, original data or studies, and transparent citations. These experience signals make your answers more trustworthy to AI systems, increasing the chance your content is quoted or recommended."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Strong AEO examples for E‑E‑A‑T include Q&A pages with named expert authors, short “in our experience” sections, original data or studies, and transparent citat"
      }
