        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What should I do if my answer engine optimization examples aren’t showing up in AI overviews or snippets?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If your answer engine optimization examples aren’t being picked up, it’s usually an issue with question selection, clarity, or authority signals. Sometimes you’re competing with stronger sites; other times answer volatility for your topic is simply high.\n\nDiagnosing the bottleneck helps you decide whether to refine content, change focus, or strengthen credibility.\n\nKey factors:\n- Are you targeting questions that matter to users and your business, or just long-tail curiosities?\n- Is your answer complete, specific, and easy to quote?\n- Do you show experience and expertise relative to competing sources?\n- Are technical basics like indexing and schema implementation correct?\n\nRun a quick audit: compare your content to pages currently winning snippets or AI citations for the same question and note gaps in clarity, depth, or trust signals. Adjust your examples accordingly and give answer engines time to re-evaluate.\n\nIf results remain slow, consider pivoting to less competitive questions where your brand can own the answer space.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "If AEO examples aren’t surfacing, audit them against pages that do appear: check whether you’re answering the right questions, providing clear and specific answers, demonstrating expertise, and using proper schema. Strengthen content and trust signals, then give answer engines time to reprocess your changes."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "If AEO examples aren’t surfacing, audit them against pages that do appear: check whether you’re answering the right questions, providing clear and specific answ"
      }
    },
