            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If you’ve had a bad SEO experience, an answer engine optimization checklist can give you transparency and control over what’s being done.\n\nThe checklist turns vague promises into specific, verifiable tasks so you can see how each change supports better answers and visibility. It’s also easier to audit and correct.\n\nKey factors:\n- Every checklist item should be understandable and testable\n- Tasks like schema implementation and heading changes can be validated with tools\n- You can tie improvements to concrete metrics (snippets, question traffic)\n- Clear documentation helps avoid “black-box” work from vendors\n\nUse the checklist as a shared framework with any agency or freelancer: require them to log completed items and show evidence. This combination of structure and proof is especially helpful if you’re rebuilding trust after past disappointments.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "An AEO checklist turns vague SEO work into clear, testable tasks: question-focused headings, schema markup, technical checks, and performance tracking. You can verify each item yourself, demand evidence from vendors, and tie changes directly to snippet and question-traffic improvements."
