              "text": "An answer engine optimization checklist can significantly improve voice search performance because many voice responses pull from concise, well-structured answers.\n\nVoice assistants prefer conversational, direct explanations with clear context, which aligns closely with AEO best practices. Optimizing one usually boosts the other.\n\nKey factors:\n- Use natural, spoken-style phrasing in questions and answers\n- Keep key responses in the 40–60 word range where possible\n- Implement Speakable or FAQ schema on appropriate pages\n- Ensure fast, mobile-friendly pages that load quickly for voice queries\n\nAdd a “voice readiness” subsection to your checklist that covers wording, length, schema, and performance. Over time, this makes your content more likely to be read aloud by assistants for local and informational queries in cities like San Jose or Dallas-Fort Worth.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Yes. AEO checklists emphasize concise, conversational answers, proper schema, and fast, mobile-friendly pages—all key for voice search. Adding a “voice readiness” section makes your content more likely to be read aloud by assistants for local and informational queries."
            }
          }
