            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "On a limited budget, you can still get meaningful GEO impact by focusing on question research, Q&A content, and a handful of high-impact schema types. You don’t need a full platform overhaul to become more visible in AI voice answers.\n\nThe key is ruthless prioritization: tackle the questions and pages closest to revenue first.\n\nKey factors:\n- Use customer conversations, support tickets, and internal search logs for real questions\n- Rewrite a small set of core pages into Q&A format\n- Implement only essential schema (Organization, LocalBusiness, FAQPage)\n- Avoid spreading effort across low-value or rarely asked topics\n\nPractically, allocate budget to a compact GEO sprint: 15–30 key questions, one strong FAQ hub, and schema applied to your top service/location pages. Reassess after 60–90 days based on AI voice testing.\n\nEven with modest resources, smart GEO choices can significantly improve how often assistants recommend your business.",
