              "text": "For a business in Austin, GEO for AI voice systems should prioritize how locals actually talk about neighborhoods, traffic, and timing when they ask for services. AI assistants lean on both structured data and natural language to answer those local questions.\n\nAustin users often mix “near me” queries with references to areas like South Congress, East Side, or Round Rock.\n\nKey factors:\n- Use LocalBusiness and FAQPage schema with Austin-specific service areas\n- Answer practical questions about timing, parking, and same-day options in Austin\n- Include common local phrasing and landmarks in your Q&A content\n- Keep your Google Business Profile and major listings tightly aligned\n\nPractically, collect the real voice-style questions you hear (“Who’s open late for X in Austin?”), answer them on your site, and mark those up. Then test the same questions with mobile voice assistants around Austin.\n\nTailored GEO makes AI voice responses feel naturally local, increasing your chances of being recommended to nearby customers.",
