            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For businesses in San Diego, GEO for AI voice systems should emphasize coastal geography, traffic patterns, and cross-border considerations that shape local questions. People often ask location-aware, timing-specific queries that AI assistants must resolve accurately.\n\nYour content needs to reflect how San Diego residents and visitors phrase those requests.\n\nKey factors:\n- Include San Diego neighborhoods, beaches, and landmarks in Q&A content\n- Answer practical questions about parking, rush-hour timing, and proximity\n- Use LocalBusiness and FAQPage schema with clear service areas\n- Keep information current for seasonal demand and event-related spikes\n\nPractically, collect common voice queries from customers (“What’s the closest X to Mission Beach open now?”) and answer them on structured pages. Test those queries via mobile voice search around San Diego.\n\nWell-localized GEO helps AI voice systems give precise, context-aware recommendations along the coast and across the broader metro area.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "In San Diego, GEO should reflect coastal and neighborhood-specific questions. Use LocalBusiness and FAQPage schema, answer practical queries about proximity, parking, and timing at local landmarks, and keep seasonal info current so AI voice assistants deliver accurate, city-aware recommendations."
