      "item": {
        "url": "aeoptimizer.com/faq/is-geo-strategy-really-different-from-seo-or-is-it-just-a-new-buzzword-for-the-s",
        "name": "Is GEO strategy really different from SEO, or is it just a new buzzword for the same thing?",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "speakable": {
          "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
          "cssSelector": [
            "h1",
            ".faq-question",
            ".faq-answer",
            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Is GEO strategy really different from SEO, or is it just a new buzzword for the same thing?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "GEO (Generative Engine Optimization) focuses on being *cited* in AI‑generated answers, while SEO focuses on *ranking* in traditional search results. A good GEO strategy complements SEO by turning your existing ranking pages into reliable sources that AI engines prefer to quote.\n\nMost businesses shouldn’t treat GEO as a replacement for SEO but as a layer that sits on top of it. SEO gets you discovered and crawled; GEO increases the likelihood that generative engines mention you when summarizing answers.\n\nKey factors:\n- SEO: clicks from search results; GEO: citations in AI answers\n- SEO signals: technical health, backlinks, keywords\n- GEO signals: clear Q&A content, structured data, brand authority\n- Overlap: strong content and trust signals help both\n\nIn practice, keep investing in SEO fundamentals, then adapt your content format (FAQs, how‑tos, comparison pages) so AI engines can pull concise, trustworthy snippets. For teams in Denver or Salt Lake City, think of GEO as optimizing your existing SEO wins for the new generation of search.\n\nIf you already have solid SEO, GEO strategy is often a relatively low‑effort, high‑impact evolution rather than a total rebuild.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "GEO strategy is different from SEO: SEO aims for high rankings in traditional search, while GEO aims for your content to be cited in AI‑generated answers. They overlap in fundamentals, but GEO focuses more on answer‑ready content, Q&A formats, and brand authority in generative engines."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "GEO strategy is different from SEO: SEO aims for high rankings in traditional search, while GEO aims for your content to be cited in AI‑generated answers. They"
      }
    },
    {
