            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "In local markets like Los Angeles or San Diego, GEO strategy matters most for discovery and recommendation queries such as “best,” “top,” or “near me.” You want AI engines to recognize your business as a relevant, trusted option for those city‑specific prompts.\n\nLocal GEO blends traditional local SEO with AI‑focused content formats that highlight your regional expertise and credibility. It’s about winning the generative version of word‑of‑mouth.\n\nKey factors:\n- Accurate, consistent business information (NAP data)\n- Local reviews and third‑party mentions\n- Content that references neighborhoods, landmarks, events\n- Local FAQs that AI can quote directly\n\nPractically, make sure your local profiles are correct, encourage detailed reviews, and publish Q&A content that answers the questions people ask about your services in that city. Use examples, case stories, and data tied to Los Angeles, San Diego, Denver, or Austin as appropriate.\n\nIf you rely heavily on local customers, treating GEO as “AI‑native local marketing” will help clarify your priorities.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "For local markets, GEO strategy focuses on being cited in AI answers to city‑specific queries like “best” and “near me.” You need accurate local listings, strong reviews, and Q&A content that references local neighborhoods, events, and problems so generative engines recognize you as a trusted local option."
