        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What should I do if AI answers keep getting details about my brand wrong, even after we update our site?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If generative AI tools misrepresent your brand—wrong prices, outdated services, or incorrect facts—you need a structured response plan: verify the issue, update source content, and strengthen authoritative signals where AI seems to be pulling data. In some cases, you can also use feedback mechanisms within the tools.\n\nGEO strategy isn’t just about more visibility; it’s also about protecting accuracy and trust. Fast correction reduces the risk of repeated misinformation.\n\nKey factors:\n- Where the incorrect information originates (your site vs. third‑party)\n- How often the error appears and on which prompts\n- Ability to update or correct external sources\n- Internal monitoring and escalation process\n\nPractically, assign ownership for AI reputation monitoring, keep a log of misrepresentations, and prioritize fixing the sources AI relies on. In larger markets like New York or Los Angeles, this may require coordinating with partners, directories, or review platforms.\n\nIf your brand is regularly misquoted, GEO work should start with cleaning up and clarifying data, not just adding new content.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Identify where AI is pulling the wrong data, correct those source pages or third‑party profiles, and strengthen clear, authoritative content that states the accurate information. Add ongoing monitoring and use available feedback tools so misrepresentations are caught and fixed quickly."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Identify where AI is pulling the wrong data, correct those source pages or third‑party profiles, and strengthen clear, authoritative content that states the acc"
      }
    },
