        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What does “AI‑friendly” content actually look like for GEO, and how do I write it?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "AI‑aware content should answer the main question directly in the first paragraph, then expand with clear, well‑labeled sections that cover the “what, why, and how.” Q&A blocks, lists, and concise summaries tend to perform well for GEO.\n\nGenerative engines favor content that is both readable for humans and easy to parse programmatically. Ambiguous, meandering text is harder to cite confidently.\n\nKey factors:\n- Direct, conversational answers up front\n- One primary topic per paragraph or section\n- Q&A and FAQ formats embedded in the page\n- Regular updates for evergreen and “best/top” content\n\nPractically, edit your pages so the key answer is obvious in the opening, then use headings and bullets to structure the rest. For businesses in Austin or Denver, add relevant examples from your region to make your expertise concrete.\n\nIf your current content is dense and academic, consider creating parallel “answer capsules” that generative engines can quote more easily.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "AI‑friendly content gives a clear, direct answer in the first paragraph, uses simple headings and Q&A blocks, and sticks to one main topic per section. Adding structured FAQs, lists, and regularly updated “best/top” guides makes it easier for generative engines to understand and cite your pages."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "AI‑friendly content gives a clear, direct answer in the first paragraph, uses simple headings and Q&A blocks, and sticks to one main topic per section. Adding s"
      }
