        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What exactly are GEO best practices and why do they matter for my website?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "GEO best practices are the guidelines for structuring and writing content so generative engines (like ChatGPT, Gemini, and Perplexity) can easily understand, summarize, and cite your site. In practice, that means answer‑first content, clear structure, and robust schema markup.\n\nGEO has emerged because AI assistants don’t just index keywords; they try to understand entities, relationships, and answers. To show up in these answers, you need to be both technically accessible and semantically clear.\n\nKey factors:\n- Lead each section with a concise, direct answer before deeper context.\n- Use headings, bullets, tables, and short paragraphs to make extraction easy.\n- Implement core schema types (Organization, Article, FAQ, HowTo).\n- Keep content updated, accurate, and clearly attributed to real experts.\n\nPractically, start by auditing 10–20 of your highest‑value pages and rewriting them in an answer‑first, FAQ‑rich format with schema. Then test those pages in AI tools to see whether they get cited and refine based on what shows up.\n\nDone well, GEO best practices help you become the “default” answer source for key questions in your niche.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "GEO best practices are guidelines for structuring and writing content so generative engines can easily understand, summarize, and cite your site. They matter because AI assistants increasingly drive discovery, and GEO helps your pages become the trusted answers they use and recommend."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "GEO best practices are guidelines for structuring and writing content so generative engines can easily understand, summarize, and cite your site. They matter be"
      }
