            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If you’re in Austin or Denver and competing nationally, GEO best practices can help you punch above your weight by establishing topic authority, not just local relevance. AI engines care more about expertise and clarity than company size.\n\nYou do this by owning a specific niche and becoming the most structured, helpful source on that niche.\n\nKey factors:\n- Choose a narrow set of topics where you can be truly best‑in‑class.\n- Build deep, answer‑first guides, FAQs, and comparison content around them.\n- Use consistent schema, author profiles, and references across all related pages.\n- Reinforce authority with case studies, data, and third‑party mentions.\n\nPractically, define your “topic clusters” and create a structured knowledge hub for each, then test national‑level prompts in AI tools to see if you’re cited alongside bigger brands. Adjust content until your pages are the easiest for AI to use.\n\nOver time, this focused GEO strategy lets mid‑market firms earn national visibility in their lane.",
