        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What can go wrong with GEO best practices—are there any real risks I should watch out for?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Risks from GEO usually come from over‑optimization and low‑quality AI‑generated content, not from the core best practices themselves. If you focus on clarity, usefulness, and transparent sourcing, GEO is low‑risk and often beneficial.\n\nProblems arise when teams chase shortcuts or mislead engines about expertise.\n\nKey factors:\n- Avoid publishing generic, lightly edited AI text at scale—it can hurt trust signals.\n- Don’t stuff pages with repetitive Q&A blocks purely for keywords.\n- Make sure author bios, credentials, and sources are real and verifiable.\n- Keep technical setup clean; don’t hide important content behind complex scripts.\n\nApproach GEO as a way to better serve users’ questions, not to trick algorithms. When in doubt, prioritize human readability and honest representation of your capabilities.\n\nThis mindset keeps GEO aligned with both platform policies and long‑term brand credibility.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "GEO problems mostly come from over‑optimization and low‑quality AI‑generated content, not from answer‑first or schema best practices themselves. Avoid thin, generic AI text, keyword‑stuffed FAQs, and misleading authority claims, and keep your technical setup clean and transparent."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "GEO problems mostly come from over‑optimization and low‑quality AI‑generated content, not from answer‑first or schema best practices themselves. Avoid thin, gen"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 1179,
      "item": {
        "url": "aeoptimizer.com/faq/what-should-i-do-if-ai-tools-never-seem-to-cite-my-site-even-after-basic-geo-wor",
        "name": "What should I do if AI tools never seem to cite my site, even after basic GEO work?",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "speakable": {
          "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
          "cssSelector": [
            "h1",
            ".faq-question",
            ".faq-answer",
            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What should I do if AI tools never seem to cite my site, even after basic GEO work?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If generative engines aren’t citing you yet, treat it as feedback that your content isn’t the easiest or most trusted answer source—yet. You can systematically close that gap with audits, re‑structuring, and schema.\n\nAbsence today doesn’t mean you’re locked out; it just means you have work to do.\n\nKey factors:\n- Compare top AI answers on your topics with your pages: structure, depth, and clarity.\n- Identify missing formats (FAQs, how‑tos, comparisons) where competitors excel.\n- Strengthen entity signals: Organization schema, author bios, and external references.\n- Refresh outdated content and fill holes where common follow‑up questions aren’t answered.\n\nBuild a shortlist of 10–15 prompts where you want visibility and optimize related pages aggressively for GEO. Re‑test every few weeks to track progress.\n\nOver time, methodical improvements often turn “not cited at all” into regular appearances in answer snippets.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "If you’re not getting cited, study the pages that do appear for your key prompts and upgrade your content to match or exceed their structure, depth, and clarity. Add FAQs, how‑tos, schema, stronger author signals, and fresher data, then retest regularly to see if citations improve."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "If you’re not getting cited, study the pages that do appear for your key prompts and upgrade your content to match or exceed their structure, depth, and clarity"
      }
    },
    {
