        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How should GEO best practices look for a complex B2B SaaS product rather than simple local services?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For B2B SaaS and complex products, GEO best practices emphasize structured education: definitions, how‑tos, comparisons, and FAQs that build a coherent knowledge base. Generative engines need clarity to explain your offering to non‑experts.\n\nYour goal is to become the primary explainer of your own product category.\n\nKey factors:\n- Define key concepts and features in plain language, then add technical depth.\n- Create step‑by‑step how‑to guides with HowTo schema for common workflows.\n- Publish comparison pages that fairly and clearly outline trade‑offs.\n- Connect content with internal links and breadcrumb schema so AI sees relationships.\n\nTreat every major feature or problem you solve as a question in your content, and write answer‑first sections that map directly to how users prompt AI tools. Over time, this makes AI assistants more likely to recommend your product or positioning.\n\nIt’s a way to scale presales education beyond your website alone.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "For complex B2B SaaS, GEO should center on structured education: clear definitions, step‑by‑step how‑tos, honest comparisons, and rich FAQs tied together with schema and internal links. This helps generative engines explain your product accurately and cite your site as the go‑to source."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "For complex B2B SaaS, GEO should center on structured education: clear definitions, step‑by‑step how‑tos, honest comparisons, and rich FAQs tied together with s"
      }
    },
