        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "We’re in a tech‑heavy city like Seattle or San Francisco—how can GEO best practices help us stand out in AI answers?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "In fast‑moving tech hubs like San Francisco or Seattle, GEO best practices should highlight genuine thought leadership, not just features. Generative engines prefer unique, expert perspectives over commodity content.\n\nIf you shape the conversation in your niche, AI tools will treat you as a reference point.\n\nKey factors:\n- Publish opinionated, well‑reasoned articles that go beyond basic how‑tos.\n- Support claims with data, case studies, and transparent citations.\n- Showcase expert authors with detailed bios and Person schema.\n- Refresh content with new trends, frameworks, and lessons at least yearly.\n\nBuild a cadence of answer‑first insight pieces and tie them to core product or service topics, then test whether AI summaries quote your frameworks or language.\n\nThis approach helps you stand out in cities where many players are competing for the same generative mindshare.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "In tech hubs, use GEO to showcase real thought leadership: publish answer‑first, expert articles with data, case studies, and strong author signals, then keep them updated. Generative engines favor unique, authoritative perspectives, so this helps your brand get cited over generic competitors."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "In tech hubs, use GEO to showcase real thought leadership: publish answer‑first, expert articles with data, case studies, and strong author signals, then keep t"
      }
