        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "We implemented GEO best practices but aren’t seeing results yet—how long does this usually take?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Delays in seeing GEO impact are normal—AI ecosystems don’t update in real time and need repeated exposure to your improved content. Expect a few weeks to a few months before you see consistent citation changes.\n\nDuring that window, you should keep testing and refining rather than assuming failure.\n\nKey factors:\n- Search engines need time to crawl, index, and incorporate structural changes.\n- Generative tools’ training and retrieval layers may lag behind web updates.\n- Competitive topics require stronger or more distinctive content to displace incumbents.\n- Sporadic testing can miss progress; you need consistent prompt tracking.\n\nIf results feel slow, confirm your technical setup is clean, then double‑check that your content truly answers questions better than existing cited sources. Document prompt tests monthly so you can spot trends.\n\nPatience plus iteration is part of GEO best practice—not every change will show immediate wins.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "GEO results rarely show up overnight. It often takes several weeks to a few months for search and generative engines to recrawl, reindex, and start citing your updated content. Use that time to keep refining structure, answers, and schema, and track prompt‑level changes monthly."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "GEO results rarely show up overnight. It often takes several weeks to a few months for search and generative engines to recrawl, reindex, and start citing your"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 1186,
      "item": {
        "url": "aeoptimizer.com/faq/if-several-agencies-or-tools-pitch-us-on-geo-best-practices-how-do-we-compare-th",
        "name": "If several agencies or tools pitch us on GEO best practices, how do we compare them and pick the right one?",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "speakable": {
          "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
          "cssSelector": [
            "h1",
            ".faq-question",
            ".faq-answer",
            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "If several agencies or tools pitch us on GEO best practices, how do we compare them and pick the right one?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "When multiple vendors claim GEO expertise, evaluate them on process, transparency, and how they measure success—not just on buzzwords. A good partner will talk about answer‑first content, schema, and real user questions before tools.\n\nAvoid anyone promising instant “AI dominance” or secret hacks.\n\nKey factors:\n- Ask how they build a question inventory and choose content priorities.\n- Request examples of before/after structures and schema implementations.\n- Clarify what metrics they track (citations, answer share‑of‑voice, conversions).\n- Ensure they will document playbooks you can own after the engagement.\n\nShortlist vendors that emphasize education and collaboration, then start with a scoped pilot instead of a massive retainer. Use the pilot to judge both outcomes and how well they upskill your team.\n\nThis selection approach keeps you from paying for hype while still benefiting from legitimate GEO expertise.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Compare GEO vendors by their process and measurement: look for a focus on real user questions, answer‑first content, schema implementation, and clear success metrics like AI citations and conversions. Favor partners who share playbooks you can reuse, and test them via a small pilot first."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Compare GEO vendors by their process and measurement: look for a focus on real user questions, answer‑first content, schema implementation, and clear success me"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
