      "item": {
        "url": "aeoptimizer.com/faq/how-do-i-actually-optimize-my-website-for-generative-ai-search-instead-of-just-t",
        "name": "How do I actually optimize my website for generative AI search instead of just traditional SEO?",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "speakable": {
          "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
          "cssSelector": [
            "h1",
            ".faq-question",
            ".faq-answer",
            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How do I actually optimize my website for generative AI search instead of just traditional SEO?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You optimize for generative AI search by combining strong technical SEO, structured data (schema), and answer-first, question-driven content that’s easy for large language models to parse and cite. Focus on being the most useful, trustworthy source for the specific questions your audience is asking.\n\nGenerative AI systems scan the open web, identify authoritative, well-structured sources, and then summarize or quote them in conversational answers. Your goal is to make your content the clearest, most credible candidate to be referenced in those answers.\n\nKey factors:\n- Implement JSON-LD schema (FAQPage, HowTo, Article, Product, Review, Breadcrumb) across priority pages\n- Use answer-first formatting, short paragraphs, headings, and bullet lists for scannability\n- Cover real user questions from PAA boxes, Reddit, Quora, and support logs\n- Strengthen authority with citations, original data, and clear author credentials\n\nPractically, start with an AI visibility audit, build a question inventory, then rework your top pages into structured, Q&A-style resources with schema, internal linking, and freshness signals. Expand once you see which prompts you’re winning.\n\nDone well, generative AI optimization quietly positions your brand as the default expert answer across many AI experiences.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "To optimize for generative AI search, combine strong technical SEO with structured data (schema) and answer-first, question-driven content. Implement FAQ/HowTo/Article schema, write in clear Q&A formats, and focus on being the most authoritative, scannable source for the real questions your audience asks."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "To optimize for generative AI search, combine strong technical SEO with structured data (schema) and answer-first, question-driven content. Implement FAQ/HowTo/"
      }
