        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "If my site is already optimized for SEO, what’s the first thing I should do differently for generative AI search?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Start by mapping the real questions your audience asks and restructuring existing pages into answer-first Q&A formats backed by schema markup. You don’t need to rebuild your whole site—focus on high-impact pages and topics first.\n\nMost sites already have valuable content; the issue is structure and signals, not starting completely over. Generative engines favor pages that clearly map to user prompts and are easy to parse technically.\n\nKey factors:\n- Audit your top 20–50 pages by traffic and conversions\n- Rewrite intros to answer the main question in 1–2 sentences\n- Add FAQ sections with individual questions and concise answers\n- Layer in JSON-LD schema (FAQPage, HowTo, Article) and tighten internal links\n\nPractically, run your key pages through an AI tool and ask it to answer core questions using only that URL—if it struggles or mis-summarizes, reformat for clarity. Treat this as an iterative retrofit, not a full rebuild.\n\nThis approach lets you modernize for generative search while preserving the SEO equity you already have.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Don’t rebuild your site. Start by auditing top pages and converting them to answer-first, Q&A-style content with FAQ/HowTo/Article schema. Make each page clearly answer specific user questions and be easy for AI systems to parse, cite, and summarize."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Don’t rebuild your site. Start by auditing top pages and converting them to answer-first, Q&A-style content with FAQ/HowTo/Article schema. Make each page clearl"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 1189,
      "item": {
        "url": "aeoptimizer.com/faq/what-s-the-real-difference-between-traditional-seo-and-generative-ai-search-opti",
        "name": "What’s the real difference between traditional SEO and generative AI search optimization?",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "speakable": {
          "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
          "cssSelector": [
            "h1",
            ".faq-question",
            ".faq-answer",
            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What’s the real difference between traditional SEO and generative AI search optimization?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Generative search still relies on classic SEO foundations, but it adds a stronger emphasis on question-driven content, structured data, and citation-worthiness. Think of SEO as getting discovered, and generative AI optimization as getting *quoted* in answers.\n\nSearch engines use generative systems to compose overviews, but those systems still pull from indexed, crawlable pages with strong technical hygiene. The difference is how content is selected and synthesized.\n\nKey factors:\n- SEO focuses on ranking pages; generative AI focuses on selecting passages to cite\n- Keyword lists give way to natural-language questions and conversational prompts\n- Schema and content structure become critical for machine comprehension\n- Authority is judged more on breadth, coherence, and external mentions\n\nPractically, keep investing in technical SEO, speed, and backlinks, but layer on question mapping, Q&A sections, and schema across core topics. Aim to be the best source for the specific prompt, not just the broad keyword.\n\nDone right, SEO and generative optimization reinforce each other rather than compete.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Traditional SEO focuses on ranking whole pages for keywords, while generative AI optimization focuses on making your content the best source to be quoted in AI answers. You still need strong SEO, but you add question-driven content, schema, and answer-first formatting so AI systems can easily cite you."
            }
          }
        ],
