        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How do I know if my generative AI search optimization efforts are actually working?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "To measure success, track both direct traffic/conversion metrics and how often your content is cited or surfaced in AI experiences. While you can’t see everything, you can piece together a picture from search tools, analytics, and controlled tests.\n\nGenerative AI visibility is partly opaque, but certain indicators reliably show progress over time.\n\nKey factors:\n- Changes in organic traffic and engagement to optimized pages\n- Appearance in AI overviews or assistant answers when you query your core topics\n- Increases in branded and question-based searches that match your content\n- Growth in external mentions, links, and social shares of your resources\n\nPractically, document a baseline before changes, then run consistent monthly check-ins using the same test prompts and dashboards. Watch for both qualitative improvements (better answers) and quantitative ones.\n\nThink of measurement as a mosaic: no single metric is perfect, but together they show whether your optimization is working.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Measure generative AI optimization by tracking organic traffic and engagement on optimized pages, testing whether your content appears or is cited in AI answers, monitoring question-based search trends, and watching for more external mentions and links. Use baselines and monthly check-ins to see progress over time."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Measure generative AI optimization by tracking organic traffic and engagement on optimized pages, testing whether your content appears or is cited in AI answers"
      }
    },
