            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "The practical process is: audit current AI answers, compare cited pages to yours, then systematically update your content and structure to match AI-friendly patterns.\n\nYou’re not guessing; you’re reverse-engineering what AI tools already reward and aligning your site with those patterns while adding your unique expertise.\n\nKey factors:\n- Step 1: Pick 20–30 real buyer questions and run them in multiple AI assistants.\n- Step 2: Catalog who gets cited, what page types they use, and how content is structured.\n- Step 3: Identify gaps in your pages (missing entities, weak structure, no schema, little data).\n- Step 4: Update, publish, request indexing, then re-check AI answers after a few weeks.\n\nTreat this like a recurring workflow: monthly or quarterly, repeat the audit, expand your coverage, and refine structures.\nOver time, this process builds both AI citations and traditional search visibility, because both reward clear, authoritative answers.",
