        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "If I manage to get cited by AI, what realistic outcomes should I expect beyond a vanity mention of my brand name?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Realistic outcomes include more brand visibility in AI answers, some referral traffic, and stronger perceived authority for users who research via assistants—but it’s not a guaranteed traffic surge.\n\nAI often summarizes without links, and even when you’re cited, users may not always click through, especially for simple questions.\n\nKey factors:\n- You gain repeated exposure when your brand appears across many related queries.\n- High-intent, comparison, and “how to choose” questions are most likely to drive clicks.\n- Citations can support sales and trust even if they don’t show up clearly in standard analytics.\n- Over time, authority from AI citations can align with better traditional search performance.\n\nMeasure outcomes by tracking branded search, direct traffic, and known referral paths from AI tools alongside manual spot-checks.\nTreat citations as part of a broader authority strategy, not a standalone channel that replaces SEO or content marketing.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Expect increased brand visibility in AI answers, some referral traffic on high-intent queries, and a stronger perception of authority, not a guaranteed traffic spike. AI citations work best as part of an overall authority strategy that also supports search, sales, and trust-building."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Expect increased brand visibility in AI answers, some referral traffic on high-intent queries, and a stronger perception of authority, not a guaranteed traffic"
      }
