          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How is optimizing for AI citations different from regular SEO, and do I have to choose between them?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "AI citation optimization overlaps heavily with SEO, but they’re not identical; you’re optimizing for both search engines and answer engines at the same time.\n\nTraditional SEO focuses on rankings and snippets, while AI citation work focuses on answer structure, entity clarity, and being a safe summarizable source.\n\nKey factors:\n- SEO emphasizes keywords, links, and on-page signals; AI adds entity, schema, and extractable blocks.\n- Featured snippets pull exact text; AI overviews paraphrase multiple sources.\n- AI answers care about clear question/answer mapping and structured comparisons.\n- Both reward trustworthy, well-maintained, user-first content.\n\nWhen you update pages, ask whether they serve both a human searching Google and an AI assistant synthesizing multiple sources.\nThe best investments—clarity, structure, evidence, freshness—pay off in both worlds.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Optimizing for AI citations is an extension of SEO, not a replacement. SEO focuses on rankings and snippets; AI citation work adds entity clarity, schema, and extractable Q&A and comparison blocks. You should design pages to serve both search engines and answer engines simultaneously."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Optimizing for AI citations is an extension of SEO, not a replacement. SEO focuses on rankings and snippets; AI citation work adds entity clarity, schema, and e"
      }
    },
