            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For a limited budget, focus on high-impact structural and content changes rather than expensive tools or large-scale rewriting.\n\nMany of the most important AI citation signals—clarity, answer-first structure, schema basics, and topical focus—can be implemented manually with existing resources.\n\nKey factors:\n- Prioritize your top 10–15 buyer questions and their corresponding pages.\n- Fix headings, intros, and FAQs so answers are obvious and extractable.\n- Add simple schema (FAQ, HowTo, Organization, Article) via plugins or generators.\n- Skip heavy redesigns until you’ve validated that citations are moving the needle.\n\nTrack a small set of queries across AI assistants so you can see incremental progress without overspending.\nOnce you’ve proven value, you can gradually invest in more sophisticated tooling or expert support.",
