            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If AI keeps citing your competitors, you need to study their cited pages and adjust your content and positioning, not just add more keywords.\n\nAI tools are signaling that those competitors’ pages are easier to summarize, more authoritative, or more comprehensive for the specific questions being asked.\n\nKey factors:\n- Analyze cited competitor pages: structure, headings, data, comparisons, and tone.\n- Check whether they cover more entities, options, or scenarios than you do.\n- Identify gaps in your own content: missing tables, unclear answers, few examples.\n- Ensure your brand signals (bios, reviews, third-party mentions) aren’t weaker.\n\nThen build or upgrade pages that are objectively more useful than competitor pages for those queries.\nYou’re aiming to be the “best training data” in the category, not merely another similar source.",
