            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "When you’re under time pressure, prioritize a small set of high-value queries and a minimal, AI-friendly structure, rather than reworking your whole site.\n\nYou can make a few pages much more “cit-able” in days by clarifying answers and adding basic schema, then expand later as you see results.\n\nKey factors:\n- Pick 5–10 urgent queries where AI citations would support immediate campaigns.\n- Rewrite intros to give a direct answer, followed by a short explanation.\n- Add FAQ sections with real follow-up questions buyers are asking right now.\n- Implement simple FAQ and Organization schema on those pages first.\n\nOnce these quick wins are in place, run AI queries weekly to watch for citation changes.\nLater, you can deepen and scale the approach when the urgent window has passed.",
