            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You get mentioned in ChatGPT by publishing highly specific, answer-first content on your site, earning citations from trusted third‑party sites, and making your pages easy for AI and search crawlers to understand.\nChatGPT pulls from sources it already trusts, so you need both strong on‑site content and off‑site signals.\n\n**Key factors**\n- Clear, 2–3 sentence answers at the top of key pages.\n- FAQ and HowTo style content that mirrors real questions.\n- Clean technical setup: crawlable HTML, correct schema, fast site.\n- Mentions and links from reputable sites, directories, and reviews.\n\nStart by listing 15–20 real buyer questions, then create one best‑on‑the‑internet answer page for each and support it with citations from other sites and profiles.\nReview ChatGPT answers to those questions monthly and refine your content based on which sources it cites.\nPosition this as an ongoing \"visibility program,\" not a one‑time SEO trick.",
