            "name": "How do I get my SaaS mentioned in ChatGPT answers alongside big platforms instead of being ignored as an alternative?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "ChatGPT often leans on \"anchor\" brands—well‑known tools or platforms—so getting mentioned next to them means positioning yourself clearly in the same ecosystem.\nYou need both integration‑style content and third‑party comparisons.\n\n**Key factors**\n- Pages that explain how you integrate or compare with major tools.\n- Clear, structured \"[YourTool] vs [BigBrand]\" comparison content.\n- Mentions in independent review sites and roundups.\n- Consistent naming and category tags across your profiles.\n\nPublish decision‑ready comparison pages that outline use cases, pros/cons, and when to choose you versus the big brand.\nThen pursue inclusion in listicles, review platforms, and community threads that discuss alternatives.\nThis makes it easier for ChatGPT to surface you when people ask for options, not just default to the largest player.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Create clear \"[YourSaaS] vs [BigPlatform]\" and integration pages, with honest pros/cons and use cases. Then earn mentions in independent reviews and listicles. When people ask ChatGPT for alternatives or comparisons, those structured signals make it likelier your product appears beside anchor brands."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Create clear \"[YourSaaS] vs [BigPlatform]\" and integration pages, with honest pros/cons and use cases. Then earn mentions in independent reviews and listicles."
      }
