            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If results feel delayed or inconsistent, treat ChatGPT like any other external platform: you can influence inputs but not control outputs.\nFocus on what you can measure and improve.\n\n**Key factors**\n- Variability in models, versions, and data refresh cycles.\n- Different behavior across prompts and phrasings.\n- Slow feedback loops from content changes to mentions.\n- Lack of official reporting or APIs for citations.\n\nCreate a prompt testing log—same 15–20 questions, run monthly—and track whether your brand appears, how often, and in what context.\nUse changes in web rankings, backlinks, and reviews as leading indicators that may precede AI visibility.\nAnchor expectations around gradual, compounding improvements rather than fixed timelines.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Expect variability and delays. Different model versions and refresh cycles mean mentions can appear slowly and change over time. Use a fixed prompt set you test monthly, track your appearances, and keep improving web rankings, content depth, and citations as leading indicators."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Expect variability and delays. Different model versions and refresh cycles mean mentions can appear slowly and change over time. Use a fixed prompt set you test"
      }
