            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "There’s no direct fee to rank in AI Overviews, but you’ll likely invest in content, technical SEO, and authority building. For most small–mid businesses, that means a few thousand dollars over several months, whether in‑house or via external help.\n\nCosts vary widely based on how much content you need, your current rankings, and whether you hire specialists or do it yourself. The “price” is essentially the SEO and content work needed to become the best answer.\n\nKey factors:\n- Content creation (research, writing, editing)\n- Technical and schema implementation\n- Link building / digital PR for authority\n- Analytics and ongoing optimization\n\nStart by prioritizing 10–20 queries with real business value and invest in those first, instead of trying to cover everything. Track revenue and leads from queries where you earn AI Overviews citations to understand ROI.\n\nThinking in “campaigns per topic” helps you budget more intelligently than chasing AI Overviews in the abstract.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "You don’t pay Google to rank in AI Overviews, but you’ll invest in content, technical SEO, and authority building—often several thousand dollars over a few months. It’s worth it when you focus on high‑value queries and can tie AI Overview visibility to measurable leads or revenue."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "You don’t pay Google to rank in AI Overviews, but you’ll invest in content, technical SEO, and authority building—often several thousand dollars over a few mont"
      }
