            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "On a limited budget, focus your AI Overview efforts on a small set of high‑value, question‑style queries and make those pages exceptional. It’s better to deeply optimize 5–10 pages than lightly touch 100.\n\nSince AI Overviews rely on organic rankings, your investment should prioritize content quality for your most profitable topics and basic technical health over fancy tools.\n\nKey factors:\n- Pick queries closely tied to revenue or qualified leads\n- Do manual research via People Also Ask and forums\n- Use simple, valid schema (FAQPage, HowTo, Article)\n- Keep page speed and mobile experience solid\n\nStart with one flagship guide per topic, structured with clear questions and 2–3 sentence answers, and support each with a few shorter FAQ posts. Revisit these pages monthly to refine based on performance.\n\nA focused, budget‑conscious approach can still earn AI Overview citations if your answers are demonstrably better than everyone else’s.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Pick 5–10 high‑value question‑style queries, then heavily optimize those pages with clear Q&A structure, concise answers, simple schema, and solid technical performance. Deeply focusing on a few money‑making topics beats spreading a small budget across your entire site."
