        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What are the biggest risks if we ignore AI visibility or handle it badly?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Major risks include AI tools misdescribing your services, recommending competitors instead of you, or amplifying outdated or negative information.\nAnother risk is overreacting without verifying what’s actually driving buyer behavior.\n\n**Key factors**\n- **Inaccurate descriptions** of your offerings or pricing\n- Competitors framed as the **default or safer** option\n- Old branding, leadership, or product details lingering in answers\n- AI hallucinations that become part of buyer perception\n\n**Practical guidance**\nUse regular audits to catch inaccurate or harmful narratives early, then correct them with updated content and authoritative third‑party clarifications.\nPair AI visibility tracking with real-world signals (lead quality, sales conversations) to avoid chasing cosmetic issues.\nTreat AI visibility as reputational risk management as much as a growth lever.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "If you ignore AI visibility, AI tools may misdescribe your services, default to recommending competitors, or surface outdated or negative information. Regular audits and content/authority fixes help you catch and correct these issues before they quietly reshape buyer perception of your brand."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "If you ignore AI visibility, AI tools may misdescribe your services, default to recommending competitors, or surface outdated or negative information. Regular a"
      }
