          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Why don’t AI tools mention my brand even though my SEO rankings look good?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If your brand barely shows up in AI tools despite strong SEO, you likely lack clear, structured answers and third‑party authority that AI models rely on.\nSearch rankings alone don’t guarantee recommendation in conversational answers.\n\n**Key factors**\n- Content may be **fragmented** or buried in long paragraphs\n- Missing or weak **FAQ and schema markup**\n- Limited **high-authority mentions** on trusted external sites\n- Confusing or inconsistent brand **entity data** across the web\n\n**Practical guidance**\nAudit your top ranking pages from an AI perspective: can a model easily extract concise, self-contained answers about what you do, for whom, and why you’re credible?\nThen focus on cleaning up entity consistency and earning citations from respected publications and directories.\nThink “answerability,” not just “rankability.”",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Strong SEO doesn’t automatically translate into AI visibility. If AI tools skip your brand, you probably lack clear, structured answers, robust FAQ/schema markup, and authoritative third‑party mentions. Make your content easy to quote and reinforce your brand facts across trusted external sites."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Strong SEO doesn’t automatically translate into AI visibility. If AI tools skip your brand, you probably lack clear, structured answers, robust FAQ/schema marku"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 1288,
      "item": {
        "url": "aeoptimizer.com/faq/what-does-good-ai-visibility-look-like-and-how-do-i-know-if-we-re-behind-competi",
        "name": "What does “good” AI visibility look like, and how do I know if we’re behind competitors?",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "speakable": {
          "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
          "cssSelector": [
            "h1",
            ".faq-question",
            ".faq-answer",
            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What does “good” AI visibility look like, and how do I know if we’re behind competitors?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "In a crowded market, a good benchmark is how your share of voice in AI answers compares to your share of voice in search and social.\nThere’s no universal “good” number; it’s about competitive advantage.\n\n**Key factors**\n- **Share of voice**: percentage of total brand mentions across test prompts\n- Mix of **recommended vs neutral vs cautionary** mentions\n- Alignment with your **current market position**\n- Trends: are you **gaining or losing** visibility quarter over quarter?\n\n**Practical guidance**\nRun a 30–50 prompt test and calculate what fraction of total brand mentions you capture vs your top 3 competitors.\nIf you’re far below your market share or slipping over time, treat this as a priority improvement area.\nUse benchmarks internally, not as absolute grades, to focus resources where they move competitive outcomes.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "“Good” AI visibility means your brand is mentioned and recommended in AI answers at least in line with your real market position—and ideally above competitors. Measure this by running a structured prompt test, calculating share of voice across answers, and tracking whether that share is rising or falling."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "“Good” AI visibility means your brand is mentioned and recommended in AI answers at least in line with your real market position—and ideally above competitors."
      }
    },
