            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Best practice is to monitor AI visibility at least quarterly, with light checks monthly if your market is fast-moving.\nYou want to catch shifts in recommendations before they impact pipeline.\n\n**Key factors**\n- **Quarterly audits** with full prompt sets and competitor analysis\n- **Monthly spot checks** on a handful of “money prompts”\n- Extra reviews after major **site changes or campaigns**\n- Ongoing log of answer changes and new competitors\n\n**Practical guidance**\nDefine a small set of high-value prompts and track them monthly, then run a broader 30–50 prompt audit every quarter.\nUse a consistent template so you can compare results over time.\nThink of AI visibility monitoring like performance analytics, not a one‑time project.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Most teams should run a full AI visibility audit quarterly and do quick spot checks on a few high‑value prompts monthly. This cadence lets you catch shifts in how AI tools recommend or describe your brand without turning monitoring into a daily burden."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Most teams should run a full AI visibility audit quarterly and do quick spot checks on a few high‑value prompts monthly. This cadence lets you catch shifts in h"
