        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What can we do if AI tools are stuck on old information about our brand or product?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If models use outdated or conflicting information, they may continue repeating old narratives until you systematically replace and reinforce correct data.\nYou have to treat this as a data clean‑up project, not just messaging.\n\n**Key factors**\n- Identify **all public sources** carrying the outdated info\n- Update or remove those entries wherever possible\n- Publish multiple **consistent, detailed explainers** of the correct facts\n- Use structured data and FAQs to highlight updated information\n\n**Practical guidance**\nCreate a checklist of sites (your own, major directories, social profiles, press releases, old blogs) and update them with consistent, current facts about your brand.\nBuild a central “About” or “What changed” page that explains key updates.\nOver time, AI tools favor the newer, more consistent data as their reference.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Systematically update every place where outdated information lives—your site, profiles, directories, old press releases—and replace it with consistent, current facts. Then emphasize the new details in structured content and FAQs so AI tools see and adopt the updated narrative over time."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Systematically update every place where outdated information lives—your site, profiles, directories, old press releases—and replace it with consistent, current"
      }
