        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What’s the fastest way to get started with AI visibility monitoring without overcomplicating it?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "To start AI visibility monitoring this week, focus on building a small but high-quality prompt set and running it across 2–3 major AI platforms. You don’t need perfect coverage to get useful insights quickly.\n\nAim to capture a baseline of where you show up, how accurately you’re described, and which competitors dominate missing spots.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Choose platforms: typically ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Google AI Overviews\n- Source prompts from search terms, customer emails, and sales questions\n- Cover branded, category, and “best X” comparison queries\n- Log visibility, citations, and accuracy in a simple spreadsheet\n\nBlock out a half-day to gather your top 50–100 questions, then run them in each AI and record who appears and what’s said. Tag prompts where you’re absent or misrepresented, and flag the cited URLs that outrank you. Use these findings to prioritize which pages or profiles to fix first. You can expand the prompt set and platforms later.\n\nFor teams under time pressure, a small, focused monitoring setup is far more valuable than trying to design a perfect system you never start.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Pick 2–3 major AI platforms, build a list of 50–100 real buyer questions, run them, and log whether you appear, how you’re described, and who else shows up. This quick baseline gives you enough data to identify immediate visibility gaps and content priorities."
            }
          }
