            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Even if you’re not ready to buy AI visibility software, you can still gather credible evidence to convince stakeholders using a lightweight monitoring pilot. Focus on a few critical prompts and show concrete gaps or improvements.\n\nStakeholders respond better to specific examples than abstract metrics alone.\n\n**Key factors:**\n- Choose 10–20 high-value prompts tied to revenue or strategic goals\n- Capture screenshots and logs of AI answers over several weeks\n- Highlight cases where competitors are recommended instead of you\n- Show any correlations between visibility changes and branded search or leads\n\nRun this pilot manually, then summarize findings in a short, visual report: examples of missing or incorrect answers, competitor dominance, and any early wins from content fixes. This evidence often makes the case for more systematic monitoring or tooling.\n\nTeams that start with a small, proof-oriented approach usually find it easier to win buy-in for broader AI visibility initiatives.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Run a small pilot with 10–20 critical prompts, log AI answers over a few weeks, and highlight where competitors are recommended or your brand is misrepresented. Pair those examples with related changes in branded search or leads to show practical, early evidence of value."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Run a small pilot with 10–20 critical prompts, log AI answers over a few weeks, and highlight where competitors are recommended or your brand is misrepresented."
      }
