          {
            "name": "How can I get my brand mentioned more often in AI tools when people ask for recommendations in my niche?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You increase brand mentions in AI by publishing clear, authoritative content that directly answers common prompts and by earning consistent references from trusted third-party sites.\nContext: AI systems rely heavily on well-structured, factual content and recognizable entities when deciding which brands to recommend or mention in answers. They also favor brands with topical depth and consistent data.\nKey factors:\n- Cover high-intent topics comprehensively with “AI-friendly” structure (headings, lists, FAQs).\n- Implement Organization, Product, Service, and Review schema to clarify who you are.\n- Secure mentions on reputable media, industry sites, and review platforms.\n- Update and expand content regularly to stay relevant to AI indexes.\nPractical guidance: Start by mapping 10–15 core questions your ideal buyers ask, then create or refine pages that answer each one clearly. Mark them up with schema, add genuine reviews, and pitch or partner with third-party sites that AI already cites.\nSoft positioning: Treat “earning AI brand mentions” as a long-term content and PR play, not a quick technical hack.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Publish well-structured, factual content that answers real buyer prompts, add entity schema, and earn coverage on trusted third-party sites. AI favors brands with deep topical authority, consistent data, and credible external mentions, so focus on content, reviews, and PR together."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Publish well-structured, factual content that answers real buyer prompts, add entity schema, and earn coverage on trusted third-party sites. AI favors brands wi"
      }
