            "name": "How do I measure whether my AI brand mention strategy is actually working over time?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Start by defining 5–10 high-intent prompts (e.g., “best SaaS for X in Austin”) and then use a simple spreadsheet to record AI answers across platforms each week.\nContext: Measuring AI brand mentions isn’t about impressions like ads; it’s about tracking when you appear, how you’re described, and whether that changes over time. You can do this manually or with specialized tracking tools.\nKey factors:\n- Use consistent prompts and test cadence (weekly or monthly).\n- Capture presence (Y/N), sentiment (positive/neutral/negative), and accuracy.\n- Note competing brands that appear instead of you.\n- Tie changes back to your content, PR, or product updates.\nPractical guidance: After each monitoring round, flag “wins” (new mentions, better descriptions) and “gaps” (no mention, inaccurate info) and assign clear follow-up actions, such as updating pages, collecting reviews, or clarifying messaging.\nSoft positioning: Treat AI mention measurement as an evolving KPI, alongside traffic and conversions, to inform your broader growth strategy.",
