            "name": "How long does it usually take to see more brand mentions in AI after I start optimizing content and PR?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "AI brand mentions can change quickly, but you’ll typically see noticeable shifts 4–12 weeks after consistent content, PR, and schema work.\nContext: AI systems update their underlying indexes at different speeds, and many rely on search engine recrawls and trusted sources. So timelines are less “instant ranking” and more “gradual visibility.”\nKey factors:\n- Search engines and AI platforms recrawl and retrain on variable schedules.\n- High-authority sites usually get reflected faster than brand-new domains.\n- Frequent content updates and new third-party coverage help accelerate changes.\n- Baseline monitoring for at least 2–4 weeks is key before judging impact.\nPractical guidance: Plan your AI visibility campaigns in quarterly cycles, tracking mention frequency and accuracy over that period rather than week-by-week. Set realistic expectations internally that AI mentions respond to sustained effort, not one-off tweaks.\nSoft positioning: Think of AI brand visibility as a compounding asset that builds over months, not days.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Expect early changes in AI brand mentions within 4–12 weeks of consistent content, schema, and PR work. Different AI platforms update at different speeds, so monitor prompts for at least 2–4 weeks to establish a baseline and assess impact over a full quarter."
            }
          }
        ],
