              "text": "To fix delayed or missing AI mention improvements, verify that your changes are crawlable, consistent, and reflected in authoritative third‑party sources.\nContext: Sometimes brands optimize pages or schema but forget that AI systems rely on the wider web; if directories, reviews, or major profiles remain outdated, AI may continue using old data.\nKey factors:\n- Ensure technical SEO is sound so changes can be discovered.\n- Align messaging across your site, profiles, and key partners.\n- Secure at least a few updated mentions on trusted external sites.\n- Give platforms time to recrawl and refresh their indexes.\nPractical guidance: If you see no change after a couple of months, re‑audit your top prompts and answers, then build an action list focused on external credibility—reviews, case studies, and thought‑leadership placements that AI is more likely to ingest.\nSoft positioning: Treat “stalled” results as a signal to broaden your footprint, not just tweak the same pages again.",
