            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If you’re in Los Angeles or San Diego, local factors matter mainly when people ask location-specific questions that LLMs answer with nearby sources.\n\nModels will prefer pages that clearly signal geography and have strong local authority. Generic content can win globally, but local content needs clear city or region cues.\n\nKey factors:\n- Use precise location references in relevant content (neighborhoods, counties)\n- Maintain strong local citations and reviews on trusted platforms\n- Ensure your site and profiles clearly state city and service area\n- Publish FAQs that match how local users describe their problems\n\nPractically, think about the questions people in LA or San Diego would ask differently than national users, and create dedicated pages that address those queries with local context and data.\n\nPositioning: For location-sensitive queries, LLM citations behave more like local search—clarity about place and real-world presence matters.",
