        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Do LLM citations actually help with conversions or are they just a visibility metric?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "LLM citations can help conversion by building trust and sending qualified users to your detailed content, but only if the cited pages answer their intent cleanly.\n\nUsers are more likely to click and stay on pages that feel like a natural extension of the AI answer, not a jarring marketing pitch.\n\nKey factors:\n- Match page content tightly to the question cited\n- Offer deeper context, examples, and next steps beyond the snippet\n- Keep design fast and readable, especially on mobile\n- Provide clear, relevant calls to action aligned with the user’s problem\n\nPractically, audit your most-cited pages and improve them for on-page clarity and conversion, assuming visitors arrive from an AI answer already primed with a specific question.\n\nPositioning: Treat LLM citations as intent-rich traffic—they’re a chance to continue a conversation the AI started and guide users to a helpful outcome.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "LLM citations can drive high-intent traffic, but they help conversion only when the cited pages clearly continue the answer and offer relevant next steps. If the landing page matches the question, adds useful detail, and has thoughtful calls to action, citations become a real revenue and adoption driver."
            }
          }
        ],
