        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How is LLM citation tracking different from regular SEO tracking or brand monitoring tools I already use?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Compared to traditional SEO and brand monitoring, LLM citation tracking focuses on whether AI answer engines mention and cite you inside generated responses, not just where you rank or get tagged on the web. It’s closer to monitoring “AI-era authority.”\n\nContext: SEO tracks organic positions and traffic, while brand monitoring tools watch social and web mentions. LLM citation tracking sits beside these, showing how AI intermediaries are summarizing your category and choosing sources.\n\nKey factors:\n- SEO: measures rankings and clicks from search results.\n- Brand monitoring: tracks mentions across sites and social.\n- LLM citation tracking: measures mentions and source links inside AI answers.\n- All three together show full digital visibility.\n\nPractical guidance: Don’t replace SEO or traditional monitoring; layer LLM citation tracking on top. Use it to explain why some queries convert differently when users rely on AI answers instead of search results. \n\nSoft positioning: Think of LLM citation tracking as the missing piece that tells you how AI itself is shaping your brand’s presence in the customer research journey.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "SEO tracking measures where you rank and get clicks; brand monitoring tracks mentions on sites and social; LLM citation tracking shows whether AI models mention and cite you as a source in their answers. Together, they give a fuller view of your digital visibility."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "SEO tracking measures where you rank and get clicks; brand monitoring tracks mentions on sites and social; LLM citation tracking shows whether AI models mention"
      }
    },
