        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How often should we be checking AI citations so we don’t miss big changes but also don’t drown in busywork?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For most brands, a weekly or bi-weekly AI citation audit is enough to spot meaningful changes without overwhelming your team. High-volatility categories or fast-moving niches might justify weekly deep dives plus lighter spot checks in between.\n\nAI answers can shift quickly as models update and new content enters the ecosystem, so a one-time snapshot is insufficient. A regular cadence turns AI citation tracking into a trend rather than a moment.\n\nKey factors:\n- How fast your industry and competitors change\n- How critical AI-driven traffic is to your pipeline\n- The number of prompts and platforms you monitor\n- Your team’s capacity for recurring analysis\n\nStart with a weekly run for your top 20–30 prompts and save full responses for comparison. After a month or two, you’ll know whether you can back off to bi-weekly or need to keep the same pace. Design a simple checklist so audits feel routine rather than ad hoc.\n\nThink of AI citation tracking as a pulse check on your digital visibility, not an emergency sprint.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Most teams get good signal with weekly or bi-weekly AI citation checks, focusing on a defined set of high-intent prompts across the main AI platforms. This cadence lets you catch shifts in visibility and competitor mentions without turning AI citation tracking into a full-time job."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Most teams get good signal with weekly or bi-weekly AI citation checks, focusing on a defined set of high-intent prompts across the main AI platforms. This cade"
      }
    },
    {
