              "text": "In Austin, Denver, and Salt Lake City, AI citation tracking can highlight how often local tech, outdoor, or startup-focused brands are mentioned in AI answers compared to national players. These ecosystems have distinctive buyer questions that AI tools may interpret differently.\n\nMonitoring citations against city-specific prompts helps you see whether AI understands your regional positioning or defaults to big national names.\n\nKey factors:\n- City-specific prompts tied to local industries (tech in Austin, outdoors in Denver, etc.)\n- Differences between generic and city-modified queries\n- Frequency of regional brand mentions vs national brands\n- Role of local publications and communities as cited sources\n\nBuild prompts like “best coworking spaces for startups in Austin,” “top outdoor gear shops in Denver,” or “best SaaS meetups in Salt Lake City” and track who appears. Use findings to strengthen content that aligns with your city’s niche and local communities AI often references.\n\nThink of regional AI citation tracking as tuning your visibility to each city’s unique demand patterns.",
