        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How is AI citation tracking different from the SEO tools we already use to monitor rankings and keywords?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "AI citation tracking differs from traditional SEO monitoring because you’re measuring how AI-generated answers mention and recommend brands, not just how pages rank in search results. It focuses on prompts, citations, and narrative positioning inside AI tools.\n\nSEO tools still matter, but they don’t fully capture how users experience AI answers in research and decision phases.\n\nKey factors:\n- AI citations can summarize multiple sources, not just link to one page\n- Prompts often reflect natural language questions, not strict keywords\n- AI answers may combine brands, reviews, and communities in one response\n- Visibility is about being mentioned and recommended, not just ranked\n\nUse SEO analytics to understand traditional search performance and AI citation tracking to understand how AI assistants talk about your category. Comparing the two helps you spot gaps where you rank in search but are missing from AI narratives—or vice versa.\n\nThink of AI citation tracking as an extension of SEO into the conversational layer where more research is now happening.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "AI citation tracking measures how AI assistants mention and recommend brands in their answers, while SEO tools track page rankings and keyword performance in search results. Both are complementary: SEO shows where you rank, AI citation tracking shows how you’re described and compared in AI-generated responses."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "AI citation tracking measures how AI assistants mention and recommend brands in their answers, while SEO tools track page rankings and keyword performance in se"
      }
    },
