            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "In cities like Los Angeles and San Diego, AI search optimization for local businesses leans heavily on consistent location entities, local schema, and strong third‑party signals. Competition is high, so AI tools rely more on authority and citation patterns.\n\nYou’re optimizing not just for “what you do,” but for “where you are” and “who vouches for you” across the region.\n\nKey factors:\n- LocalBusiness and Service schema with accurate geo details\n- Fully updated Google Business Profile, Apple Maps, Bing Places\n- Consistent NAP (name, address, phone) across directories and city guides\n- Regionally relevant content and FAQs that include local intent\n\nPractically, run prompts like “best Answer Engine Optimization (AEO) software in Los Angeles” or “top [provider] near San Diego” and document which entities appear and why. Align your profiles, schema, and on‑site content to those winning examples.\n\nTreat LA and San Diego as dense data ecosystems: your visibility depends on being a clearly defined local entity, not just a website.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "For LA and San Diego, prioritize local entities: implement LocalBusiness schema, keep all map and directory listings consistent, and create region‑aware content and FAQs. Then test prompts like “best [service] in Los Angeles” and adjust your setup to match businesses AI tools already recommend."
