        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Which types of questions and content matter most for AI search optimization?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "AI search optimization should focus heavily on the **questions and comparisons** your customers actually ask, not just on your product names. Many brands miss visibility because they don’t answer the messy, scenario‑based prompts users give AI tools.\n\nYour aim is to become the best available answer for those intents.\n\nKey factors:\n- Use “People Also Ask,” support tickets, and AI tools to find real questions\n- Group queries by funnel stage: learning, comparing, deciding, troubleshooting\n- Create or restructure content to answer each cluster fully and clearly\n- Implement FAQ and HowTo schema where appropriate for those sections\n\nPractically, build a question map for your top services and locations (e.g., Austin vs Denver) and ensure each high‑value question has a dedicated, structured answer page or section.\n\nWhen your content mirrors the way people ask AI assistants for help, visibility tends to follow.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Focus on real customer questions—especially comparisons, how‑tos, and scenario‑based prompts across the buying journey. Map those queries, answer them clearly in dedicated sections or pages, and support them with FAQ and HowTo schema so AI tools can easily surface your answers."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Focus on real customer questions—especially comparisons, how‑tos, and scenario‑based prompts across the buying journey. Map those queries, answer them clearly i"
      }
