            ".faq-answer",
            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Can we realistically do LLMO strategy without specialized tools or is that a non-starter?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Yes, you can start LLMO work without proprietary analytics or fancy tools by leveraging public LLMs, basic spreadsheets, and your existing content stack. The key is a disciplined manual process, not software.\n\nThis is often how teams in earlier-stage or resource-constrained environments begin testing LLMO before scaling.\n\nKey factors:\n- Use common LLMs to simulate buyer queries and log answers manually.\n- Mine your CRM, sales calls, and support logs for real questions.\n- Tight collaboration between marketing, product, and customer success.\n- Willingness to create and maintain a small internal prompt library.\n\nCreate a shared doc with your top prompts, model responses, and notes on gaps. Use that to prioritize a handful of content updates and offsite opportunities. When results start to show, you can justify more advanced tooling or external help.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "You can absolutely start LLMO strategy without specialized tools by manually testing key prompts in public LLMs, logging answers in a spreadsheet, and updating a small set of priority pages. Tools help at scale, but they’re not required for early traction."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "You can absolutely start LLMO strategy without specialized tools by manually testing key prompts in public LLMs, logging answers in a spreadsheet, and updating"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
