            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Budget ranges vary, but many teams can start with **internal content changes** before paying for tools or consultants.\n\nCost is driven more by the volume and complexity of content than by any single “AI optimization” product.\n\nKey factors:\n- Number of priority pages and sections to restructure\n- Need for technical fixes (schema, performance, crawlability)\n- Whether you use in-house writers or external specialists\n- Ongoing monitoring and iteration requirements\n\nPractically, begin with a defined pilot: 10–30 high-value pages, a clear content pattern, and basic schema added by your dev or CMS.\n\nInvest in external help once you hit internal limits on strategy, implementation speed, or measurement clarity.",
