            "name": "What are the real risks if I don’t optimize my content properly for AI answers? Can it actually hurt my brand?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "The main risks are **being misquoted, overlooked, or simplified** if your content is ambiguous, outdated, or contradicts itself.\n\nAI systems prefer sources with clean claims, consistent facts, and up-to-date examples; messy content can cause them to skip or distort you.\n\nKey factors:\n- Conflicting statements across pages about pricing, features, or policies\n- Lack of dates, authorship, or context for claims\n- Thin or promotional copy with no evidence\n- Poor structure that hides the real answer\n\nReduce risk by reviewing key pages for clarity, consistency, and recent data before pushing schema and Q&A structures.\n\nTreat every important section as a quotable statement you’d be comfortable seeing repeated elsewhere.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Yes. If your content is unclear, outdated, or inconsistent, AI systems may misquote you, skip you entirely, or reduce your message to oversimplified snippets. Tightening claims, dates, and structure significantly lowers brand risk in AI-generated answers."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Yes. If your content is unclear, outdated, or inconsistent, AI systems may misquote you, skip you entirely, or reduce your message to oversimplified snippets. T"
      }
