              "text": "If you need AI answer visibility fast, focus on **a compact pilot with your most commercially important questions**, not your whole site.\n\nSpeed comes from tight scope, clear patterns, and quick review cycles, not rushing half-finished changes everywhere.\n\nKey factors:\n- Choose 15–30 prompts that directly drive leads or sales\n- Map each prompt to a dedicated section with a direct answer\n- Add FAQPage/Article schema and fix basic technical issues\n- Monitor AI answers weekly and refine weak sections first\n\nRun this as a 4–8 week sprint where content, dev, and analytics collaborate closely.\n\nOnce you see early wins, you can extend the approach to secondary topics at a more sustainable pace.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Pick 15–30 high-impact questions and turn each into a structured section with a direct answer, supporting bullets, and clean schema. Fix basic technical issues, then monitor AI answers weekly. A focused 4–8 week sprint on critical topics usually produces the fastest visible gains."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Pick 15–30 high-impact questions and turn each into a structured section with a direct answer, supporting bullets, and clean schema. Fix basic technical issues,"
      }
    },
