            "name": "If I want my whole team writing AI-optimized content, what kind of internal guidelines should I set up?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Start with a **repeatable content pattern** so writers know exactly how to structure AI-ready sections.\n\nDocumentation doesn’t need to be long; it needs to be prescriptive and easy to follow across teams and projects.\n\nKey factors:\n- Standard section template: question heading → 1–2 sentence answer → bullets/examples\n- Rules for length, tone, and use of schema\n- Guidance on citing data and including dates/authors\n- Checklists for pre-publish review and periodic updates\n\nCreate a short playbook and a sample “gold standard” page, then train your writers and editors on using that template.\n\nConsistent patterns make AI optimization scalable without turning every page into a bespoke project.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Define a simple template: question-style headings, a 1–2 sentence direct answer, short supporting paragraphs or bullets, clear citations and dates, and specific schema rules. Document this in a concise playbook and use a “model page” as an example so everyone can produce consistent, AI-ready content."
            }
          }
