            "name": "What should I do if AI tools are already giving wrong information about my company or services?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If AI answers about your brand are wrong or outdated, you need to **fix both your own content and the external sources AI relies on**.\n\nSimply updating one page rarely changes entrenched misconceptions by itself.\n\nKey factors:\n- Identify which sites or documents AI is citing in incorrect answers\n- Update your website with clear, prominent corrections and explanations\n- Reach out to third-party platforms to update or clarify old information\n- Add structured data and FAQs addressing the specific misconceptions\n\nTrack key prompts over time and adjust your content until AI answers shift toward the corrected narrative.\n\nYou’re essentially running a reputation and facts alignment project across both owned and external content.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Audit the prompts and sources behind those answers, then update your own site with clear, prominent corrections and supporting schema. Where AI is citing third-party pages, work to update or clarify those as well. Monitor the same prompts over time until the AI responses reflect your corrected information."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Audit the prompts and sources behind those answers, then update your own site with clear, prominent corrections and supporting schema. Where AI is citing third-"
      }
