              "text": "You don’t need to choose between DIY and professional help; you can **combine internal content restructuring with targeted expert support**.\n\nDIY works well for applying a basic pattern, while specialists can help with strategy, measurement, and complex technical issues.\n\nKey factors:\n- Internal capacity for writing, editing, and simple schema\n- Need for advanced analytics, experimentation, or platform-specific tactics\n- Complexity of your site architecture and existing SEO investments\n- Appetite for ongoing iteration versus one-off fixes\n\nStart by piloting DIY changes on a subset of pages, then consider bringing in experts to refine your approach or scale it.\n\nUse professional support where you’ll get leverage, not just labor you already have.",
