            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Optimizing for AI overviews is an extension of SEO: you keep classic on-page and technical best practices, but you deliberately structure content for short, extractable answers and clusters of related questions.\n\nInstead of chasing single keywords, you’re building answer-ready resources around topics and entities.\n\nKey factors:\n- SEO focus: rankings, traffic, and backlinks; AI overview focus: succinct, high-confidence answer snippets.\n- Both need technical health and quality content, but AIO rewards clean Q&A formatting and clear summaries more heavily.\n- Topical authority matters more than isolated “perfect” pages.\n- Monitoring shifts from just positions to whether your site is cited in AI summaries.\n\nKeep doing SEO fundamentals, but revise key pages to lead with direct answers, expand with structured detail, and include FAQs that mirror real user follow-ups. Track both rankings and AI overview visibility when judging success.\n\nIf you bring in a consultant, ask how they handle “answer engine optimization” on top of standard SEO.",
