            "name": "I’m on a limited budget—what’s the most cost-effective way to optimize my content for AI overviews?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "On a tight budget, prioritize a few high-intent pages and fix structure, clarity, and freshness before anything else—this alone can dramatically improve your odds of being used in AI overviews.\n\nYou don’t need new tools right away; you need focused edits that make existing content more answer-friendly.\n\nKey factors:\n- Start with pages that already rank on page 1–2 for valuable queries.\n- Rewrite intros and major sections to lead with 1–3 sentence direct answers.\n- Add 5–10 well-researched FAQs using real question phrasing.\n- Update outdated stats, examples, and screenshots.\n\nSet aside a small weekly block to optimize one page at a time: tighten headings, add bullets and tables, and refresh data. Track impressions and clicks for related queries to see which pages respond.\n\nIf you later hire help, they can build on this foundation instead of redoing everything from scratch.",
