            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For local businesses, AI overviews can surface both general advice and nearby providers, so you need content that proves you understand the local context plus strong local SEO basics.\n\nIn places like Los Angeles, San Diego, Austin, Denver, or Salt Lake City, competition is higher, so clarity and authority matter even more.\n\nKey factors:\n- Local signals: accurate Google Business Profiles, consistent NAP data, and local reviews.\n- Content: pages that discuss local issues, regulations, climate, or customer scenarios.\n- Entities: clear descriptions of your services, locations, and service areas.\n- Links: mentions from local publications, organizations, or partners.\n\nCreate location-aware resources (guides, FAQs, case studies) that answer questions your local audience actually asks, then tie those to strong business profiles and internal links. Monitor which local queries trigger AI overviews and refine accordingly.\n\nLocal-savvy SEO help is especially valuable in competitive metro areas where generic content rarely wins.",
