          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Is it safe to use AI-generated content if I want to rank in and be cited by AI overviews?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If you rely heavily on AI-generated drafts, you need a strong human review and editing process to ensure the final content is accurate, nuanced, and aligned with your brand and expertise.\n\nSearch engines and AI overviews reward quality and trust, not raw AI output.\n\nKey factors:\n- Fact-checking: verify data, claims, and examples before publishing.\n- Expertise: inject your real experience, opinions, and case studies.\n- Structure: reshape AI drafts into clear, question-led sections with concise summaries.\n- Voice: edit for tone, readability, and brand consistency.\n\nUse AI as a starting point for outlines, ideas, or first drafts, then have subject matter experts and editors refine the content into something you’re proud to put your name on. Avoid publishing untouched AI output.\n\nProfessionals who understand both AI tools and editorial standards can help you build safe, efficient workflows.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "You can use AI as a drafting aid, but you must layer on human expertise: fact-check, add your own insights, restructure for clear Q&A sections, and edit for quality. Raw, unedited AI text is unlikely to perform well or be trusted in AI overviews."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "You can use AI as a drafting aid, but you must layer on human expertise: fact-check, add your own insights, restructure for clear Q&A sections, and edit for qua"
      }
    },
    {
