            "name": "What does “success” with Perplexity answers actually look like for my business beyond vanity citations?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Your goal isn’t just to “appear” once, but to become a stable, go‑to source that Perplexity cites repeatedly for the questions that matter to you. Good outcomes look like consistent citations on category, brand, and comparison queries.\n\nOver time, this can drive qualified traffic, trust, and indirect conversions—especially on complex, research-heavy decisions.\n\nKey factors:\n- Frequency of citations across your target prompt list\n- Position of your URL in Perplexity’s sources for those answers\n- Accuracy of how your services, pricing, and differentiators are represented\n- Growth in organic and referral traffic from cited pages\n\nSet up a simple tracking sheet of 20–40 prompts, check them monthly, and note whether you’re mentioned or cited, plus any traffic patterns. Use that feedback to refine content and expand into adjacent topics.\n\nThink of Perplexity visibility as compounding: once you’re the reliable answer in one area, it becomes much easier to earn trust in related areas.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Success is consistent, accurate citations on the questions that matter to your business—category, brand, and comparison prompts—plus measurable traffic and trust gains. Track a set of target queries monthly, watch your citation frequency and position, and refine content so Perplexity repeatedly treats you as a go‑to source."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Success is consistent, accurate citations on the questions that matter to your business—category, brand, and comparison prompts—plus measurable traffic and trus"
      }
