            "name": "Does it cost anything to show up in Google AI Overviews, and how should I budget for it?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "There is no direct cost or paid program to appear in Google AI Overviews; inclusion is organic. The “cost” is the time, tools, and expertise you invest in content, technical SEO, and structured data.\n\nGoogle doesn’t sell AI Overview placement or run an application process. Instead, it cites pages that already perform well in search for the question being asked. That means your budget goes into high-quality content, technical optimization, and possibly SEO platforms to research queries that trigger AI Overviews.\n\nKey factors:\n- Content creation and optimization hours\n- SEO tools for keyword and AI Overview tracking\n- Developer time for performance and schema markup\n- Ongoing monitoring and iteration\n\nPractically, treat AI Overview optimization as part of your broader SEO budget, not a stand-alone line item. Start with your highest-value queries so you get maximum impact per dollar.\n\nSoft positioning: Teams that see strong ROI from AI Overviews usually align them with existing SEO and content investments rather than chasing them as a separate expense.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "You can’t pay to appear in Google AI Overviews; placement is organic. The real cost is your investment in SEO: creating clear Q&A content, adding schema markup, improving site performance, and using tools to track and refine your visibility."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "You can’t pay to appear in Google AI Overviews; placement is organic. The real cost is your investment in SEO: creating clear Q&A content, adding schema markup,"
      }
