        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What’s the first thing I should do to optimize my content specifically to be pulled into Google AI Overviews?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Start by identifying queries that already trigger AI Overviews and where your business should be visible, then rework your content to match how Google’s AI is answering those questions. You’re essentially reverse-engineering the answer format.\n\nGoogle AI Overviews tend to pull content that gives short, direct answers, followed by well-structured detail, often supported by FAQ schema or HowTo markup. Look at existing AI Overviews in your niche, note the layout (lists, tables, steps), and adjust your pages to mirror that structure while staying original.\n\nKey factors:\n- Manual review of existing AI Overviews in your niche\n- Matching answer formats (paragraph, list, comparison)\n- Adding question H2s with concise answer paragraphs\n- Implementing FAQPage and HowTo schema where relevant\n\nPractically, take your top informational pages and layer in explicit questions users ask, each with a 2–3 sentence direct answer, then supporting detail. Re-check the search results monthly and continue shaping content toward the winning patterns.\n\nSoft positioning: The brands that reliably appear in AI Overviews study the current answer formats as closely as they study keyword metrics.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "First, map which of your target queries already show AI Overviews, then study how those answers are structured. Rework your pages to match that pattern with clear question headings, short direct answers, supporting detail, and FAQ/HowTo schema."
            }
          }
        ],
