        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Will writing city-specific content for places like Los Angeles, San Diego, Austin, Denver, and Salt Lake City help me show up more often in Google AI Overviews?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Scenario-based content—like explaining local issues in Denver’s climate or Austin’s regulations—can significantly increase your odds of appearing in AI Overviews for those specific queries. Google’s AI responds to detailed, contextual answers.\n\nWhen users search “how to do X in Los Angeles” or “best way to Y in Salt Lake City winter,” AI Overviews look for pages that explicitly address that city or condition. Generic nationwide content often loses to location-aware answers with practical detail.\n\nKey factors:\n- City- or region-specific examples and guidance\n- Local terminology, conditions, and constraints\n- Dedicated location pages and FAQs\n- Consistent internal linking between general and local content\n\nPractically, build content that tackles the same core topic but tailored for LA, San Diego, Austin, Denver, and Salt Lake City, including separate FAQs for each city where meaningful differences exist. This gives Google’s AI clear sources for geo-specific questions.\n\nSoft positioning: Businesses that “think like locals” in their content often win the local AI Overview snippets when users search with city modifiers.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Yes. City‑specific content that addresses local conditions and questions makes you much more likely to be cited in AI Overviews for geo‑modified searches like “how to do X in Denver” or “best way to Y in Los Angeles.”"
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Yes. City‑specific content that addresses local conditions and questions makes you much more likely to be cited in AI Overviews for geo‑modified searches like “"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
