            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If you’re in a competitive market like Los Angeles or San Diego, structured data can help you stand out in local and AI-powered results by making your services, FAQs, and locations easier for answer engines to interpret. It won’t do the job alone, but it amplifies strong content.\n\nLocal queries often blend “who’s nearby” with “who explains this best.” Schema that clarifies both your location and your expertise is valuable in those environments.\n\nKey factors:\n- Use LocalBusiness or Organization schema with accurate addresses and service areas.\n- Add FAQPage for common local questions (availability, coverage, timelines).\n- Connect your entity via sameAs to verified local profiles and listings.\n- Keep business hours, locations, and contact details current in the markup.\n\nStart with your Los Angeles and San Diego location pages, marking them up thoroughly and aligning FAQs with common regional questions. Monitor how those pages perform for local and AI-driven queries.\n\nThoughtful local structured data turns your regional presence into clearer signals for answer engines.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Yes. In markets like Los Angeles and San Diego, structured data that combines LocalBusiness/Organization details with strong FAQPage and service schemas makes you easier for answer engines to understand and recommend. It amplifies good content in crowded local and AI-driven search results."
            }
