              "text": "In cities like Austin and Denver, structured data for AEO is most useful when it explains both what you do and where you do it, in a way answer engines can trust. It’s a way to make your regional presence machine-readable.\n\nTech-forward markets often have savvy competitors who already use schema. Matching or surpassing their implementation helps ensure you’re part of the answer set for local and expert queries.\n\nKey factors:\n- Mark key location pages with Organization or LocalBusiness schema.\n- Include city-specific FAQs and HowTo content with corresponding schemas.\n- Use sameAs to link to trusted local directories and profiles.\n- Keep your structured data consistent across Austin and Denver sites or sections.\n\nPractically, start with your Austin and Denver service pages, outlining what’s unique there (coverage, timelines, integrations) and reflecting that in both content and schema. Validate and monitor changes in local and AI-search visibility.\n\nStructured data gives answer engines a clearer picture of your city-level presence and expertise.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Mark Austin and Denver location pages with Organization/LocalBusiness schema, add city-specific FAQPage and HowTo content, and link to trusted local profiles via sameAs. Consistent, city-aware structured data helps answer engines understand and surface your regional services more reliably."
            }
