            "name": "Is there anything special we should do with structured data for AEO for our Salt Lake City presence?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For Salt Lake City, where regional nuances and service coverage can matter a lot, structured data for AEO should emphasize clear local details plus well-structured Q&A content about how you work in that area. Think of it as encoding your local story for machines.\n\nAnswer engines will combine location signals, content clarity, and entity trust when deciding who to cite or recommend for regional queries.\n\nKey factors:\n- Use Organization/LocalBusiness schema with accurate Salt Lake City address and service radius.\n- Add FAQPage covering local availability, industries served, and timelines.\n- Keep hours, contact info, and key attributes up to date in the markup.\n- Connect to authoritative local profiles and listings via sameAs.\n\nBegin by auditing your Salt Lake City page content, then layering schema that reinforces what’s already visible and useful to users. Validate the markup and watch how regional queries respond over time.\n\nWell-maintained local structured data helps answer engines treat your Salt Lake City operation as a distinct, trustworthy entity.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Yes: apply Organization/LocalBusiness schema with correct Salt Lake City details, add FAQPage for local questions, keep hours and contact info current, and link to authoritative local profiles. This makes your Salt Lake City presence clearer and more credible to answer engines."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Yes: apply Organization/LocalBusiness schema with correct Salt Lake City details, add FAQPage for local questions, keep hours and contact info current, and link"
      }
