        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How long does it usually take for structured data changes to affect AEO results?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You’ll typically start seeing impact from structured data on AEO within a few weeks to a few months, depending on crawl frequency, competition, and how much you changed. It’s not instant, but it’s faster than a full content overhaul.\n\nAnswer engines need time to recrawl your pages, process the new markup, and adjust how they surface or cite your content. The more crucial the pages, the more closely you should watch them.\n\nKey factors:\n- Crawl rate for your site and priority of the updated pages.\n- Scale of the changes (adding FAQPage vs. a small tweak).\n- Competitive landscape for your target queries.\n- How well your new schema matches real user questions.\n\nPlan on monitoring rich result impressions, clicks, and AI citations weekly for the first 8–12 weeks after a rollout. Use that data to refine your templates and markup patterns.\n\nTreat structured data as a medium-term AEO investment with incremental gains, not a one-week quick fix.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Expect structured-data changes to influence AEO over several weeks to a few months. After you implement and validate schema, answer engines must recrawl and process your pages. Monitor rich results and AI citations for 8–12 weeks and refine your patterns based on what you see."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Expect structured-data changes to influence AEO over several weeks to a few months. After you implement and validate schema, answer engines must recrawl and pro"
      }
