        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "My structured data validates fine, but AEO results aren’t improving. What am I missing?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If your structured data passes validation but you’re not seeing better AEO results, the issue is usually content alignment, query targeting, or competitive pressure—not just the technical markup. Valid schema is necessary but not sufficient.\n\nAnswer engines still prioritize relevance and usefulness. Schema helps them understand your content; it doesn’t guarantee that your content wins.\n\nKey factors:\n- Check whether your pages answer the queries you’re targeting directly.\n- Compare your FAQs and guides to top competitors’ depth and clarity.\n- Ensure headings and first sentences clearly match your schema structure.\n- Evaluate whether you’ve marked the right pages, not just any pages.\n\nGo back to your query and journey mapping, adjust content to better address real questions, and refine which pages get FAQPage, Article, or HowTo schema. Monitor changes over several weeks.\n\nTreat schema as an amplifier of strong content, and focus improvements on both technical and editorial sides for better AEO gains.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Valid schema alone won’t drive AEO gains. Reassess whether your content directly answers the queries you target, how it compares to competitors, and whether you’ve marked the right pages. Improve question alignment, clarity, and depth, then let structured data amplify those stronger answers."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Valid schema alone won’t drive AEO gains. Reassess whether your content directly answers the queries you target, how it compares to competitors, and whether you"
      }
    },
