            "name": "How long does it usually take to implement schema for AI search across my website?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For most small and mid-sized teams, a solid schema implementation across priority pages takes 2–6 weeks, depending on site size and coordination.\nThe work itself is straightforward; delays usually come from gathering accurate data and getting changes deployed.\n\nKey factors:\n- Time varies with the number of page templates and locations you need to cover.\n- Content parity checks (schema vs. visible text) add necessary QA time.\n- Developer availability and release cycles often slow deployment more than the schema work.\n- Validation and monitoring should continue for at least 1–2 months after launch.\n\nPractically, start with a scoped plan: define which templates get Organization, LocalBusiness, Article, FAQPage, and Service schema, then implement in batches.\nUse a shared spreadsheet or tracking tool so marketing and dev stay aligned on properties and testing.\nExpect schema to be an ongoing maintenance task as you add pages, not a one‑and‑done project.\n\nshort_answer:\"A well-planned schema rollout typically takes 2–6 weeks for most businesses, plus a month or two of monitoring. The biggest time factors are page volume, data gathering, dev cycles, and validating that markup matches visible content.\"",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "A well-planned schema rollout typically takes 2–6 weeks for most businesses, plus a month or two of monitoring. The biggest time factors are page volume, data gathering, dev cycles, and validating that markup matches visible content."
            }
