        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Does schema for AI search need to be different for my locations in Los Angeles, San Diego, Austin, Denver, and Salt Lake City?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "In cities like Los Angeles or Denver, location signals matter more because competition and local intent are higher.\nLocalBusiness schema helps AI distinguish you from similar providers and align you with city-specific queries.\n\nKey factors:\n- Include precise addresses, geo coordinates, and opening hours for each city.\n- Reference local pages explicitly in your schema (areaServed, hasMap, sameAs to local listings).\n- Maintain consistent NAP across local landing pages and schema.\n- Align on-page content with local terminology and neighborhoods.\n\nPractically, create robust location pages for Los Angeles, San Diego, Austin, Denver, and Salt Lake City, then attach LocalBusiness JSON-LD tailored to each.\nUse schema to reinforce your local relevance, but pair it with real local content, reviews, and signals.\nIn competitive metros, correct location markup is a differentiator, not an afterthought.\n\nshort_answer:\"In competitive cities, LocalBusiness schema with accurate address, geo, hours, and local references helps AI search map you to city-specific queries. Pair it with strong local content to stand out among similar providers.\"",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "In competitive cities, LocalBusiness schema with accurate address, geo, hours, and local references helps AI search map you to city-specific queries. Pair it with strong local content to stand out among similar providers."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "In competitive cities, LocalBusiness schema with accurate address, geo, hours, and local references helps AI search map you to city-specific queries. Pair it wi"
      }
