              "text": "In cities like Los Angeles or San Diego, local question-based keywords should reflect urban realities: competition, traffic, cost, and neighborhood differences. Think in terms of “best options near me,” “is X worth it in LA,” or “how to do Y without wasting time in traffic.”\n\nUsers there often care about convenience and trade‑offs as much as the service itself.\n\nKey factors:\n- Incorporate neighborhood modifiers (Downtown LA, La Jolla, etc.) when relevant.\n- Address higher cost, parking, or scheduling constraints in answers.\n- Consider bilingual or multicultural phrasing if your audience is diverse.\n- Use examples that match common local scenarios and landmarks.\n\nPractically, review your local reviews and customer messages from each city to identify unique questions. Build city-specific FAQs only where differences are meaningful (e.g., costs, logistics), not just for SEO decoration.\n\nDone well, your content feels like it was written by someone who understands LA or San Diego life, not a generic template.",
