            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If your question-based content isn’t getting traffic, first check whether you’re targeting questions with any search volume, then evaluate if your answers are clearer and more comprehensive than what already ranks. Sometimes the problem is intent mismatch rather than SEO.\n\nYou may be writing good content for questions almost no one asks—or answering a different question than the one on the page.\n\nKey factors:\n- Validate search volume and difficulty for target questions.\n- Analyze top-ranking pages and compare depth and structure.\n- Ensure on-page basics: titles, headings, meta descriptions, internal links.\n- Check indexing, crawl issues, and page speed as hygiene factors.\n\nIn practice, start with a content and SERP audit for 5–10 underperforming questions. You might consolidate thin pages, improve answer clarity, or pivot to adjacent questions with stronger demand.\n\nTreat poor performance as feedback: it’s pointing you toward either better questions or better answers.",
