            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Costs range from essentially free (DIY using internal data and simple tools) to ongoing budget for specialized SEO, content strategy, and analytics support. The biggest investment is usually time: research, rewriting, and maintaining question‑based content.\n\nIf you already produce content regularly, conversational optimization is often a shift in approach rather than a major new expense.\n\nKey factors:\n- DIY vs hiring specialists for SEO, analytics, and content writing\n- Tool stack: free options (Search Console, PAA) vs paid keyword/insight tools\n- Scale: a few core FAQs vs comprehensive topic clusters across the site\n- Internal effort to align product, support, and marketing around user questions\n\nPractically, start small: optimize your top 10–20 pages for conversational queries and measure impact before committing larger budgets. That data helps justify further investment.\n\nThink of cost less as a line item and more as modernizing how you communicate online.",
