        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How can I use Google’s People Also Ask box to find better conversational search queries to target?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Google’s “People Also Ask” box is one of the best shortcuts to discovering conversational queries because it exposes real follow‑up questions users ask after an initial search. Each PAA entry is a phrased question you can potentially answer.\n\nInstead of guessing, you can pull clusters of related questions directly from PAA and build content around them.\n\nKey factors:\n- PAA surfaces live user questions tied to your core topics\n- It reveals intent variations: how‑to, troubleshooting, comparisons, cost\n- You can expand PAA lists by clicking questions to load more\n- Tools exist to scrape and analyze PAA at scale\n\nUse PAA to validate and enrich the question sets you already have from Search Console and internal data. Prioritize questions that recur across multiple related searches.\n\nThink of PAA as a window into the real late‑night questions your audience types (or speaks) when they’re stuck.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Search your main topics in Google and study the People Also Ask box. Each entry is a real conversational question. Expand it by clicking questions, then collect and cluster those queries to guide your FAQ pages, answer‑first content, and topic clusters."
            }
          }
