            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For businesses in Los Angeles and San Diego, local conversational queries often add neighborhood, traffic, and timing constraints, like “best coworking space near Downtown LA open late” or “family‑friendly brunch in North Park this weekend.” Your content needs to mirror that specificity.\n\nLocal searchers in these cities rely heavily on mobile and voice, especially while driving or planning nights out.\n\nKey factors:\n- Include precise local modifiers: areas (Silver Lake, La Jolla), landmarks, transit\n- Address parking, peak hours, and seasonal events where relevant\n- Keep Google Business Profiles accurate and synced with on‑site info\n- Ensure pages load quickly and are easy to skim on phones\n\nWhen crafting FAQs, think like a local: what someone in traffic or on the sidewalk would ask their phone. Reflect those real scenarios in your questions and answers.\n\nYou’re not just answering “what,” but “what, where, and when” for Los Angeles and San Diego users.",
