        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How do I measure whether my conversational search query optimization is actually working?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Use metrics that reflect both discovery and usefulness: impressions and clicks for question‑style queries, featured snippet and FAQ visibility, time on page, and downstream conversions or reduced support load. Conversational optimization isn’t just about traffic; it’s about how well your answers work.\n\nTrack performance at the query level whenever possible.\n\nKey factors:\n- Monitor “how/what/why/where” and “best/difference/near” queries in Search Console\n- Check click‑through rates for pages with short, answer‑first sections\n- Watch for growth in long‑tail question rankings and snippet ownership\n- Measure changes in support tickets about topics you’ve covered in FAQs\n\nSet up dashboards that connect questions to outcomes, not just to pageviews. Review them monthly and adjust content based on emerging queries.\n\nYou’re creating a feedback loop between what people ask and what you publish.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Track impressions and clicks for question‑style queries, featured snippet and FAQ appearances, engagement on Q&A pages, and conversions or reduced support tickets for covered topics. Success is when more of the right people find clear answers and take useful next steps."
