          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How important is zero-click visibility for local businesses in cities like Los Angeles or San Diego?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Zero-click visibility is crucial for local discovery in cities like Los Angeles or San Diego, where many decisions happen directly in search and Maps.\nPeople often call or navigate without ever visiting a website.\n\nContext: In dense, competitive markets, the business that dominates local packs, Maps, and snippets becomes the default choice.\nOptimizing your presence there drives foot traffic and calls even if organic clicks plateau.\n\nKey factors:\n- Google Business Profile completeness and categories\n- Local reviews, photos, and Q&A\n- Location schema and city-specific landing pages\n- Distance, relevance, and prominence signals in Maps\n\nPractical guidance: For each city—LA, San Diego, Austin, Denver, Salt Lake City—build robust profiles and city pages that answer local intent queries.\nMonitor calls and direction requests per location, not just site traffic.\n\nSoft positioning: Think of zero-click visibility as owning the digital street corner in each market you serve.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Zero-click visibility is critical in cities like Los Angeles or San Diego because many customers choose and contact businesses directly from Google and Maps. Strong profiles, reviews, and local content can drive calls and foot traffic even if website clicks don’t increase."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Zero-click visibility is critical in cities like Los Angeles or San Diego because many customers choose and contact businesses directly from Google and Maps. St"
      }
    },
