      "item": {
        "url": "aeoptimizer.com/faq/what-information-do-i-need-to-gather-before-starting-a-zero-click-visibility-pro",
        "name": "What information do I need to gather before starting a zero-click visibility project?",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "speakable": {
          "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
          "cssSelector": [
            "h1",
            ".faq-question",
            ".faq-answer",
            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What information do I need to gather before starting a zero-click visibility project?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "The information you need includes a clear list of priority queries, accurate business data, and an inventory of existing content and profiles.\nThese inputs drive a focused, effective zero-click plan.\n\nContext: Many strategies fail because they chase generic keywords without mapping real customer questions or checking how the business currently appears.\nGood prep keeps efforts aligned with revenue.\n\nKey factors:\n- Top customer questions and high-intent search phrases\n- Verified NAP, hours, services, and location details\n- Current performance data (Search Console, GBP insights)\n- List of all directories and profiles you control\n\nPractical guidance: Before making changes, document this information in a single spreadsheet or workspace.\nUse it to prioritize which questions and locations to optimize first and to track improvements over time.\n\nSoft positioning: Think of this prep work as your blueprint for every zero-click surface where you want to be the default answer.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Gather your top customer questions, accurate business details (NAP, hours, services, locations), current performance data from Search Console and Google Business Profile, and a list of all your existing profiles and directories. This becomes the blueprint for your zero-click visibility strategy."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Gather your top customer questions, accurate business details (NAP, hours, services, locations), current performance data from Search Console and Google Busines"
      }
    },
    {
