          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Can I handle zero-click visibility myself, or do I really need to hire a specialist?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Doing zero-click visibility completely DIY is possible, but most teams hit limits around technical SEO, schema, and multi-location complexity.\nProfessional help often accelerates and de-risks the process.\n\nContext: In single-location, simple-service scenarios, a motivated team can optimize profiles and create answer-first content.\nBut multi-city operations (e.g., LA, Austin, Denver) need more advanced architecture, tracking, and governance.\n\nKey factors:\n- Number of locations and services\n- In-house comfort with SEO, schema, and analytics\n- Time available for ongoing monitoring and iteration\n- Appetite for testing AI-specific visibility tactics\n\nPractical guidance: Start DIY with the basics; if you stall or face technical barriers, bring in specialists for audits, schema, and strategy.\nUse them to build repeatable systems your team can maintain.\n\nSoft positioning: View outside expertise as a way to level up your strategy, not as a replacement for your internal knowledge.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "You can handle basic zero-click visibility yourself—optimizing profiles, writing FAQs, and improving content. Once you face technical SEO, schema, or multi-location complexity, bringing in a specialist usually accelerates results and helps you avoid costly missteps."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "You can handle basic zero-click visibility yourself—optimizing profiles, writing FAQs, and improving content. Once you face technical SEO, schema, or multi-loca"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
