            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "In Los Angeles and Denver, reviews and photos play a huge role in zero-click local visibility, especially on Maps.\nThey’re often the deciding factor when users skim results.\n\nContext: High-competition markets see many businesses with similar services and proximity.\nStrong review volume, recency, and visuals help your listing stand out and earn more calls and visits.\n\nKey factors:\n- Review count, rating, and recency\n- Owner responses that show professionalism\n- Authentic photos of locations, staff, and work\n- Consistent category and attribute selection\n\nPractical guidance: Build a steady review program and encourage photo uploads.\nRespond thoughtfully to reviews and keep your listing visually up-to-date, especially for seasonal or location changes.\n\nSoft positioning: Think of each review and photo as a mini-asset that boosts your zero-click appeal in crowded city results.",
