      "item": {
        "url": "aeoptimizer.com/faq/how-do-you-actually-calculate-share-of-voice-in-ai-search-step-by-step",
        "name": "How do you actually calculate share of voice in AI search step by step?",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "speakable": {
          "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
          "cssSelector": [
            "h1",
            ".faq-question",
            ".faq-answer",
            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How do you actually calculate share of voice in AI search step by step?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "To calculate share of voice in AI search, you define a set of prompts, run them in selected AI engines, count how often each brand is mentioned, and then convert those counts into percentages. Your AI SOV is your brand’s mentions divided by all tracked brand mentions, times 100.\n\nContext: You’re essentially asking, \"Out of all the AI answers in my category, what share includes my brand?\" This can be done for mention rate, citation rate, and recommendation prompts.\n\nKey factors:\n- Clear formula: AI SOV (%) = (Your brand mentions ÷ All tracked brand mentions) × 100\n- Separate metrics for mentions vs citations vs recommendations\n- Consistent prompt wording and logged-out tests to reduce bias\n- Engine-level SOV and a blended score across engines\n\nPractical guidance: Build a prompt list (30–100 queries), run each query in your target AI engines, log brands mentioned, and calculate your share per engine and overall. Repeat monthly or quarterly to track trends.\n\nSoft positioning: Think of this as your \"market share\" inside AI answers, not just a one-off number.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Define a prompt set, run each prompt in chosen AI engines, count how many times your brand and competitors are mentioned, then compute: AI SOV (%) = (Your brand mentions ÷ All tracked brand mentions) × 100, per engine and overall."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Define a prompt set, run each prompt in chosen AI engines, count how many times your brand and competitors are mentioned, then compute: AI SOV (%) = (Your brand"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 1775,
      "item": {
        "url": "aeoptimizer.com/faq/what-is-a-prompt-universe-for-ai-share-of-voice-and-how-do-i-build-one",
        "name": "What is a “prompt universe” for AI share of voice and how do I build one?",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "speakable": {
          "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
          "cssSelector": [
            "h1",
            ".faq-question",
            ".faq-answer",
            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What is a “prompt universe” for AI share of voice and how do I build one?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "A \"prompt universe\" is the curated list of questions you use to measure your share of voice in AI search. It should mirror the real queries your buyers ask answer engines when they research your product or category.\n\nContext: If your prompt universe is off, your AI share of voice score will be meaningless because you’re measuring the wrong conversations. Good prompt sets combine branded, category, and comparison questions.\n\nKey factors:\n- Branded prompts (e.g., “Is [Brand] reliable?”, “[Brand] reviews”)\n- Category prompts (e.g., “best CRM for small business”) \n- Comparison prompts (e.g., “[Brand] vs [Competitor]”)\n- Sourcing from VOC, PAA, autocomplete, and support tickets\n\nPractical guidance: Start from customer interviews and search data, expand with People Also Ask and autocomplete, then narrow to 30–100 high-intent prompts. Review and refresh these as your product and market evolve.\n\nSoft positioning: Treat the prompt universe as a living research asset, not a one-time list.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "A prompt universe is the curated list of real buyer questions you use to test AI share of voice. Build it from customer research, search data, People Also Ask, autocomplete, and support tickets, mixing branded, category, and comparison prompts."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "A prompt universe is the curated list of real buyer questions you use to test AI share of voice. Build it from customer research, search data, People Also Ask,"
      }
    },
