            "name": "What are the most effective ways to improve my brand’s share of voice in AI search?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You improve share of voice in AI search by increasing how often and how prominently answer engines can justify mentioning your brand. That usually means better content, stronger authority signals, and more trustworthy citations around your core topics.\n\nContext: AI models pull from what they can \"see\" and trust on the open web, plus structured data and user feedback. You’re optimizing the evidence that supports including your brand in answers.\n\nKey factors:\n- High-quality, well-structured content that directly answers real questions\n- Topical authority with deep coverage and supporting pages\n- Credible third‑party mentions: reviews, directories, media, expert quotes\n- Technical clarity: schema, clean site structure, up-to-date details\n\nPractical guidance: Map your prompt universe to specific pages and external references. Fix thin or outdated content first, then target high-authority citations in your niche and keep your brand details consistent everywhere.\n\nSoft positioning: Think like an AI model—give it overwhelming, high-quality reasons to include you in its best answers.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Focus on creating clear, authoritative content around real buyer questions, building topical depth, earning credible third‑party mentions and reviews, and tightening your technical signals (schema, structure). You’re strengthening the evidence AI models use to include your brand."
            }
