            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Yes, you can absolutely start by measuring share of voice in AI search yourself. Manual testing across a handful of prompts and engines is enough to uncover whether you’re invisible, underrepresented, or competitive.\n\nContext: Specialized tools help with scale and nuance, but a DIY approach is valuable for learning the basics, aligning stakeholders, and proving the concept before investing heavily.\n\nKey factors:\n- Limited, well-chosen prompt set\n- Careful logging of brand mentions and citations\n- Clear competitor definitions\n- Time set aside for analysis and follow-through\n\nPractical guidance: Treat your first DIY run as a discovery project. Focus on what patterns you see—where you appear, how you’re described, and where competitors dominate—and derive 5–10 concrete improvements from that.\n\nSoft positioning: Think of DIY AI share of voice measurement as the on-ramp to a more mature, tool-assisted program later.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "You can absolutely start by measuring AI share of voice yourself. Use a small set of high-intent prompts, test them in a few AI engines, log mentions and citations in a spreadsheet, and focus on the patterns you uncover before investing in tools."
