        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Why should my team care about answer engine results if we’re already doing SEO?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Answer engine optimization (AEO) matters because more users are getting answers directly from AI—often without clicking through to websites—so your brand risks becoming invisible if you only optimize for traditional search. AEO makes your content “answer-ready” so AI systems can understand, verify, and reuse it.\n\nAs tools like Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT, and Perplexity grow, they increasingly act as a customer’s first touchpoint with information. Being consistently cited there influences awareness and trust before a click ever happens.\n\nKey factors:\n- Shift focus from rankings to citations and answer visibility\n- Treat conversational AI as a core discovery channel, not a side experiment\n- Align content with how people actually ask questions\n- Track AI mentions as a real performance metric\n\nIn practice, prioritize pages that guide high-value decisions and refactor them for AEO. Monitor how often those pages are quoted in answer engines and refine based on what gets picked up.\n\nTreat AEO as an essential part of your search strategy, not an optional add-on, if you want to stay visible as search evolves.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "You should care about answer engine results because more users now get direct AI answers instead of scrolling traditional SERPs. Answer engine optimization ensures your content is understood, trusted, and cited by tools like ChatGPT and Google AI Overviews, protecting your visibility as search becomes answer-first."
