            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "To optimize for Google’s AI Overviews and other answer engine results, you should structure pages around specific questions, lead with a concise answer paragraph, and support it with well-organized detail and schema markup. This makes your content easy for Google to extract and summarize.\n\nAI Overviews look for clear, authoritative passages that directly answer the query, often in 40–80 words, plus supporting sections for nuance. They also rely on schema, fast load times, and mobile-friendly layouts.\n\nKey factors:\n- Question-based headings (“What is…”, “How to…”, “Why…”) \n- First 100–200 words written as a complete, direct answer\n- FAQ and HowTo schema on relevant sections\n- Strong E-E-A-T signals: author expertise, sources, and transparency\n\nPractically, rewrite your top informational pages to follow this pattern and monitor changes in AI Overview visibility via search console and manual testing. Iterate based on which pages get quoted.\n\nThink of each page as a structured answer package designed for both users and Google’s AI systems.",
