            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If you need answer engine visibility quickly, prioritize a small set of high-intent questions and create or refactor pages to answer them clearly in the next few weeks. You won’t control when AI models refresh, but you can influence what they see and how they interpret it.\n\nSome impact—especially in AI Overviews and real-time crawlers—can appear within days or weeks as your new content is indexed and evaluated. Deeper model-level learning takes longer.\n\nKey factors:\n- Speed of crawling and indexing for your site\n- How closely your new content matches active user queries\n- Use of schema and clear answer formatting\n- Existing domain authority and trust signals\n\nPractically, pick 10–20 priority questions, ship well-structured answers, and monitor AI citations weekly. Adjust based on where you start to see traction.\n\nIn urgent scenarios, focus on clarity and structure over volume; a few excellent answer pages beat many average ones.",
