        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Is answer engine optimization just a buzzword for SEO, or is it actually something different?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Answer engine optimization is not just a rebranded version of SEO, although they overlap. Traditional SEO focuses on rankings and clicks; AEO focuses on being the content that AI systems quote inside their answers, even when no click occurs.\n\nIn practice, you still need technical health and authority, but you shift how you write: questions first, answers upfront, and language that sounds like a helpful human rather than a marketing page.\n\nKey factors:\n- Goal change: citations and inclusion in AI answers vs blue-link rankings\n- Content style: conversational, question-led, evidence-backed\n- Measurement: tracking AI mentions, referrals, and zero-click influence\n- Technicals: schema markup and crawlable structures built around questions\n\nPractically, treat AEO as a layer on top of SEO, not a replacement. Use existing SEO strengths and refactor priority content for answer engines.\n\nFraming it this way helps your team understand why AEO deserves its own strategy and metrics.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Answer engine optimization is related to SEO but different in goal: instead of chasing rankings and clicks, AEO focuses on making your content the material AI systems quote inside answers. It emphasizes question-led, conversational content, schema markup, and tracking citations in tools like ChatGPT and AI Overviews."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Answer engine optimization is related to SEO but different in goal: instead of chasing rankings and clicks, AEO focuses on making your content the material AI s"
      }
