              "text": "For businesses in Los Angeles and San Diego, answer engine results are especially important because customers rely heavily on mobile and voice to find local services quickly. AI assistants often give a single recommended option, so you either show up or you don’t.\n\nLocal intent—“near me,” traffic, parking, neighborhood specifics—must be reflected directly in your answers for AI systems to trust you as a relevant result.\n\nKey factors:\n- Consistent NAP (name, address, phone) and local entities across your site\n- Content that speaks to LA/SD neighborhoods, transit, and local context\n- Reviews and mentions on trusted local platforms\n- Schema markup that reinforces your location and service areas\n\nPractically, build local FAQ pages answering “near me” style queries with specifics (areas served, timing, logistics). Ensure all local signals are aligned.\n\nIn cities with dense competition like LA and San Diego, a strong local AEO strategy can be the difference between being the answer and being invisible.",
