            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You can definitely start answer engine optimization without a huge technical overhaul, but you can’t ignore structure altogether. The fastest wins come from rewriting content into clear Q&A formats and adding basic schema, even on your existing site.\n\nIf your platform limits heavy customization, focus on what you can control: language, layout, headings, and lightweight markup options.\n\nKey factors:\n- Ability to edit page copy and headings\n- Access to add simple JSON-LD or plugin-based schema\n- Site speed and basic mobile usability\n- Internal linking between related question pages\n\nPractically, prioritize content changes first—direct answers, question-based sections, FAQs—then layer on whatever schema your system allows. Upgrade technical foundations later when you see proof of value.\n\nThis phased approach lets you participate in answer engine ecosystems without waiting for a full redesign.",
