            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If answer engine results feel too generic or off-target for your brand, the fix is usually to surface your unique expertise and data more clearly, not to chase broader keywords. AI models can only highlight what they can see and understand.\n\nHidden knowledge in internal docs, support tickets, or sales decks should be turned into public, structured answers that differentiate you from competitors.\n\nKey factors:\n- Identify insights that aren’t widely published elsewhere\n- Publish them as clear, question-led articles and FAQs\n- Provide context, examples, and evidence that show real experience\n- Use schema and internal links to highlight these differentiators\n\nPractically, run an internal audit of “things we explain all the time but never publish” and convert them into answer-ready content. This gives AI something distinctive to cite.\n\nBy leading with your specific strengths, you make answer engine results feel more tailored to your brand and less interchangeable.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Turn your unique, often internal knowledge into public, structured answers. Publish question-led articles and FAQs that showcase specific insights, examples, and data, then support them with schema and internal links. This gives answer engines distinctive material to cite instead of generic industry statements."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Turn your unique, often internal knowledge into public, structured answers. Publish question-led articles and FAQs that showcase specific insights, examples, an"
