        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How important is structured data (schema) for brand authority in AI search, and what should we implement first?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Structured data helps AI search because it gives **machine‑readable facts** about your brand: who you are, what you offer, and how different profiles connect. It’s a shortcut for entity clarity.\n\nWithout schema, models must infer relationships from text and links, which is fragile, especially for brands in crowded markets like Los Angeles or San Diego.\n\nKey factors:\n- Organization schema (name, logo, contact, sameAs links)\n- Service or Product schema for key offerings\n- Consistent NAP (name, address, phone) across all profiles\n- Claiming and optimizing your Google knowledge panel where available\n\nImplement basic schema on your homepage and core service pages, then align it with your Google Business Profile and major social/review sites. Validate your markup and keep it updated when your services evolve.\n\nSoft positioning: Think of structured data as the technical backbone of brand authority—it doesn’t replace proof and reviews, but it makes them easier for AI systems to connect to your entity.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Structured data is critical for helping AI recognize and connect your brand. Start with Organization schema on your site, add Service or Product schema to key pages, use consistent NAP, and align sameAs links with major profiles and your knowledge panel for clearer entity signals."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Structured data is critical for helping AI recognize and connect your brand. Start with Organization schema on your site, add Service or Product schema to key p"
      }
