        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What is a “brand authority map” for AI search and how do I build one for my company?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Your brand authority map is a **living blueprint** of what you want to be known for in AI search: category, ICP, core use cases, key competitors, proof points, and source‑of‑truth pages. It’s the anchor for all your authority work.\n\nWithout a map, content and PR decisions become reactive and scattered, which weakens your signals.\n\nKey factors:\n- Primary category and 1–2 secondary categories you’ll own\n- Ideal customer profile (role, industry, size, problem)\n- Top 20–30 buyer prompts you want to be cited for\n- The specific pages and external sources that should answer each prompt\n\nBuild the map collaboratively, then use it to prioritize which pages to strengthen, which proof to publish, and which mentions to pursue. Revisit it quarterly as your market and services evolve.\n\nSoft positioning: A well‑defined brand authority map turns AI search from a guessing game into a focused, trackable strategy.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "A brand authority map defines the category, ICP, core use cases, buyer prompts, competitors, proof points, and source‑of‑truth pages you want AI tools to associate with your brand. Document these, then use the map to guide which content, proof, and mentions you build and track."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "A brand authority map defines the category, ICP, core use cases, buyer prompts, competitors, proof points, and source‑of‑truth pages you want AI tools to associ"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 1840,
      "item": {
        "url": "aeoptimizer.com/faq/what-is-local-aeo-and-how-is-it-different-from-regular-local-seo",
        "name": "What is “local AEO” and how is it different from regular local SEO?",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "speakable": {
          "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
          "cssSelector": [
            "h1",
            ".faq-question",
            ".faq-answer",
            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What is “local AEO” and how is it different from regular local SEO?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Local AEO means optimizing your business so **AI search engines and answer tools** (like ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google’s AI overviews) recognize you as the best local answer for queries in your area. It’s an evolution of local SEO focused on entities, evidence, and answer-ready content.\n\nInstead of just chasing blue links, local AEO makes sure AI systems understand *who you are, where you are, and what you do*, then trust you enough to surface your answers. It’s especially important for service businesses in competitive cities.\n\n**Key factors** \n- Clear, consistent business entity data (name, address, phone, categories). \n- Strong local proof (reviews, photos, case stories, local partners). \n- Short, direct answers to common questions on your site and profiles. \n- Proper schema markup (LocalBusiness, Organization, FAQPage) and citations.\n\nPractically, you’ll audit your local profiles, tighten NAP consistency, add answer-focused FAQs to your main service and location pages, and build a few credible local mentions and reviews. Over time, you monitor which queries you get surfaced for and refine content.\n\nIf you care about being “the obvious local choice” when people ask AI for help, local AEO is now a core strategy, not a nice-to-have.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Local AEO is about making your business the **trusted local entity** AI search tools pick when people ask questions in your area. It goes beyond local SEO by focusing on entity clarity, local proof, and answer-ready content so you get cited in AI-driven results, not just traditional search listings."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Local AEO is about making your business the **trusted local entity** AI search tools pick when people ask questions in your area. It goes beyond local SEO by fo"
