            "name": "If I invest in local AEO now, how long before I see results in AI answers and local search?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "In most cases, expect **early signals in 4–8 weeks** and more meaningful gains in 3–6 months, assuming consistent work and a competitive market. AI systems and search engines need time to crawl, reconcile, and trust your new entity signals.\n\nTimeline varies by city and niche: Los Angeles or Austin may take longer than a small town because there are more competing entities and content.\n\n**Key factors** \n- How messy your current data and content are. \n- Competition level in your category and geography. \n- Frequency of updates (reviews, content, schema, local mentions). \n- How often AI search tools refresh and retrain on the web.\n\nPlan for a 6‑month horizon where you track citations in AI tools, changes in local rankings, and leads from “discovery” searches—not just branded searches. Avoid anyone promising “instant AEO wins” in a couple of weeks.\n\nTreat local AEO as an ongoing practice; gains tend to compound, not spike overnight.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Most local AEO efforts start showing **early movement in 4–8 weeks**, with more meaningful improvements in AI citations and local visibility over 3–6 months. The timeline depends on how clean your data is, how competitive your city is, and how consistently you update reviews and content."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Most local AEO efforts start showing **early movement in 4–8 weeks**, with more meaningful improvements in AI citations and local visibility over 3–6 months. Th"
      }
