            "name": "What does local AEO typically cost, and how do I know if it’s worth it for my budget?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Local AEO can be done **very lean** at first: your real “cost” is time plus whatever tools you choose. Agencies or software subscriptions typically range from a few hundred to a few thousand dollars monthly, depending on scope.\n\nThe main value is greater visibility in AI-driven results and more qualified local leads that are already primed to convert.\n\n**Key factors** \n- DIY vs. done‑for‑you: labor is your biggest cost. \n- Number of locations and services you need to optimize. \n- Depth of content, schema, and off-site work (citations, PR, partners). \n- The value of one additional high‑quality local customer to you.\n\nWith a limited budget, focus on high‑impact basics: clean NAP, optimized Google Business Profile, strong reviews, and a few answer-ready pages before buying advanced tools. Evaluate cost by comparing against even a small uplift in monthly customers.\n\nThink of local AEO as a revenue engine; if it doesn’t pencil out against realistic lead gains, adjust the scope rather than dropping the idea entirely.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Local AEO can start with mostly **time investment** and low-cost tools, while more advanced agency or software setups often run from a few hundred to a few thousand dollars a month. It’s “worth it” if the expected lift in qualified local leads covers that cost with margin."
