              "text": "If you tried an SEO agency before and saw little impact, approach local AEO with **tighter scoping and clearer metrics**. Focus less on generic keyword rankings and more on AI citations, local profile engagement, and qualified leads.\n\nYou may also want more transparency: see exactly which questions you’re being surfaced for and how entity data is being managed.\n\n**Key factors** \n- Set concrete goals: questions you want to own, neighborhoods you care about. \n- Demand reporting on citations, not just positions. \n- Avoid vague “traffic” promises; prioritize contact and conversion data. \n- Ensure you keep ownership of accounts, logins, and content.\n\nStart with a pilot on one service and one city rather than a sprawling, multi‑location rollout. Validate that you can gain real visibility for specific queries in AI tools before scaling.\n\nGood local AEO feels like a partnership; if a provider can’t show you how their work translates into answer placements and leads, keep looking.",
