            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If you’re in Los Angeles or San Diego, prioritize **location proof and neighborhood nuance**. With so many businesses, AI tools need clear signals that you genuinely operate in specific areas, not just claim them.\n\nGeneric city pages rarely cut it; you need tangible local evidence and content tailored to the way residents talk about their neighborhoods and needs.\n\n**Key factors** \n- Real local photos, case stories, and testimonials tied to LA/SD neighborhoods. \n- Local partner mentions (chamber, community orgs, events, collaborations). \n- Service pages that explain how offerings differ by neighborhood or city. \n- FAQs that reference local constraints (traffic, regulations, climate, culture).\n\nCreate or update one strong page per primary area you serve, then seed it with a “Quick answers” section geared to that city (e.g., parking, scheduling, seasonal demand). Monitor how AI tools respond when you ask about services specifically “in [neighborhood].”\n\nIn crowded coastal markets, depth of local proof is often the deciding factor for AEO.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "In Los Angeles and San Diego, focus local AEO on **strong location proof and neighborhood-specific content**: real local photos and stories, partner mentions, and FAQs that address city-specific questions. Generic city pages aren’t enough; AI tools favor tangible, localized evidence."
            }
