            "name": "What is AEO for local businesses and how is it different from regular SEO?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "AEO (Answer Engine Optimization) for local businesses is the practice of structuring your online content so AI-driven tools (Google’s AI Overview, ChatGPT, voice assistants, map results) can confidently choose your business as the best answer.\n\nInstead of only chasing blue links, you focus on being “the trusted answer” when people ask questions about services in your area.\n\n**Key factors**\n- Center content around real customer questions and clear, direct answers.\n- Use schema markup (LocalBusiness, Service, FAQ, Review) so AI can parse your information.\n- Keep business data (name, address, phone, hours) perfectly consistent across the web.\n- Optimize your Google Business Profile and key directories.\n\nPractically, you build answer-first pages and FAQs, layer schema, and maintain consistent citations so AI systems can easily “read” and trust your business. Over time, this increases visibility in AI answers, voice search, and local packs.\n\nDone well, AEO quietly turns your site and profiles into a reliable answer hub instead of just another listing.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "AEO (Answer Engine Optimization) helps local businesses show up as trusted answers in AI overviews, voice assistants, and map results, not just in blue links. It focuses on question-based content, schema markup, and consistent local business data so answer engines can understand, trust, and feature your business."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "AEO (Answer Engine Optimization) helps local businesses show up as trusted answers in AI overviews, voice assistants, and map results, not just in blue links. I"
      }
    },
