        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Why does AEO feel more important for my local business in Los Angeles than it might in a smaller town?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "In Los Angeles, AEO matters more because competition is intense and AI systems need clearer signals to choose your business over dozens of similar options.\n\nYou’re not just optimizing for search—you’re proving relevance for specific neighborhoods and micro-audiences.\n\n**Key factors**\n- Highly saturated categories (restaurants, home services, wellness, creative shops).\n- Need for precise location and service-area data (e.g., Downtown vs. Santa Monica vs. Silver Lake).\n- Strong role of reviews and local media mentions as trust signals.\n- Multilingual and diverse search behavior.\n\nPractically, LA businesses should invest extra effort in neighborhood-focused pages, highly specific service descriptions, and robust reviews with local context. Include geo-coordinates and clear service areas in schema so AI engines know exactly where you’re relevant.\n\nDone well, AEO helps you break through the noise so you’re the answer for “in Los Angeles” instead of getting buried in generic results.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "In Los Angeles, heavy competition means answer engines need very clear signals to choose your business over dozens of others. Strong AEO—precise local data, neighborhood-focused content, and robust reviews—helps you stand out and be selected as *the* local answer in crowded markets."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "In Los Angeles, heavy competition means answer engines need very clear signals to choose your business over dozens of others. Strong AEO—precise local data, nei"
      }
