            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "If your Google Business Profile keeps getting suspended or flagged, fix that before pushing hard on AEO, because answer engines treat a stable GBP as a core trust signal for local businesses.\n\nUnstable profiles can undermine your entire visibility.\n\n**Key factors**\n- Make sure your business name, category, and address match reality and your website.\n- Avoid keyword-stuffed names or virtual addresses that violate guidelines.\n- Keep ownership and verification details clean and up to date.\n- Document changes carefully when you update info.\n\nOnce your profile is stable and compliant, rebuild AEO around it: consistent NAP, schema that matches your GBP, and clean citations.\n\nThink of GBP stability as a prerequisite—if that foundation is shaky, answer engines will hesitate to feature you, no matter how good your content is.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Pause aggressive AEO and fix your Google Business Profile first—ensure your name, address, category, and website are accurate and guideline-compliant. Once your GBP is stable and verified, align your schema and citations to it so answer engines can trust and feature your business."
