        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How do I actually optimize my site for voice search and AEO, step by step?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You start by identifying the exact spoken questions your customers ask, then rewriting key pages with question-based headings and short, direct answers in natural language. Next, you add structured data (FAQPage, HowTo, LocalBusiness, Speakable schema) so voice assistants can reliably extract and read your answers.\n\nVoice search AEO is about becoming the \"go-to answer\" for AI assistants like Siri, Google Assistant, and Alexa when someone asks a question aloud. Instead of just chasing blue links, you design content specifically for conversational queries and featured snippets.\n\nKey factors:\n- Map real voice queries from Search Console, “People Also Ask,” and tools like AnswerThePublic\n- Use question-form H2/H3 headings with 30–60 word direct answers right below\n- Implement FAQPage / HowTo / LocalBusiness / Speakable schema on key pages\n- Ensure fast, mobile-first pages with clear local info and reviews\n\nPractically, pick 20–30 core questions, build Q&A sections around them, and mark them up with schema so AI systems can trust and reuse your answers. Review monthly which queries trigger voice results and refine content.\n\nIf you’re overwhelmed, a specialized AEO/voice search partner can shortcut the research and implementation work while you focus on your product and customers.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Start by mapping the real spoken questions your customers ask, then turn each into a question-based heading with a short, direct, conversational answer. Add FAQPage/HowTo/LocalBusiness/Speakable schema, improve mobile speed, and regularly test voice queries to see if assistants read your content back."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Start by mapping the real spoken questions your customers ask, then turn each into a question-based heading with a short, direct, conversational answer. Add FAQ"
      }
    },
