      "item": {
        "url": "aeoptimizer.com/faq/what-s-the-difference-between-seo-and-aeo-for-voice-search-and-do-i-really-need",
        "name": "What’s the difference between SEO and AEO for voice search, and do I really need both?",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "speakable": {
          "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
          "cssSelector": [
            "h1",
            ".faq-question",
            ".faq-answer",
            "[itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\"]"
          ]
        },
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "What’s the difference between SEO and AEO for voice search, and do I really need both?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "AEO (Answer Engine Optimization) is optimizing your content so AI assistants and voice search tools can confidently choose your answer, not just your link. It’s different from traditional SEO because it focuses on conversational questions, structured data, and position-zero answers.\n\nWhere SEO mainly targets ranking pages in search results, AEO targets the actual answers that Siri, Google Assistant, Alexa, and AI chatbots speak or display. You’re optimizing for *what gets read aloud* and shown in answer boxes.\n\nKey factors:\n- Emphasis on natural language, Q&A formats, and question-based headings\n- Heavy use of FAQPage, HowTo, LocalBusiness, and Speakable schema\n- Focus on featured snippets, zero-click results, and AI assistant outputs\n- Measurement via voice queries, snippet share, and AI discovery, not just clicks\n\nPractically, you keep your SEO foundations but layer AEO on top: rework content into Q&A blocks, add schema, and monitor voice and AI discovery metrics. Over time, you become the “canonical answer” for your niche questions.\n\nFor most businesses, the winning strategy is SEO + AEO together, not one instead of the other.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "SEO focuses on ranking pages in search results, while AEO focuses on getting your answers chosen and spoken by voice assistants and AI tools. You usually need both: SEO for visibility, AEO for owning featured snippets, zero-click answers, and voice search responses."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "SEO focuses on ranking pages in search results, while AEO focuses on getting your answers chosen and spoken by voice assistants and AI tools. You usually need b"
      }
    },
