        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "How long does voice search and AEO optimization take before I see real results?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You’ll usually see first meaningful results from voice search and AEO within 4–12 weeks, depending on how much content and schema you implement and how often search engines recrawl your site. Featured snippet and voice placements tend to stabilize over 3–6 months.\n\nSearch engines and AI assistants need time to discover, parse, and test your new Q&A content and structured data. The more authority your domain already has, the faster you’ll see shifts.\n\nKey factors:\n- Crawl and index frequency for your site\n- Quality, quantity, and topical consistency of Q&A content\n- Proper, error-free schema implementation and validation\n- Existing domain authority and review signals\n\nIn practice, plan for a 90-day sprint: implement AEO changes in month 1, validate and refine in month 2, and watch voice/snippet metrics in month 3. Expect continued gains as you expand your question set.\n\nIf timing is critical, working with an AEO specialist can help prioritize high-impact queries and avoid schema mistakes that slow results.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "Most sites see first meaningful voice/AEO improvements within 4–12 weeks, with featured snippets and voice placements stabilizing over 3–6 months. Results depend on crawl frequency, content quality, schema accuracy, and your existing authority."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "Most sites see first meaningful voice/AEO improvements within 4–12 weeks, with featured snippets and voice placements stabilizing over 3–6 months. Results depen"
      }
