              "text": "For local businesses in Los Angeles and San Diego, voice search and AEO matter because so many “near me” queries and on-the-go searches are now spoken into phones and car dashboards. If you’re not optimized, assistants will route customers to better-structured competitors.\n\nDense, competitive metros amplify the impact: small differences in local schema, reviews, and Q&A content can decide who gets recommended.\n\nKey factors:\n- Accurate LocalBusiness schema with NAP, hours, and services\n- Fully optimized Google Business Profile with reviews and photos\n- Locally focused Q&A content (neighborhoods, traffic, parking, timing)\n- Mobile speed and map integration for quick directions\n\nPractically, audit how Siri/Google respond to “near me” and city-specific queries for your category in LA and San Diego, then close gaps in schema and profiles. Aim to become the obvious spoken recommendation.\n\nIf your local footprint is critical, professional AEO support can help you stand out in crowded West Coast markets.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "In cities like Los Angeles and San Diego, many “near me” and on-the-go searches are voice-based. If your local profiles, schema, and Q&A content aren’t optimized, Siri and Google will route customers to competitors with better-structured, better-reviewed information."
            }
