              "text": "You don’t have to be technical, but you should understand the basics: Q&A content structure, schema concepts, and how to validate markup. Many tools and plugins can handle the technical pieces once you’ve written good, conversational answers.\n\nYour main job is knowing your customers’ questions and answering them clearly.\n\nKey factors:\n- Comfort with editing content and headings in your CMS\n- Ability to use schema plugins or generators with copy‑paste JSON-LD\n- Willingness to run rich result and schema validation tests\n- Process for keeping answers and business data up to date\n\nPractically, start with content: write question-form headings and 30–60 word answers, then work with a plugin or developer to add FAQPage/HowTo/LocalBusiness schema. Test and iterate.\n\nIf you prefer to stay non-technical, partnering with an AEO-focused team can let you focus purely on subject matter expertise.",
