            "name": "How can I improve my local voice search visibility if I’m on a tight budget and can’t hire a big SEO agency?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "With a limited budget, focus on the essentials: clean up your Google Business Profile and major listings, write strong FAQ content in natural language, and ensure your site loads quickly on mobile. These are low‑cost, high‑impact moves for voice search.\n\nYou don’t need custom Alexa skills or advanced schema right away; get the basics solid so assistants can trust and surface your information. Most of this can be done in‑house with some guidance.\n\nKey factors:\n- Prioritize free platforms: Google Business Profile, Apple Maps, Yelp, Bing Places\n- Use simple tools (PageSpeed Insights, Search Console) for diagnostics\n- Write conversational FAQs using real customer questions\n- Add reviews and keep NAP details consistent everywhere\n\nAllocate a small monthly budget to ongoing improvements: adding FAQs, requesting reviews, and updating hours or services. Avoid expensive one‑time “voice SEO packages” that don’t explain what they’re changing.\n\nIf you later decide to invest more, a professional can layer in schema markup and deeper content, but the low‑budget basics you set now will still pay off.",
              "@type": "Answer",
              "description": "On a tight budget, get the basics right: fully optimize your Google Business Profile, keep your name/address/phone identical on all listings, write conversational FAQs with direct answers, and ensure your site is fast and mobile‑friendly. These low‑cost steps significantly improve local voice visibility."
            }
          }
        ],
        "description": "On a tight budget, get the basics right: fully optimize your Google Business Profile, keep your name/address/phone identical on all listings, write conversation"
      }
