            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "You can usually start seeing early improvements in voice‑driven visibility and calls within 4–8 weeks once you fix listings, add FAQs, and improve site speed, but more competitive markets may take several months. Voice search relies on the same index and trust signals as regular SEO.\n\nSearch engines need time to crawl your changes, test them, and adjust rankings. Reviews and engagement also accumulate gradually, strengthening your presence.\n\nKey factors:\n- Crawl and index frequency for your site\n- Competitiveness of your category and city\n- Volume and quality of fresh reviews\n- Consistency of NAP and ongoing updates\n\nTrack progress using Google Search Console queries and changes in impressions for question‑style and “near me” terms. Watch for more calls and direction requests from your Google profile.\n\nIf you don’t see any change after 3–4 months, revisit your basics—many stalls come from inconsistent data or thin FAQ content.",
