            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For a Salt Lake City business, voice optimization should reflect local geography, commuting patterns, and cultural touchpoints—queries like “coffee near Temple Square,” “family restaurant in Sugar House,” or “bike shop near University of Utah.” Mention these areas naturally in content and profiles.\n\nAssistants use proximity and relevance; if your presence doesn’t clearly tie to those landmarks or neighborhoods, you may be invisible to local voice queries that reference them.\n\nKey factors:\n- Neighborhoods and districts (Sugar House, Downtown, Avenues, Millcreek)\n- Key landmarks and institutions (Temple Square, U of U)\n- Clear directions and parking FAQs\n- Consistent, detailed service areas in listings\n\nAdd localized FAQs such as “How close are you to Temple Square?” or “Is there parking at your Sugar House location?” and mirror that language in your profiles.\n\nIf you serve multiple nearby suburbs, define each in your content so assistants can distinguish which location is closest to the user.",
